E["item:bingles-blastencapper"] = {t="item",n="Bingles' Blastencapper",z="lochmodan",s="Troggs hold Bingles' Blastencapper after his gyrocopter fell into the Loch. Without it, Bingles' plans to aid Gnomeregan's liberation are in danger.",h="Troggs hold Bingles' Blastencapper after his gyrocopter fell into the Loch.",sec={{t="A Volatile Invention",b="Bingles Blastenheimer built the Blastencapper to strike from the air at the troggs and leper gnomes who overran Gnomeregan. Mechanical failure sent his gyrocopter into the Loch, but Bingles survived. Troggs from the northern islands raided the wreckage and carried the volatile weapon to their camps.",sp=0},{t="Air Support for Gnomeregan",b="Bingles needs the Blastencapper to help retake Gnomeregan. The exiled gnomes are preparing to reclaim their radioactive home, and he counts on his gyrocopter and signature munitions for the air assault. In trogg hands, the explosive could accidentally cause a catastrophe in Loch Modan. Recovering it would preserve a valuable weapon for the gnomish resistance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Bingles' Blastencapper?",a="Bingles Blastenheimer made the Blastencapper to strike from the air at the troggs and leper gnomes occupying Gnomeregan.",al={"what is blastencapper","blastencapper","bingles explosive"},it="identity"},{q="How did the Blastencapper end up in the Loch?",a="Bingles crashed his gyrocopter into the Loch. Troggs from nearby islands raided the wreckage and carried off his tools, including the explosive.",al={"why is it in the loch","how did bingles lose it","crash"},it="origin"},{q="Who currently has the Blastencapper?",a="Troggs from the Loch’s northern islands took the Blastencapper from the wreckage and guard it in their camp.",al={"who stole the blastencapper","who has it","troggs"},it="target"},{q="Why does Bingles need the Blastencapper returned?",a="Bingles needs the Blastencapper and his tools to repair his gyrocopter and launch an aerial assault in support of Gnomeregan’s reclamation.",al={"why need it back","why is blastencapper important","for gnomeregan"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Every tool and munition matters as the gnomes struggle to reclaim Gnomeregan. Recovering Bingles’ explosive could let gnomish aerial ingenuity strike back at the trogg invaders.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Blastencapper shows gnomish engineering flair: complex and explosive, it can devastate from high above."},kw={"bingles","blastencapper","blastenheimer","explosives","gnomeregan","gyrocopter","loch modan","trogg"},rel={"quest:2038","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:gnomeregan","item:bingles-wrench","item:bingles-hammer","item:bingles-screwdriver","topic:trogg"},src={"Bingles' Blastencapper","Bingles' Missing Supplies"}}
E["item:bingles-hammer"] = {t="item",n="Bingles' Hammer",z="lochmodan",s="At his crash site in Loch Modan, Bingles Blastenheimer needs Bingles' Hammer back from the troggs. With his gear restored, he can repair his flying machine and help free Gnomeregan.",h="At his crash site in Loch Modan, Bingles Blastenheimer needs Bingles' Hammer back from the troggs.",sec={{t="A Stranded Aviator's Toolkit",b="Troggs raided Bingles Blastenheimer's crash site on the freshwater islands. They took his hammer and high-potency explosives. The hammer is needed to repair the dented airframe and adjust the gyrocopter's mechanical parts. Without his equipment, Bingles cannot fly support runs for the gnome forces fighting to reclaim Gnomeregan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Bingles' Hammer be found?",a="Bingles' Hammer lies inside one of Bingles's Toolbuckets scattered across the trogg-infested islands in the northern Loch.",al={"hammer location","where is bingles hammer","how to find hammer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who does this hammer belong to?",a="The hammer belongs to Bingles Blastenheimer, a gnome engineer and pilot. His flying machine crashed along the shores of Loch Modan.",al={"who owns the hammer","bingles hammer owner"},it="identity"},{q="Why is this tool so important to Bingles?",a="Bingles needs his full set of tools to rebuild his downed gyrocopter. He plans to fly it against the troggs and leper gnomes occupying Gnomeregan.",al={"why need hammer","bingles hammer use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who stole Bingles' Hammer?",a="Troggs living on the lake islands raided the crash site. They took Bingles' toolbuckets and custom blastencapper explosives.",al={"who took the hammer","trogg thieves"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, each tool you recover brings the airborne assault to free your ancestral home closer.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know a fine gnome-crafted hammer is hard to replace. Bingles needs one to rebuild his experimental gyrocopter in the wilderness."},kw={"bingles","blastenheimer","gnomeregan","hammer","loch modan","toolbucket","trogg"},rel={"npc:bingles-blastenheimer","quest:2038","item:bingles-blastencapper","item:bingles-screwdriver","item:bingles-wrench","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:gnomeregan"},src={"Bingles' Hammer","Bingles' Missing Supplies"}}
E["item:bingles-screwdriver"] = {t="item",n="Bingles' Screwdriver",z="lochmodan",s="Across Loch Modan's northern islands, Bingles' Screwdriver lies among the gear lost in a crash. Troggs carried it off with the tools of pilot Bingles Blastenheimer.",h="Across Loch Modan's northern islands, Bingles' Screwdriver lies among the gear lost in a crash.",sec={{t="A Pilot's Vital Kit",b="When Bingles Blastenheimer crashed into Loch Modan, he lost the tools needed to repair his gyrocopter. Troggs on nearby islands carried off his tool buckets, and the screwdriver was packed in one of them. Bingles needs it for fine adjustments as he repairs the craft and handles its armaments.",sp=0},{t="Preparations for the Retaking",b="Bingles works to free Gnomeregan from troggs and leper gnomes. He means to join his flying skill with volatile Blastencapper munitions in an aerial assault. The screwdriver, wrench, and hammer will help him rebuild his gyrocopter and keep the airborne counteroffensive alive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bingles' Screwdriver found?",a="After Bingles crashed, troggs scattered his Toolbuckets across the islands in northern Loch Modan. The screwdriver is inside one of them.",al={"screwdriver location","find bingles screwdriver","where is the screwdriver"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the screwdriver so important to Bingles?",a="Bingles needs the screwdriver and his other tools to rebuild his gyrocopter and prepare explosives for the campaign to retake Gnomeregan.",al={"why does bingles need it","what is it for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who stole the screwdriver in the first place?",a="After Bingles crash landed, troggs living on the islands in Loch Modan took his tool buckets and Blastencapper explosives.",al={"who took the tools","who stole bingles tools"},it="threat"},{q="What other tools did Bingles lose in the crash?",a="Along with the screwdriver, Bingles lost his wrench, hammer, and volatile supply of Blastenheimer Blastencapper explosives.",al={"other bingles tools","what else is missing"},it="item"},{q="What is Bingles' Screwdriver?",a="Bingles' Screwdriver is an engineering tool belonging to Bingles Blastenheimer, a gnome aviator stranded in Loch Modan. Along with his wrench and hammer, it is one of the essential implements he carried aboard his gyrocopter to maintain his flying machine and construct ordnance for the gnomish resistance.",al={"what is bingles screwdriver","bingles screwdriver info","about bingles screwdriver"},it="identity",add="f72526b7"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, each tool you recover brings Bingles closer to rebuilding his craft and fighting the troggs and leper gnomes who drove your kin from Gnomeregan.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know a precisely made screwdriver is vital for intricate gyrocopter rotors and delicate trigger assemblies."},kw={"bingles","blastenheimer","gyrocopter","loch modan","screwdriver","toolbucket","troggs"},rel={"quest:2038","item:bingles-wrench","item:bingles-hammer","item:bingles-blastencapper","quest:2039","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:gnomeregan"},src={"Bingles' Screwdriver","Bingles' Missing Supplies"}}
E["item:bingles-wrench"] = {t="item",n="Bingles' Wrench",z="lochmodan",s="In the Loch, Bingles' Wrench is missing with the pilot's other tools. Troggs took it after Bingles Blastenheimer crash-landed his flying machine.",h="In the Loch, Bingles' Wrench is missing with the pilot's other tools.",sec={{t="Salvage on the Islands",b="Bingles Blastenheimer survived when his gyrocopter crashed into the Loch. Then the troggs raided the crash site on the small northern islands. They took his specialized supplies and scattered his tools among buckets in their camps.\n\nBingles' Wrench is one of three critical hand tools, alongside his high-yield Blastencapper explosives. Without the wrench, Bingles cannot repair his downed gyrocopter. His planned aerial offensive to aid the exiled gnomes fighting to reclaim Gnomeregan must wait.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who does this wrench belong to?",a="The wrench belongs to Bingles Blastenheimer, an eccentric gnome pilot whose gyrocopter crashed into the Loch.",al={"who is bingles","bingles owner","wrench owner"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the wrench so important to Bingles?",a="Bingles needs his specialized tools to repair his damaged flying machine and arm his explosive payload for an aerial assault against the troggs and leper gnomes occupying Gnomeregan.",al={"why does bingles need his wrench","wrench purpose","what is wrench for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where did the wrench end up after the crash?",a="Local troggs scavenged the wrench and stashed it in one of Bingles' stolen toolbuckets among their camps on the northern islands of the Loch.",al={"where is bingles wrench","wrench location","find bingles wrench"},it="place"},{q="What else was stolen along with the wrench?",a="The troggs also took Bingles' Screwdriver, Bingles' Hammer, and his experimental Blastenheimer Blastencapper explosives.",al={"other supplies","missing tools","what else did troggs take"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, every recovered tool brings the resistance closer to taking the fight back to Gnomeregan's irradiated halls.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know a craftsman without a custom wrench is grounded, especially with troggs scavenging nearby."},kw={"bingles","blastenheimer","gyrocopter","loch modan","toolbucket","troggs","wrench"},rel={"quest:2038","item:bingles-screwdriver","item:bingles-hammer","item:bingles-blastencapper","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:gnomeregan","topic:trogg"},src={"Bingles' Wrench","Bingles' Missing Supplies"}}
E["item:brock-s-list"] = {t="item",n="Brock's List",z="lochmodan",s="At Thelsamar, Brock Stoneseeker sends a list of mining pupils honored with picks from Ironforge's guild halls.",h="At Thelsamar, Brock Stoneseeker sends a list of mining pupils honored with picks from Ironforge's guild halls.",sec={{t="A Miner's Distinction",b="In Khaz Modan, apprentices must prove their skill before taking on serious work in the mines. Brock records those who excel in their lessons. He entrusts the list to travelers bound for Ironforge, where the honored names can be engraved on the picks.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Great Forge",b="A gryphon carries Brock's List from Thelsamar's roost to Golnir Bouldertoe at the Deep Mountain Mining Guild in Ironforge's Great Forge. There, the students' names are engraved on their honorary picks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Brock's List?",a="Brock Stoneseeker, Thelsamar's mining instructor, writes a roster of apprentices who excel in their mining lessons and earn honorary picks.",al={"brocks list","what is this item","brock list purpose"},it="identity"},{q="Who do I deliver Brock's List to?",a="Show Brock's List to Thorgrum Borrelson, the gryphon master in Thelsamar, to arrange passage. Then carry it to Golnir Bouldertoe at the Deep Mountain Mining Guild in Ironforge's Great Forge.",al={"where do i take the list","who gets brocks list","brocks list turn in"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Golnir Bouldertoe need this document?",a="Golnir Bouldertoe oversees the Deep Mountain Mining Guild's tools in Ironforge. He has honorary picks ready and needs Brock's roster to engrave each student's name on one.",al={"why golnir","why does ironforge need the list"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the list sent by gryphon rather than foot?",a="The mountain passes through Loch Modan connect to Dun Morogh. A gryphon from Thorgrum Borrelson's roost carries the list swiftly and safely to the Great Forge.",al={"why fly to ironforge","why take a gryphon"}},{q="Where does Brock's List come from, and who made it?",a="The list is written by Brock Stoneseeker, a veteran miner based in the town of Thelsamar within Loch Modan. As young dwarves pass through his doors to learn the craft, Brock evaluates their progress and drafts this roster to record the exceptional students who have earned special recognition for their hard work.",al={"who made brocks list","where did brocks list come from","brocks list creator"},it="origin",add="bca439a3"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a prospector, you can see that Brock's List honors apprentices who have earned a place in the Deep Mountain Mining Guild's traditions.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the list honors young miners devoted to the pick and shovel beneath Khaz Modan."},kw={"brock's list","golnir bouldertoe","great forge","ironforge","loch modan","mining","thelsamar","thorgrum borrelson"},rel={"quest:6387","quest:6391","npc:golnir-bouldertoe","npc:thorgrum-borrelson","item:honorary-picks","subzone:thelsamar","subzone:great-forge","zone:ironforge"},src={"Brock's List","Honor Students (Classic)","Ride to Ironforge (Classic)"}}
E["item:chok-sul-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Chok'sul's Head",z="lochmodan",s="In Thelsamar, Chok'sul's death is proved by the head Magistrate Bluntnose demands. The local dwarven authorities set a bounty, and he requires this proof before paying it.",h="In Thelsamar, Chok'sul's death is proved by the head Magistrate Bluntnose demands.",sec={{t="Proof of the Chieftain's Fall",b="Ogres from Mo'grosh Stronghold threaten Loch Modan's settlements. They strike Thelsamar, excavation sites, and the Stonewrought Dam. Magistrate Bluntnose placed a bounty on Chok'sul, the brute believed to direct these attacks.\n\nThe northeastern hills are in turmoil, so the magistrate demands proof before releasing township funds. Chok'sul's severed head gives the dwarven council the certainty it needs to mark the bounty fulfilled.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Chok'sul?",a="Chok'sul was an ogre chieftain at Mo'grosh Stronghold in northeastern Loch Modan. Dwarven officials believe he directed raids on Thelsamar, the Stonewrought Dam, and nearby excavation sites.",al={"who is choksul","choksul lore","chok'sul identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Magistrate Bluntnose want the head?",a="Magistrate Bluntnose set a public bounty for Chok'sul's death by any means. Ogre raids have strained the region, so he requires clear proof of the chieftain's death before paying from Thelsamar's coffers.",al={"why bluntnose wants head","choksul head purpose","who wants choksuls head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where did Chok'sul operate?",a="Chok'sul led his warband from Mo'grosh Stronghold in the craggy hills of northeastern Loch Modan.",al={"where is choksul","mo'grosh stronghold location","choksul location"},it="place"},{q="What threats did Chok'sul pose to the region?",a="Chok'sul was believed to direct attacks on Thelsamar and nearby dwarven works, including the Stonewrought Dam and local excavation sites.",al={"why is choksul wanted","what did choksul do"},it="threat"},{q="Where does Chok'sul's Head come from?",a="This grim trophy is taken directly from the ogre Chok'sul within Mo'grosh Stronghold, located in the northeastern wilderness of Loch Modan. It is not an artifact or crafted item, but the severed head of the ogre warlord himself, claimed by adventurers seeking to fulfill the official bounty posted by the town of Thelsamar.",al={"origin of choksul head","where did choksul head come from","who made choksuls head"},it="origin",add="8aed7d95"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, defeating Chok'sul eases the danger to Ironforge's rural settlements and protects the Stonewrought Dam from destruction."},kw={"chok'sul","chok'sul's head","loch modan","magistrate bluntnose","mo'grosh","ogre","stonewrought dam","thelsamar"},rel={"quest:256","subzone:thelsamar","subzone:mo-grosh-stronghold","zone:lochmodan","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:ironforge"},src={"Chok'sul's Head","WANTED: Chok'sul"}}
E["item:crocolisk-tear-classic"] = {t="item",n="Crocolisk Tear (Classic)",z="lochmodan",s="At the Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir needs Crocolisk Tear to counter Dark Iron explosives.",h="At the Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir needs Crocolisk Tear to counter Dark Iron explosives.",sec={{t="A Curious Component",b="Crocolisk Tears come from reptiles in Loch Modan's waters. Chief Engineer Hinderweir found another use for their secretions. Mixed with potent spider venom and resonant ogre minerals, a tear gains the chemical properties needed to counter the volatile Dark Iron demolition charges threatening the Stonewrought Dam.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Crocolisk Tear used for?",a="At the Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir needs a Crocolisk Tear for a mixture meant to disarm explosives planted by Dark Iron saboteurs.",al={"crocolisk tear purpose","why do i need crocolisk tear","who wants crocolisk tears"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Crocolisk Tears be gathered?",a="Loch Crocolisks and Large Loch Crocolisks live in Loch Modan's waters and shallows. Their tears can be gathered there.",al={"where do crocolisk tears drop","crocolisk tear location","how to get crocolisk tears"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What other materials are combined with the tear?",a="Hinderweir combines the tear with Lurker Venom from local forest spiders and a Mo'grosh Crystal from ogres in the northeastern hills. Together, they make the defusing agent.",al={"hinderweir ingredients","disarming materials","what else is needed with crocolisk tear"}},{q="What is a Crocolisk Tear?",a="A Crocolisk Tear is a rare alchemical reagent harvested directly from the crocolisks that inhabit the waters of Loch Modan. Despite the old saying about insincere weeping, these physical secretions possess unusual properties that make them useful in specialized mixtures, particularly when compounded with other potent local reagents to neutralize volatile explosives.",al={"crocolisk tear","what is crocolisk tear","crocolisk tear item"},it="identity",add="27a8e6d1"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Dwarven engineers such as Chief Engineer Hinderweir use unusual alchemical compounds to neutralize advanced explosives when ordinary tools are not enough."},kw={"crocolisk tear","dark iron","hinderweir","loch modan","reagent","stonewrought dam","the loch"},rel={"quest:161","subzone:the-loch","zone:lochmodan","item:lurker-venom","item:mo-grosh-crystal"},src={"Crocolisk Tear (Classic)","A Dark Threat Looms (5)"}}
E["item:disarming-mixture"] = {t="item",n="Disarming Mixture",z="lochmodan",s="At Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir prepares Disarming Mixture to stop a Seaforium charge planted by Dark Iron saboteurs.",h="At Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir prepares Disarming Mixture to stop a Seaforium charge planted...",sec={{t="A Chemical Neutralizer",b="The heavy Seaforium charge lies beneath the dam’s foundation, and no Mountaineers are close enough to help. Hinderweir turns to ingredients named by explosives expert Ashlan Stonesmirk. He stirs them into a chemical neutralizer, then mixes it with the powder keg underwater. The reactive compounds are neutralized, and the charge is left harmless.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Disarming Mixture used for?",a="The mixture neutralizes a large Seaforium explosive keg planted underwater at Stonewrought Dam’s foundation by Dark Iron insurgents.",al={"what does disarming mixture do","use of disarming mixture","disarming mixture purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who creates the Disarming Mixture?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir blends the ingredients while overseeing maintenance and defense at Stonewrought Dam.",al={"who makes disarming mixture","who gives disarming mixture","hinderweir mixture"},it="origin"},{q="Why was the mixture necessary instead of simply disarming the bomb?",a="Dry Seaforium powder is harmless, but wet powder can explode with tremendous force. The mixture neutralizes the reactive powder while the keg remains submerged beneath the dam.",al={"why not disarm normally","why use chemicals on the bomb","why disarming mixture"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Disarming Mixture?",a="The Disarming Mixture is a specialized chemical concoction prepared specifically to neutralize volatile explosive compounds. When mixed into seaforium or high-grade blasting powder, it reacts with the explosive materials and chemically deactivates them, rendering the charges inert with a harmless fizzle instead of a catastrophic detonation.",al={"what is disarming mixture","disarming mixture item","about disarming mixture"},it="identity",add="8d78f743"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For an engineer, the Disarming Mixture shows how chemical neutralization can render a volatile Seaforium charge harmless without setting it off.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you help protect the valleys and lowlands around Stonewrought Dam. Applying the neutralizer quickly helps defend them."},kw={"dark iron","disarming mixture","explosives","hinderweir","loch modan","powder keg","seaforium","stonewrought dam"},rel={"quest:161","zone:lochmodan"},src={"Disarming Mixture","A Dark Threat Looms (6)"}}
E["item:ironband-s-progress-report"] = {t="item",n="Ironband's Progress Report",z="lochmodan",s="In eastern Loch Modan, troggs have brought Prospector Ironband's excavation to a halt. His report asks for more blastpowder, though the Explorers' League sent supplies weeks ago.",h="In eastern Loch Modan, troggs have brought Prospector Ironband's excavation to a halt.",sec={{t="A Plea for Gunpowder",b="Jern Hornhelm receives the dispatch in Thelsamar and forwards it to the Explorers' League in Ironforge. Ironband reports that work has stalled and asks for heavy munitions. The League leaders are baffled. They sent him plenty of blastpowder weeks ago, and now wonder where it went.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ironband's Progress Report?",a="Prospector Ironband's report describes troggs disrupting his excavation in Loch Modan and asks for more blastpowder.",al={"progress report","ironbands report","what is this report"},it="identity"},{q="Who receives this report?",a="Jern Hornhelm receives the report in Thelsamar, then sends it to Prospector Stormpike at the Explorers' League headquarters in Ironforge.",al={"who gets the report","who do i give the report to","deliver progress report"},it="target"},{q="Why does Ironband need more blastpowder?",a="Ironband says he needs blastpowder for his digging, though nearby trogg raids may also make explosives useful for defense. Hornhelm and Stormpike believe they sent him plenty weeks ago.",al={"why blastpowder","what happened to the powder","powder shortage"},it="purpose"},{q="How does Prospector Stormpike react to the report?",a="Prospector Stormpike is furious that work has advanced so slowly. He is baffled that Ironband does not mention the large shipment sent earlier, and wonders where the missing blastpowder went.",al={"stormpike reaction","is stormpike mad"}},{q="Where does Ironband's Progress Report come from, and who made it?",a="The document is drafted by Prospector Ironband himself at his excavation site in eastern Loch Modan. Overseeing the arduous digging efforts amidst persistent trogg harassment, Ironband penned the report to provide formal updates on his operation's sluggish momentum and officially log his ongoing material requisitions.",al={"who wrote ironbands progress report","who made ironband's report","where does ironbands report come from"},it="origin",add="9e6c80e6"},{q="Why does anyone want Ironband's Progress Report?",a="The report is vital documentation required by administrative contacts in Thelsamar and the Explorers' League headquarters in Ironforge. Without this official account detailing the site's difficulties and trogg interference, superiors like Prospector Stormpike will not grant bureaucratic approval to release and dispatch fresh shipments of blastpowder.",al={"why is ironbands progress report needed","why take ironbands report","purpose of ironband's progress report"},it="why_wanted",add="2cf6b481"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf who explores or mines, you know the dangers of excavating ancient titan sites in Khaz Modan.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know blastpowder can clear stubborn rock. You also know how dangerous it is when supplies go missing in trogg territory."},kw={"blastpowder","explorers league","ironband","jern hornhelm","loch modan","prospector stormpike","thelsamar","troggs"},rel={"quest:298","quest:301","npc:jern-hornhelm","npc:prospector-stormpike","topic:explorers-league","subzone:thelsamar","zone:ironforge","zone:lochmodan"},src={"Ironband's Progress Report","Excavation Progress Report","Report to Ironforge"}}
E["item:jordan-s-ore-shipment"] = {t="item",n="Jordan's Ore Shipment",z="lochmodan",s="In the northeastern hills of Loch Modan, Mo'grosh ogres hold Jordan's Ore Shipment. The ore came by caravan from the Wetlands for Bailor Stonehand to refine into an alloy for the smith Jordan Stilwell.",h="In the northeastern hills of Loch Modan, Mo'grosh ogres hold Jordan's Ore Shipment.",sec={{t="An Ambushed Delivery",b="Jordan Stilwell's ore was bound for Bailor Stonehand, a dwarf who would refine it into his special alloy. The caravan carried it south through the mountains from the Wetlands into Loch Modan. Then Mo'grosh ogres ambushed the travelers and dragged the shipment to their stronghold in the wilderness. The surviving guards died of their wounds, and Jordan's smithing project waits for the ore's return.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the shipment?",a="The shipment holds ore for Bailor Stonehand to refine into his special alloy. Jordan Stilwell needs it for his metalwork in Ironforge.",al={"what is in jordan's ore shipment","what ore is this","jordan ore contents"}},{q="Who stole Jordan's Ore Shipment?",a="Mo'grosh ogres ambushed the caravan as it traveled south from the Wetlands. They slaughtered the escorts and hauled the crates to their territory northeast of the Loch.",al={"who took the ore shipment","who stole it","ogres ore shipment"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Bailor Stonehand?",a="Bailor Stonehand is a dwarven craftsman stationed in Loch Modan and an old friend of Jordan Stilwell. He arranged the alloy shipment before ogres overran it.",al={"bailor stonehand","who is bailor"},it="people"},{q="Why is this shipment important to paladins?",a="Paladins undertaking the Test of Righteousness seek the alloy to help Jordan Stilwell forge a consecrated weapon of the Light.",al={"paladin ore shipment","test of righteousness ore","why do paladins need this"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Jordan's Ore Shipment?",a="Jordan's Ore Shipment is a crate of ore that the dwarf Bailor Stonehand was to refine into his special alloy for the smith Jordan Stilwell in Ironforge. The cargo was carried by a caravan inbound from the Wetlands before being ambushed and seized by Mo'grosh ogres in northern Loch Modan.",al={"what is jordans ore shipment","jordan ore shipment info","what is bailors ore"},it="identity",add="bb183b6f"},{q="Where does Jordan's Ore Shipment come from, and who made it?",a="The shipment consists of ore that was en route via caravan from the Wetlands into Loch Modan, where Bailor Stonehand was to refine it into his alloy for his old friend, Jordan Stilwell. Ogres intercepted the transport and killed its guards before it arrived.",al={"who made jordans ore shipment","where did jordans ore shipment come from","origin of jordans ore shipment"},it="origin",add="84b5d642"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, recovering the stolen alloy from the Mo'grosh ogres is a vital step in Jordan Stilwell's commission. It proves your dedication during the Test of Righteousness.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can recognize Bailor Stonehand's specialized alloy as fine dwarven metallurgy. Jordan Stilwell refused ordinary substitutes for his craft."},kw={"alloy","bailor stonehand","jordan stilwell","jordan's ore shipment","loch modan","mo'grosh","test of righteousness"},rel={"quest:1655","npc:bailor-stonehand","quest:1653","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},src={"Jordan's Ore Shipment","Bailor's Ore Shipment"}}
E["item:lurker-venom"] = {t="item",n="Lurker Venom",z="lochmodan",s="In Loch Modan, dwarven defenders need Lurker Venom to counter Dark Iron sabotage. Predatory spiders in the rocky hills and woods provide the toxin.",h="In Loch Modan, dwarven defenders need Lurker Venom to counter Dark Iron sabotage.",sec={{t="A Volatile Reagent",b="Lurker Venom helps dwarves disarm explosives planted by the Dark Iron. Ashlan Stonesmirk, an explosives expert, named spider poison as an ingredient in the mixture Chief Engineer Hinderweir prepares. The solvent joins the venom with rare minerals and tears from the loch’s crocolisks. Together, they form a reactive compound that can disarm complex explosives.\n\nLurker spiders range from common wood lurkers to the matriarch Shanda the Spinner. Their bites threaten travelers and mountaineers across Loch Modan’s hills and crags.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Lurker Venom come from?",a="Loch Modan’s lurker spiders provide the venom. They include Cliff Lurkers, Forest Lurkers, Wood Lurkers, and their matriarch, Shanda the Spinner.",al={"how to get lurker venom","who drops lurker venom","where find lurker venom"},it="origin"},{q="What is Lurker Venom used for?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir uses the venom in a chemical mixture to neutralize and defuse explosives placed by Dark Iron infiltrators around the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"why do i need lurker venom","lurker venom purpose","what does hinderweir do with venom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why use venom to defuse an explosive?",a="Dwarven engineers use reactive, acidic, or caustic mixtures to dissolve delicate mechanical parts or neutralize unstable blasting powders without setting them off.",al={"why spider poison for bombs","how does venom stop dark iron bombs"}},{q="Is Shanda the Spinner the only source?",a="Shanda the Spinner carries the venom, but common wild lurker spiders in Loch Modan’s woodlands and rocky cliffs can provide it too.",al={"do i have to kill shanda","shanda lurker venom"},gp=true},{q="What is Lurker Venom?",a="Lurker Venom is a potent natural toxin harvested from the predatory lurker spiders native to the rugged wilderness of Loch Modan. While deadly to prey, its distinct chemical properties make it valuable to specialized craftsmen and engineers. Chief Engineer Hinderweir specifically utilizes the volatile fluid as a crucial reagent in an alchemical neutralizing solvent designed to safely disarm Dark Iron dwarven explosives.",al={"what is lurker venom","lurker venom lore","what kind of item is lurker venom"},it="identity",add="0e11e6d3"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Using organic toxins to disable hostile explosives shows how dwarven engineers improvise with reactive materials in battle.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Loch Modan’s mountaineers and defenders use dangers from the local wilds to protect vital Khaz Modan works from the Dark Iron clan."},kw={"chief engineer hinderweir","cliff lurker","loch modan","lurker venom","shanda the spinner","spider venom","stonewrought dam","wood lurker"},rel={"quest:161","npc:shanda","zone:lochmodan","item:crocolisk-tear-classic","item:mo-grosh-crystal","subzone:the-loch"},src={"Lurker Venom","A Dark Threat Looms (5)"}}
E["item:miners-gear"] = {t="item",n="Miners' Gear",z="lochmodan",s="In northern Loch Modan, Miners' Gear waits in the Silver Stream Mine. Kobolds have overrun the tunnels, and the Miners' League wants its tools recovered before the local guards attack.",h="In northern Loch Modan, Miners' Gear waits in the Silver Stream Mine.",sec={{t="Supplies of the Miners' League",b="The Silver Stream Mine ran out of ore, so the Miners' League made its quiet tunnels a depot for mining equipment. Kobolds overran the mine, seized the stored goods and made nests among the crates. The league fears an assault by the Mountaineers could wreck the dwarven gear, or scavengers could ruin it. Enter the mine and bring the crates to safety before either fate befalls them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Miners' Gear?",a="Miners' Gear is the Miners' League's crates of dwarven excavation tools, including picks and shovels, stored in the Silver Stream Mine's dry tunnels.",al={"what is miners gear","miners gear items","miners gear loch modan"},it="identity"},{q="Why was the gear left in the mine?",a="After the Silver Stream Mine ran out of ore, the Miners' League turned its empty tunnels into a storage depot. The gear stayed there until kobolds infested the shafts.",al={"why is gear in silver stream mine","why leave gear there"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants this gear recovered?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike directs the Miners' League's recovery effort. He wants the tools salvaged before his fellow warriors march in to kill the kobolds.",al={"who wants miners gear","who needs the gear","mountaineer stormpike gear"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Miners' Gear found?",a="The Miners' League's crates are scattered through the Silver Stream Mine's shafts, in northern Loch Modan east of Algaz Station.",al={"miners gear location","where to find miners gear","miners league crates location"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know the worth of well-forged dwarven iron. Leaving high-grade picks and shovels with candle-wearing scavengers is a small tragedy.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may find kobolds laying their filthy paws on dwarven craft an intolerable insult. The mine calls to be cleared at once."},kw={"filthy paws","kobold","loch modan","miners gear","miners league","mountaineer stormpike","silver stream mine"},rel={"quest:307","subzone:silver-stream-mine","npc:mountaineer-stormpike","zone:lochmodan","topic:kobold","topic:warrior"},src={"Miners' Gear","Filthy Paws (Classic)"}}
E["item:mo-grosh-crystal"] = {t="item",n="Mo'grosh Crystal",z="lochmodan",s="In northeastern Loch Modan, Mo'grosh ogres mine and guard rare crystals with unusual alchemical properties. Dwarven engineers use them to neutralize Dark Iron explosives.",h="In northeastern Loch Modan, Mo'grosh ogres mine and guard rare crystals with unusual alchemical properties.",sec={{t="A Rare Ogresh Commodity",b="Mo'grosh ogres mine the crystals at their stronghold in northeastern Loch Modan. Though the clan favors brute strength over delicate metalwork, its members prize these stones. Enforcers, mystic shamans, and towering leaders carry them. The crystals are uncommon, so the ogres guard them closely within the Mo'grosh Stronghold.",sp=0},{t="Countering the Dark Iron Threat",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir seeks a Mo'grosh Crystal, spider lurker venom, and crocolisk tears. He learned that Dark Iron saboteurs plan to attack the Stonewrought Dam. Dwarven engineers combine the mineral with those reagents to make a compound that disarms and defuses the volatile explosives before the valley can be flooded.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do Mo'grosh Crystals come from?",a="Mo'grosh ogres mine and keep the crystals in northeastern Loch Modan. Any clan member in the Mo'grosh Stronghold might carry one, including mystics, brutes, enforcers, and shamans.",al={"mogrosh crystal location","where to find mogrosh crystal","who drops mogrosh crystal"},it="origin"},{q="What is the crystal used for?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir at the Stonewrought Dam needs a crystal for a neutralizing mixture. Combined with lurker venom and crocolisk tears, it disarms Dark Iron explosives meant to sabotage the dam.",al={"what does mogrosh crystal do","use of mogrosh crystal","why hinderweir wants crystal"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the ogres mining these crystals?",a="Mo'grosh ogres mine rare crystals in the hills around their stronghold. What they use the crystals for is not recorded.",al={"why ogres have crystals","ogre crystal lore"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Mo'grosh Crystal?",a="A Mo'grosh Crystal is an exceptionally rare mineral mined by the Mo'grosh ogres in their stronghold to the northeast of Loch Modan. Prized for its unusual properties, Chief Engineer Hinderweir identifies it as an essential component in brewing a specialized mixture meant to defuse Dark Iron explosives threatening the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"what is mogrosh crystal","mogrosh crystal lore","mo'grosh crystal identity"},it="identity",add="1713c585"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know defending the Stonewrought Dam takes ingenuity. Dwarven engineers turn the ogres' mined treasure into protection against Dark Iron treachery.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can tell these raw minerals come from deep within ogre territory. They react in unusual ways when combined with organic reagents."},kw={"dark threat looms","hinderweir","loch modan","mo'grosh crystal","mogrosh","stonewrought dam"},rel={"quest:161","item:lurker-venom","item:crocolisk-tear-classic","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch"},src={"Mo'grosh Crystal","A Dark Threat Looms (5)"}}
E["item:strange-smelling-powder"] = {t="item",n="Strange Smelling Powder",z="lochmodan",s="In Loch Modan, Strange Smelling Powder has alarmed engineers investigating sabotage. Chief Engineer Hinderweir fears it may be explosive and seeks an expert's judgment.",h="In Loch Modan, Strange Smelling Powder has alarmed engineers investigating sabotage.",sec={{t="A Volatile Discovery",b="Strange Smelling Powder was found amid signs of sabotage against Loch Modan's infrastructure. Chief Engineer Hinderweir fears it may be an engineered explosive, unlike the powder usually used in mining. He cannot identify its mixture or origin, and will not tamper with it himself. Even a small spark could bring disaster.",sp=0},{t="The Road North",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir sends samples through the Algaz Gate into the Wetlands for inspection. Ashlan Stonesmirk, a seasoned explosives expert with the regiment at Dun Modr near the Thandol Span, is to examine the grains and determine what kind of blast the saboteurs are preparing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Strange Smelling Powder?",a="Strange Smelling Powder is suspicious chemical residue found in Loch Modan during an inquiry into local sabotage. Its strong odor and composition lead dwarven engineers to suspect it is explosive.",al={"what is strange smelling powder","what is this powder","powder loch modan"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Chief Engineer Hinderweir want it examined?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir suspects the powder is a specialized explosive. He needs an expert in heavy demolitions to understand the threat to Loch Modan.",al={"why examine powder","hinderweir powder","who needs this powder"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who can identify the powder?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir directs travelers to take the sample to Ashlan Stonesmirk, an explosives expert with the regiment at Dun Modr near the Thandol Span.",al={"who identifies the powder","where do i take the powder","powder expert"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is transporting the powder dangerous?",a="The powder may be volatile, and carrying it means traveling through the Algaz Gate into the marshy, hostile roads of the Wetlands.",al={"is the powder dangerous","why dangerous"},it="danger"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you may recognize the sulfurous scent of unstable blasting mixtures, unlike the standard formulas used in Alliance mining outposts.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know that protecting Loch Modan's stonework and reservoirs is paramount. Any sign of enemy explosives is an immediate crisis for the clan."},kw={"a dark threat looms","ashlan stonesmirk","dun modr","hinderweir","loch modan","strange smelling powder","thandol span"},rel={"quest:161","npc:ashlan-stonesmirk","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","zone:lochmodan"},src={"Strange Smelling Powder","A Dark Threat Looms (3)","A Dark Threat Looms (2)"}}
E["item:trogg-stone-tooth"] = {t="item",n="Trogg Stone Tooth",z="lochmodan",s="In Loch Modan's hills, Stonesplinter troggs leave rugged, mineralized teeth behind. Dwarven defenders use each tooth as proof that the troggs are being hunted along the southern frontier.",h="In Loch Modan's hills, Stonesplinter troggs leave rugged, mineralized teeth behind.",sec={{t="Bounty of the Southern Gate",b="Captain Rugelfuss calls for volunteers to hunt Stonesplinter troggs near Loch Modan's southern gate. With the Ironforge Reserve committed to the Alliance Front, local dwarven garrisons are stretched thin across Khaz Modan. Rugelfuss cannot spare the soldiers at the southern gate guard tower to patrol the nearby hills. So volunteers hunt the lurking troggs and bring back Trogg Stone Teeth as crude, undeniable proof of each beast slain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants these trogg stone teeth?",a="At Loch Modan's southern guard tower, Captain Rugelfuss collects the teeth as proof that travelers are hunting Stonesplinter troggs.",al={"who takes trogg stone teeth","rugelfuss teeth","who needs stone teeth"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the teeth made of stone?",a="Troggs have an earthy, subterranean nature tied to ancient stone origins. Their tusks and teeth are heavy and mineralized, like raw rock.",al={"why stone tooth","trogg anatomy teeth","are trogg teeth rocks"},it="origin"},{q="Why can't the dwarven garrison hunt the troggs themselves?",a="The Ironforge Reserve has joined the wider Alliance war effort, leaving local outposts undermanned. Captain Rugelfuss's regiment must guard the southern gate and cannot leave its fortification unmanned.",al={"why rugelfuss needs help","why are dwarves not fighting troggs","ironforge reserve"},it="why_me"},{q="Which troggs carry these teeth?",a="The teeth come from Stonesplinter troggs in Loch Modan's hills and excavations. They include common diggers, scouts, bone-snapping warriors and geomancers.",al={"where to get trogg stone teeth","who drops stone teeth"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is a Trogg Stone Tooth?",a="A Trogg Stone Tooth is a literal stone-hard tooth taken from the jaws of the Stonesplinter troggs infesting the crags of Loch Modan. Reflecting the troggs' bizarre, earthen nature, these hardened teeth serve the local dwarven defenders as undeniable physical proof that a marauding trogg has been permanently put down.",al={"what is trogg stone tooth","trogg stone tooth info","stone tooth trogg"},it="identity",add="d6a17ab5"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, each recovered tooth helps secure Khaz Modan while much of Ironforge's military serves abroad with the Alliance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, answering Captain Rugelfuss's call eases pressure on the trade paths linking the dwarven kingdoms to the wider Alliance."},kw={"loch modan","rugelfuss","stonesplinter","the trogg threat","trogg","trogg stone tooth"},rel={"quest:267","npc:captain-rugelfuss","topic:trogg","zone:lochmodan","npc:magni-bronzebeard","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance"},src={"Trogg Stone Tooth","The Trogg Threat (Classic)"}}
E["npc:bailor-stonehand"] = {t="npc",n="Bailor Stonehand",z="lochmodan",s="In Thelsamar, Bailor Stonehand waits on ore shipments stolen by Mo'grosh ogres. The skilled dwarven smith crafts a specialized alloy for masterwork armaments and once taught the human weaponsmith Jordan Stilwell.",h="In Thelsamar, Bailor Stonehand waits on ore shipments stolen by Mo'grosh ogres.",sec={{t="Master of the Forge",b="Bailor Stonehand tends the forge in Thelsamar. His knowledge of minerals and specialized alloys reaches beyond Khaz Modan. He taught Jordan Stilwell the foundations of metallurgy and shared formulas for blessed paladin armaments such as Verigan's Fist.",sp=0},{t="Ogre Ambush",b="Mo'grosh ogres in the hills northeast of Thelsamar stole ore shipments bound for Bailor's forge. Without the raw material, he cannot make his rare alloys. He needs travelers and allies to recover the supplies from the ogres' encampments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bailor Stonehand?",a="Bailor Stonehand is a veteran dwarven smith in Thelsamar, Loch Modan. He smelts rare metal alloys and taught Jordan Stilwell the craft of weaponsmithing.",al={"bailor stonehand","who is bailor","thelsamar smith"},it="identity"},{q="What is Bailor's connection to Jordan Stilwell?",a="Bailor taught Jordan Stilwell, a human smith near Ironforge, to work refined ore. He also taught him a special alloy used to make the holy warhammer Verigan's Fist.",al={"bailor and jordan","jordan stilwell teacher","verigan's fist smith"},it="ties"},{q="What happened to Bailor's ore?",a="Mo'grosh ogres in Loch Modan's northeastern mounds intercepted and stole Bailor's raw ore shipment. He has no materials for his specialized metalwork.",al={"bailor ore shipment","who stole bailor's ore","ogre shipment"},it="threat"},{q="Where can Bailor Stonehand be found?",a="Bailor can be found near the center of Thelsamar, the main dwarven town along Loch Modan's main road.",al={"bailor location","where is bailor stonehand","bailor thelsamar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Bailor Stonehand on?",a="Bailor Stonehand is firmly aligned with Ironforge and the Alliance. Residing among his kin in Thelsamar, he plies his craft to support the local dwarven township and aids traveling Alliance adventurers—particularly paladins seeking his metallurgical expertise—in defending the realm against hostile threats.",al={"bailor stonehand faction","is bailor alliance","bailor side"},it="side",add="0eb0f83a"},{q="What does Bailor Stonehand want?",a="Bailor wants to practice his smithing trade undisturbed, but his primary concern is recovering his valuable raw materials. With Mo'grosh ogres having raided and stolen his recent ore shipment, he seeks capable travelers willing to venture into ogre territory to retrieve his lost supplies.",al={"what does bailor want","bailor stonehand goal","bailor motivation"},it="wants",add="a41b979c"},{q="Why is Bailor Stonehand in Thelsamar?",a="Bailor resides in Thelsamar to run his forge and supply the settlement with fine dwarven metalwork. Situated close to the mines and rugged terrain of Loch Modan, the town provides an ideal outpost for an experienced smith, even if local ogre raids occasionally complicate his supply chain.",al={"why is bailor here","bailor loch modan why","why is bailor in thelsamar"},it="why_here",add="346dae44"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you follow a craft Bailor taught Jordan Stilwell. His specialized alloy formula is used to make the sacred hammer Verigan's Fist.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see Bailor's pursuit of rare, resilient metals. His specialized alloys are known across Khaz Modan."},kw={"bailor stonehand","jordan stilwell","loch modan","mo'grosh","smith","thelsamar","verigan's fist"},rel={"npc:jordan-stilwell","subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","quest:1655","topic:dwarf"},src={"Bailor Stonehand"}}
E["npc:bingles-blastenheimer"] = {t="npc",n="Bingles Blastenheimer",z="lochmodan",s="On Loch Modan’s southeastern shore, Bingles Blastenheimer waits beside the wreck of his flying machine. Stranded among troggs and beasts, the gnomish aviator needs his tools and parts back.",h="On Loch Modan’s southeastern shore, Bingles Blastenheimer waits beside the wreck of his flying machine.",sec={{t="A Rough Landing",b="Bingles Blastenheimer took his customized flying craft into the skies, but the landing went badly. His gyrocopter malfunctioned and crashed on Loch Modan’s southeastern shore. Bingles survived, though the machine broke apart. Far from Ironforge, he stays near the wreck, wary of hungry crocolisks and hostile troggs. Troggs from a nearby island stole his tools and Blastencapper explosives, so he asks passing travelers to recover them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bingles Blastenheimer?",a="Bingles Blastenheimer is a gnomish pilot and tinkerer, stranded after his flying machine crashed on Loch Modan’s southeastern shore.",al={"who is bingles","bingles blastenheimer lore","who is the gnome by the lake"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to his flying machine?",a="Bingles crashed his gyrocopter into the Loch. Troggs from a nearby island attacked him and stole his tools and Blastencapper explosives.",al={"why did bingles crash","bingles gyrocopter","what happened to bingles plane"}},{q="Why hasn't Bingles returned to town?",a="Bingles is stranded without his gyrocopter, and troggs from a nearby island stole his tools and Blastencapper explosives. He wants them back for the movement to retake Gnomeregan, so he waits by the wreck for someone to recover them.",al={"why is bingles stranded","why stay by the lake"},it="wants"},{q="Where does Bingles end up after his craft is fixed?",a="Bingles remains at his crash site on the Loch’s southeastern shore, waiting for travelers to recover his missing supplies.",al={"where does bingles go","bingles lodge"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Bingles Blastenheimer on?",a="Bingles is a loyal gnome aligned firmly with Gnomeregan and the Alliance. He relies on friendly Alliance travelers to help recover his lost equipment and ensure his survival in the wilderness of Loch Modan.",al={"bingles blastenheimer faction","is bingles alliance","who does bingles work for"},it="side",add="1e141199"},{q="Why is Bingles Blastenheimer here?",a="Bingles was taking a flight over Loch Modan in his beloved gyrocopter when disaster struck. His flying machine crashed along the shores of the lake, leaving him stranded and isolated among the dangerous beasts and hostile troggs roaming the wilderness.",al={"why is bingles in loch modan","how did bingles get here","bingles blastenheimer crash"},it="why_here",add="89c66e03"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you share Bingles’s drive to take gnomish invention into the skies, even when mechanical failure brings a hard landing.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know the trouble of losing custom spanners and gadgets to troggs after a flight goes wrong."},kw={"bingles","blastenheimer","gnome","gyrocopter","loch modan","pilot"},rel={"quest:2038","quest:2039","subzone:the-loch","zone:lochmodan","topic:gnome"},src={"Bingles Blastenheimer"}}
E["npc:brock-stoneseeker"] = {t="npc",n="Brock Stoneseeker",z="lochmodan",s="In Thelsamar, Brock Stoneseeker teaches mining to novice prospectors. At his School of Mining and Surveying, he trains them to find and extract ores and minerals.",h="In Thelsamar, Brock Stoneseeker teaches mining to novice prospectors.",sec={{t="Master of Mining and Surveying",b="In Thelsamar, Brock Stoneseeker teaches miners at his School of Mining and Surveying. Loch Modan's hills hold rich mineral veins, and miners need a sure hand with a pickaxe and a keen eye for rock. Brock teaches them to find ore, extract raw metals, and survey underground deposits. His lessons help Alliance tradesfolk supply Ironforge's smithies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brock Stoneseeker?",a="Brock Stoneseeker trains miners in Thelsamar, in Loch Modan. At his School of Mining and Surveying, he teaches tradesfolk to extract ore and survey mineral deposits.",al={"brock stoneseeker","who is brock","brock thelsamar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Brock Stoneseeker be found?",a="Brock Stoneseeker can be found in Thelsamar, the main dwarven town in Loch Modan. He runs his mining school near the local tradesmen.",al={"where is brock","brock stoneseeker location","brock map"},gp=true},{q="What profession does Brock teach?",a="Brock Stoneseeker teaches Mining. He shows travelers how to gather rough stone, copper, and other early ores found across the Khaz Modan countryside.",al={"what does brock teach","brock trainer type","mining trainer thelsamar"},gp=true},{q="What is Brock's School of Mining and Surveying?",a="Brock's School of Mining and Surveying is a training school in Thelsamar. Brock teaches prospectors to extract minerals safely and read underground veins throughout the mountains.",al={"brocks school","school of mining thelsamar"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Brock Stoneseeker on?",a="Brock Stoneseeker stands firmly with the Ironforge dwarves and the Grand Alliance. Operating out of the tranquil settlement of Thelsamar in Loch Modan, he serves the mountaineers and wayfarers of Khaz Modan by training skilled miners to prospect the craggy hills of the dwarven homeland.",al={"brock stoneseeker faction","is brock stoneseeker alliance","who does brock stoneseeker serve"},it="side",add="38215f8d"},{q="Why is Brock Stoneseeker here?",a="Brock makes his home in Thelsamar to run Brock's School of Mining and Surveying. The cliffs and mountains surrounding Loch Modan are rich with raw stone and mineral veins, making it an ideal post to instruct aspiring miners and send them out into the surrounding crags.",al={"why is brock stoneseeker in thelsamar","why is brock here","what brought brock to loch modan"},it="why_here",add="53fa3834"},{q="What does Brock Stoneseeker want?",a="Brock wants to teach the essential dwarven craft of mining to newcomers and honor the most dedicated students of his school. He seeks to ensure that prospectors head into the rugged wilds of Khaz Modan well-equipped to strike rich ore and survey the land.",al={"what does brock stoneseeker want","brock stoneseeker goals","what does brock want"},it="wants",add="7d1f98e6"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner in Loch Modan, you can find Brock Stoneseeker in Thelsamar to begin or advance your training in unearthing and smelting regional ores.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Khaz Modan, you inherit a tradition built on stone and metal. Teachers like Brock help sustain Ironforge's craft traditions."},kw={"brock stoneseeker","loch modan","mining trainer","school of mining","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf","quest:6387","quest:6392"},src={"Brock Stoneseeker"}}
E["npc:captain-rugelfuss"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Rugelfuss",z="lochmodan",s="At Loch Modan’s southern gate, Captain Rugelfuss meets a sudden trogg uprising. The stern dwarf organizes the defense of the border.",h="At Loch Modan’s southern gate, Captain Rugelfuss meets a sudden trogg uprising.",sec={{t="Holding the Southern Gate",b="From the Valley of Kings, Captain Rugelfuss guards Loch Modan’s southern gateway. Ironforge’s forces are stretched thin across the world, so veteran officers like him defend its home territories. He sets military ceremony aside and turns to the danger at the border.",sp=0},{t="The Trogg Incursion",b="Troggs surge into the highlands from ancient caverns. They have overwhelmed outlying dwarven patrols and built fortified footholds nearby. Rugelfuss calls on capable travelers to thin their ranks and drive them back from the roadway, defending the King’s lands.",sp=0},{t="Frontline Reconnaissance",b="Rugelfuss’s mountaineers keep watch beyond the gate. They continually scout trogg encampments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Rugelfuss?",a="At Loch Modan’s southern gateway in the Valley of Kings, Captain Rugelfuss commands Ironforge’s defense. He guards the frontier against the trogg uprising.",al={"captain rugelfuss lore","who is rugelfuss","rugelfuss loch modan"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Captain Rugelfuss be found?",a="You can find Captain Rugelfuss near the South Gate in the Valley of Kings. He guards the southern pass from Loch Modan toward Dun Morogh.",al={"where is rugelfuss","captain rugelfuss location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Captain Rugelfuss concerned about troggs?",a="A recent trogg uprising threatens dwarven settlements and supply lines. Troggs have reached the southern gateway and attacked Ironforge patrols, putting the King’s territory at risk.",al={"why fight troggs","trogg threat loch modan"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Rugelfuss brush off military formalities?",a="Rugelfuss sets ceremony aside because he sees it as a distraction while the King’s lands face attack. He wants practical action at the border.",al={"rugelfuss personality","at ease race"}},{q="Whose side is Captain Rugelfuss on?",a="Captain Rugelfuss stands firmly with Ironforge and the Grand Alliance. As an officer defending the southern approaches of Loch Modan, his sworn duty is safeguarding the dwarven lands and upholding King Magni Bronzebeard's authority against outside threats.",al={"captain rugelfuss faction","who does rugelfuss serve","is rugelfuss alliance"},it="side",add="506fbcb9"},{q="What does Captain Rugelfuss want?",a="Rugelfuss wants to suppress the trogg uprising threatening the Valley of Kings and the King's lands. He relies on passing travelers to cull the invading trogg ranks and push the creatures back from the roads of Loch Modan.",al={"what does rugelfuss need","rugelfuss objective","what is rugelfuss trying to do"},it="wants",add="8c27dafb"},{q="Why is Captain Rugelfuss stationed in the Valley of Kings?",a="Rugelfuss is posted at the southern frontier of Loch Modan to guard the pass leading toward Dun Morogh. With troggs swarming the surrounding valleys, an organized dwarven military presence is essential to hold the roadway and coordinate defense for the King's lands.",al={"why is captain rugelfuss here","why is rugelfuss at the south gate","rugelfuss post"},it="why_here",add="0fa68497"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Ironforge’s resolve in Captain Rugelfuss’s defense of ancestral mountain passes against subterranean foes.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know that guarding the homelands from savage incursions matters while armies fight elsewhere.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you may recognize Rugelfuss’s direct approach: clear the front lines with blade and shield."},kw={"captain rugelfuss","ironforge guard","loch modan","mountaineer","rugelfuss","trogg threat","valley of kings"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-kings","zone:lochmodan","quest:217","quest:267","topic:trogg","topic:dwarf"},src={"Captain Rugelfuss"}}
E["npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii"] = {t="npc",n="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",z="lochmodan",s="Atop the Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII watches over its workings and defenses. The veteran dwarf keeps the great structure and its machinery sound as grave dangers threaten it.",h="Atop the Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII watches over its workings and defenses.",sec={{t="Master of the Dam",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII tends the Stonewrought Dam, whose stonework holds back Loch Modan's waters. Along the crest, he watches the waterways and sluice gates. He also checks for strain from the elements and local hazards. The dam's workings need constant care.",sp=0},{t="Sabotage and Subversion",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII finds signs of planned sabotage at the dam. A breach could flood the lowlands and ruin Khaz Modan's delicate infrastructure. So he calls on reliable Alliance adventurers to trace the plot, disarm hidden explosives, and stop the threat before the stone gives way.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII tends and defends the Stonewrought Dam in northern Loch Modan.",al={"hinderweir","chief engineer","dam engineer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="You can find Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII on the Stonewrought Dam's top walkway. The dam crosses Loch Modan's northern edge near the Wetlands border.",al={"hinderweir location","where is hinderweir","find hinderweir"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Stonewrought Dam?",a="The Stonewrought Dam is a great dwarven structure that holds back Loch Modan's waters. It keeps them from spilling violently into the lower wetlands to the north.",al={"what is the dam","stonewrought dam purpose","why is the dam important"}},{q="What threats is Hinderweir worried about?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII investigates sabotage at the dam. He has found signs of dark plots and explosive devices planted to crack its foundations.",al={"dam threats","a dark threat looms","who wants to destroy the dam"},it="threat"},{q="Why does his name include 'VII'?",a="VII is the Roman numeral for seven. No record explains why it appears in Hinderweir's name.",al={"hinderweir name","why the seventh","hinderweir vii meaning"},it="name"},{q="What quests does Chief Engineer Hinderweir offer?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII offers the chain called 'A Dark Threat Looms'. It sends adventurers to investigate tampering and protect the Stonewrought Dam from destruction.",al={"hinderweir quests","quests at the dam","a dark threat looms quest"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII on?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is a proud dwarf loyal to Ironforge and the Alliance. Stationed at the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan, his foremost duty is safeguarding one of the greatest engineering marvels of the dwarven kingdom from any outside perils.",al={"hinderweir faction","is hinderweir alliance","who does hinderweir serve"},it="side",add="35f113ec"},{q="What does Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII want?",a="Hinderweir wants to ensure the absolute integrity and defense of the Stonewrought Dam. Suspecting foul play and looming sabotage against the massive structure, he seeks reliable adventurers to investigate suspicious activities nearby and neutralize any dark threats before catastrophe strikes Loch Modan.",al={"hinderweir goal","what does chief engineer hinderweir want","hinderweir motive"},it="wants",add="3db73bdf"},{q="Why is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII here?",a="As the chief engineer overseeing the Stonewrought Dam, Hinderweir is stationed directly on the massive structure to supervise its ongoing operation and security. He remains vigilant on-site to address structural concerns and confront immediate dangers menacing the loch.",al={"why is hinderweir at the dam","why is chief engineer hinderweir here","hinderweir loch modan purpose"},it="why_here",add="53bdb0ce"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Hinderweir's solemn duty: protecting Khaz Modan's greatest works in stone from outside malice.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate the dam's vast machinery, where civil architecture meets mechanical control.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you cannot afford to let the dam fall. Its destruction would disrupt supply routes and devastate allied lands north of Loch Modan."},kw={"a dark threat looms","dwarf","engineer","hinderweir","loch modan","sabotage","stonewrought dam"},rel={"subzone:stonewrought-dam","quest:161","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf"},src={"Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII"}}
E["npc:daryl-the-youngling"] = {t="npc",n="Daryl the Youngling",z="lochmodan",s="At Farstrider Lodge, Daryl the Youngling tests travelers' marksmanship against Loch Modan's beasts. The young human hunter hopes to earn his place among veteran dwarven trackers.",h="At Farstrider Lodge, Daryl the Youngling tests travelers' marksmanship against Loch Modan's beasts.",sec={{t="A Human Among Mountaineers",b="Dwarven mountaineers, trackers, and seasoned outdoorsmen watch Loch Modan's wilderness from Farstrider Lodge. Daryl tests his hunting instincts against travelers there. He challenges them to hunt the tough wild boars and other beasts roaming the crags and lakeshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Daryl the Youngling?",a="Daryl is a young human hunter at Farstrider Lodge in Loch Modan. Among the lodge's seasoned dwarven marksmen, he challenges newcomers to test their hunting and tracking skills.",al={"who is daryl","daryl lore","who is daryl the youngling"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Daryl be found?",a="Daryl stays at Farstrider Lodge, on forested cliffs above Loch Modan's southeastern shores.",al={"daryl location","where is daryl the youngling","where to find daryl"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is he called 'the Youngling'?",a="The lodge's dwarven marksmen and regulars have spent decades patrolling Khaz Modan's rugged backcountry. Daryl is young and untested beside them, still earning a lasting reputation as a hunter.",al={"why youngling","daryl nickname"},it="name"},{q="Whose side is Daryl the Youngling on?",a="Daryl is allied with the Alliance and makes his camp among the dwarven marksmen of Loch Modan. Stationed at Farstrider Lodge, he works alongside his fellow mountaineers and outdoorsmen to secure the region's wilderness.",al={"daryl faction","is daryl alliance","who does daryl serve"},it="side",add="e75652fe"},{q="What does Daryl the Youngling want?",a="Daryl is eager to prove his skill as an archer and outdoorsman. He looks for capable adventurers to test their tracking and hunting abilities against the local wildlife of Loch Modan, relishing the thrill of the chase and the challenges of the hunt.",al={"what does daryl want","daryl goals","daryl quests"},it="wants",add="a39b90d4"},{q="Why is Daryl the Youngling at Farstrider Lodge?",a="Farstrider Lodge serves as a haven for the valley's finest trackers and beast hunters. Daryl spends his time here honing his craft alongside veteran dwarven sharpshooters, taking advantage of the rich game that roams the hills of Loch Modan.",al={"why is daryl here","why is daryl in loch modan","daryl youngling farstrider lodge"},it="why_here",add="f7496387"},{q="Who is Daryl the Youngling tied to?",a="Daryl keeps company with the huntsmen and lodge keepers of Farstrider Lodge, including Vyrin Swiftwind. He shares their dedication to the hunt and assists them in managing the wild beasts that prowl near the dwarven outpost.",al={"daryl allies","daryl farstrider lodge","who is daryl with"},it="ties",add="d22cfcb5"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Daryl's contests test the tracking, knowledge of beast behavior, and hunting skill that wandering hunters bring to Farstrider Lodge.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can find a young person learning wilderness craft deep in dwarven territory. Practical camaraderie joins Ironforge and the human kingdoms."},kw={"boar hunting","daryl","farstrider lodge","hunter","hunter's boast","loch modan","youngling"},rel={"subzone:farstrider-lodge","zone:lochmodan","quest:257","quest:258"},src={"Daryl the Youngling"}}
E["npc:huldar"] = {t="npc",n="Huldar",z="lochmodan",s="Huldar is stranded on Loch Modan’s southern road after his blast powder delivery is stopped. The dwarven teamster needs help getting the cargo to the southern excavation site, where archaeologists and prospectors need supplies.",h="Huldar is stranded on Loch Modan’s southern road after his blast powder delivery is stopped.",sec={{t="A Powder Run in Peril",b="Huldar’s damaged wagon leaves him stranded near the lake’s southern bend. Local wildlife and troggs threaten the road, and Dark Iron infiltrators lurk nearby. He needs passing travelers to guard the remaining powder kegs and carry the shipment to the dig.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Huldar?",a="Huldar is a dwarven teamster stranded beside his wagon on Loch Modan’s southern bank. His blast powder delivery to the nearby excavation site was stopped.",al={"who is huldar","huldar loch modan","wagon dwarf"},it="identity"},{q="What is in Huldar's wagon?",a="Huldar’s wagon carries barrels of blast powder. Dwarven prospectors and archaeologists at the southern excavation site need the explosives.",al={"what is huldar transporting","huldar wagon cargo","what are the barrels"},it="item"},{q="Why is Huldar stuck on the road?",a="Hostile beasts, troggs, and Dark Iron dwarf saboteurs threaten the roads through southern Loch Modan. An ambush stopped Huldar’s shipment, so he seeks help guarding and delivering the remaining supplies.",al={"why is huldar stranded","huldar ambush"},it="why_here"},{q="Why do the Dark Iron dwarves care about his cargo?",a="The Dark Iron clan seeks to undermine Ironforge’s presence and historical research throughout Loch Modan. By cutting off blast powder, they can halt excavation and deprive dwarven operations of defensive and industrial supplies.",al={"dark iron blast powder","why dark irons attack huldar"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Huldar on?",a="Huldar is loyal to Ironforge and the Alliance. He works directly in service of the dwarven prospectors and miners operating in Loch Modan, hauling essential munitions across the territory while standing firm against the hostile Dark Iron clan infiltrating the region.",al={"is huldar alliance","who does huldar serve","huldar faction"},it="side",add="ff7033f4"},{q="What does Huldar want?",a="Huldar wants to deliver his shipment of blasting powder safely to the dwarven excavation site. Dark Iron dwarves ambushed his caravan along the Loch's southern road, leaving him in need of stalwart travelers to protect the cargo and push back the saboteurs.",al={"what is huldar trying to do","huldar goal","what does huldar need"},it="wants",add="9f03f8e3"},{q="Who is Huldar tied to?",a="Huldar is tied to the dwarven excavators stationed in Loch Modan. His team is tasked with hauling vital supplies and blasting powder directly to their dig sites, ensuring their operations can continue despite the growing threat of Dark Iron incursions.",al={"who does huldar work for","huldar connections","who is huldar supplying"},it="ties",add="577cb64e"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, helping Huldar supports the Explorer's League dig site and supplies your kin with powder to unearth ancient titan secrets.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know raw blast powder is valuable and volatile, especially in exposed wooden barrels."},kw={"blast powder","caravan","dark iron","excavation","huldar","loch modan","wagon"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","quest:273","quest:309","quest:454","topic:dwarf"},src={"Huldar"}}
E["npc:jern-hornhelm"] = {t="npc",n="Jern Hornhelm",z="lochmodan",s="In Thelsamar, Jern Hornhelm keeps the Explorers' League supplied and its messages moving. He coordinates deliveries between the town, Ironforge, and Loch Modan's deeper dig site, while travelers carry supplies and progress reports across the region.",h="In Thelsamar, Jern Hornhelm keeps the Explorers' League supplied and its messages moving.",sec={{t="Logistics in Thelsamar",b="From Thelsamar, Jern Hornhelm sends supplies to Loch Modan's dig sites. Dwarven scholars and field teams search the wilderness for their ancestral past, and their work depends on steady deliveries of resources and tools. Jern also makes sure messages reach the active digs.",sp=0},{t="Serving the Explorers' League",b="Jern Hornhelm connects field archaeologists with the Explorers' League leadership in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. Ironband's Excavation needs blasting powder, equipment, and regular dispatches to keep its work moving. Jern asks trusted travelers to carry supplies and reports along trogg-infested roads, so the dig can continue.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jern Hornhelm?",a="Jern Hornhelm is a dwarven miner in Thelsamar who coordinates logistics for the Explorers' League. He keeps local excavation work supplied and moving.",al={"who is jern","jern hornhelm identity","thelsamar dwarf jern"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Jern Hornhelm?",a="Jern Hornhelm stands outdoors in Thelsamar, near the center of Loch Modan along the main road.",al={"jern hornhelm location","where is jern","jern hornhelm map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What faction does Jern Hornhelm belong to?",a="Jern Hornhelm is aligned with the Alliance and represents the dwarven Explorers' League. He manages the movement of personnel and mining supplies.",al={"jern hornhelm faction","who does jern work for","is jern explorers league"},it="side"},{q="Why does Jern need blasting powder sent to the excavation?",a="The mountainous dig site needs blasting powder to break through stubborn rock faces. Jern coordinates its delivery to Prospector Ironband's site east of the lake, where the crew works to uncover ancient ruins.",al={"powder to ironband lore","why excavation needs powder","blasting powder loch modan"},it="wants"},{q="What is Jern Hornhelm's connection to Ironforge?",a="Jern Hornhelm connects Loch Modan's remote digs with Explorers' League leadership in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. He frequently sends field progress reports back to Ironforge.",al={"jern hornhelm ironforge","report to ironforge jern"},it="ties"},{q="What problems are the dig sites facing in Loch Modan?",a="Troggs harry Ironband's Excavation and slow its progress. Supply runs are also in danger: Dark Iron dwarves ambushed a blastpowder shipment bound for the site, so Jern depends on armed travelers to get deliveries through.",al={"ironband excavation problems","loch modan dig dangers","why jern needs help"},it="threat"},{q="Why is Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar?",a="Jern Hornhelm is stationed in Thelsamar to manage logistics for local archaeological digs across Loch Modan. Working in support of the Explorers' League, he coordinates critical supplies, reports, and blasting materials between Ironforge and remote digs like Ironband's Excavation, ensuring the League's operations stay funded and equipped.",al={"why is jern hornhelm here","jern hornhelm purpose loch modan","why is jern in thelsamar"},it="why_here",add="1cf890d8"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you help uncover your people's ancient Titan heritage, buried deep within the mountains.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can appreciate Jern's trade background and practical knowledge of underground logistics, blasting, and hauling resources.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler in Loch Modan, you can turn to Jern for help securing the region and maintaining dwarven infrastructure."},kw={"blasting powder","excavation","explorers' league","ironband","jern hornhelm","loch modan","miner","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","topic:explorers-league","quest:436","quest:302","quest:273","quest:298","quest:301"},src={"Jern Hornhelm"}}
E["npc:marek-ironheart"] = {t="npc",n="Marek Ironheart",z="lochmodan",s="At the Farstrider Lodge in south-eastern Loch Modan, Marek Ironheart tests hunters who seek the lodge’s respect. The veteran dwarf follows the traditions of the wild.",h="At the Farstrider Lodge in south-eastern Loch Modan, Marek Ironheart tests hunters who seek the lodge’s...",sec={{t="Master of the Hunt",b="The Farstrider Lodge gathers marksmen and trackers from across the dwarven lands on a ridge above the lake. Marek cares little for titles or boasts. Visitors earn the hunters’ respect through skill against Loch Modan’s beasts, and by showing a true hunter’s patience and nerve.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marek Ironheart?",a="At the Farstrider Lodge in Loch Modan, Marek Ironheart tests visitors seeking acceptance among its trackers and outdoorsmen.",al={"marek ironheart","who is marek"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Marek Ironheart?",a="Marek Ironheart can be found at the Farstrider Lodge, in the hills along Loch Modan’s south-eastern shore.",al={"marek ironheart location","where is marek"},gp=true},{q="What kind of tasks does Marek offer?",a="Marek sends hunters to track and cull local wildlife around the loch. Dangerous crocolisks test their skill at survival.",al={"marek ironheart quests","marek quests"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Marek related to any other known dwarves?",a="Marek Ironheart may be kin to Archaeologist Adamant Ironheart and Imme Ironheart, who share his notable dwarven surname. Marek devotes his life to hunting rather than excavating relics.",al={"ironheart family","marek relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Marek Ironheart on?",a="Marek stands with the Alliance and the dwarven clans of Ironforge. Operating out of Farstrider Lodge in the southeastern wilds of Loch Modan, he welcomes fellow Alliance travelers to prove their worth by mastering the surrounding wilderness.",al={"marek ironheart faction","marek ironheart alliance","is marek ironheart alliance"},it="side",add="ac3880c9"},{q="What does Marek Ironheart want?",a="Marek works from the Farstrider Lodge in Loch Modan, where he invites hunters to pursue the crocolisks around the loch.",al={"what does marek want","marek ironheart goals","why talk to marek ironheart"},it="wants",add="2928b65a"},{q="Why is Marek Ironheart at Farstrider Lodge?",a="Marek makes his home at Farstrider Lodge to test and train woodsmen in the untamed hills of Loch Modan. From this remote outpost, he watches over the local wildlife and guides hunters seeking to hone their fieldcraft in the highland wilderness.",al={"why is marek in loch modan","marek ironheart farstrider lodge purpose","why is marek here"},it="why_here",add="ddec60fb"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you see Marek Ironheart’s Farstrider Lodge traditions in challenges that test your accuracy and tracking against local wildlife.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see in Marek the outdoorsman culture cherished by many Khaz Modan dwarves. He chooses the mountains’ quiet watch over Ironforge’s forge fires."},kw={"crocolisk hunting","farstrider lodge","hunter","hunting","ironheart","loch modan","marek ironheart"},rel={"subzone:farstrider-lodge","zone:lochmodan","quest:385","topic:dwarf"},src={"Marek Ironheart"}}
E["npc:mountaineer-kadrell"] = {t="npc",n="Mountaineer Kadrell",z="lochmodan",s="Across from the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar, Mountaineer Kadrell keeps watch over Loch Modan.",h="Across from the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar, Mountaineer Kadrell keeps watch over Loch Modan.",sec={{t="The Sentry of Thelsamar",b="Mountaineer Kadrell watches over Thelsamar and directs Loch Modan’s dwarven defenses. Troggs, gnolls, and native beasts press against outposts along the valley’s edges. From the town’s center, Kadrell sends reinforcements, relays orders, and considers reports from scouts in the field.",sp=0},{t="Keeping the Lines Open",b="Mountaineer Kadrell stays in touch with Thelsamar’s distant forward posts. He coordinates with Mountaineer Stormpike and sends adventurers to report to sentries such as Mountaineer Rockgar. The outposts guard the mountain passes, so Kadrell helps supply them, reinforce their ranks, and carry word of threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Mountaineer Kadrell be found?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell can be found across the road from the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar, among Loch Modan’s rolling hills.",al={"kadrell location","where is kadrell","find kadrell"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Kadrell's role in Loch Modan?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell serves with the dwarven Mountaineers, carrying messages between Thelsamar’s local leaders and distant guard posts. He coordinates patrols, supplies, and reports from the border.",al={"what does kadrell do","kadrell purpose","kadrell job"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do other mountaineers send runners to Kadrell?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell is stationed by Thelsamar’s inn and main thoroughfare, where field dispatches can reach him. Urgent reports from distant scouts pass through him to the settlement’s defenses.",al={"report to kadrell","why report to kadrell"},it="motive"},{q="Who does Kadrell coordinate with?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell works with other mountaineers in the field, including Mountaineer Stormpike and Mountaineer Rockgar. They share scouting reports and arrange defenses against local threats.",al={"kadrell contacts","who does kadrell know"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Mountaineer Kadrell?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell is a dwarven defender stationed in Thelsamar. As a member of the Mountaineers, Ironforge's dedicated territorial guard, he helps oversee the defense of the Loch Modan region, organizing local scouting efforts and keeping supply lines and outposts secure.",al={"who is kadrell","mountaineer kadrell","kadrell identity"},it="identity",add="fc9aa592"},{q="Whose side is Mountaineer Kadrell on?",a="Kadrell stands firmly with the Kingdom of Ironforge and the Alliance. His duties place him in the service of King Magni Bronzebeard, working alongside fellow mountaineers, town marshals, and local dwarves to hold the borders of Khaz Modan against encroaching threats.",al={"kadrell faction","is kadrell alliance","kadrell loyalty"},it="side",add="24c7e32d"},{q="What does Mountaineer Kadrell want?",a="Kadrell wants to secure Thelsamar and the surrounding wilderness of Loch Modan. With local forces stretched thin, he looks for capable travelers to help clear out the tunnel rat kobolds fouling the western foothills, roving gnoll packs, and other pests menacing the roads and outlying guard stations.",al={"what does kadrell want","kadrell goal","kadrell objectives"},it="wants",add="3819644d"},{q="Why is Mountaineer Kadrell in Thelsamar?",a="Kadrell is stationed directly across from the Stoutlager Inn to act as a central contact point in Thelsamar. Because the town is the primary hub of Loch Modan, remaining here allows him to receive reports from remote guard posts and dispatch travelers where help is needed most.",al={"why is kadrell in thelsamar","why is kadrell here","kadrell post"},it="why_here",add="56ea1ebe"},{q="Who is Mountaineer Kadrell tied to?",a="Kadrell is closely connected to the network of Ironforge Mountaineers patrolling the valley, including Mountaineer Stormpike and Mountaineer Rockgar. He coordinates with outpost scouts across Loch Modan to channel information and reinforcements wherever border stations come under pressure.",al={"kadrell connections","who does kadrell work with","kadrell ties"},it="ties",add="f9923f59"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler passing through Thelsamar, you can carry messages and aid distant mountaineer outposts facing regional threats.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Kadrell belongs to the Mountaineer corps. Their watch protects Ironforge’s eastern territories from dangers in the wilderness."},kw={"kadrell","loch modan","mountaineer","rockgar","stormpike","stoutlager inn","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","subzone:stoutlager-inn","quest:414","quest:468","npc:mountaineer-stormpike","quest:1339","quest:467"},src={"Mountaineer Kadrell"}}
E["npc:mountaineer-stormpike"] = {t="npc",n="Mountaineer Stormpike",z="lochmodan",s="At Algaz Station, Mountaineer Stormpike keeps watch over Loch Modan's northern road into the Wetlands. A proud member of Ironforge's Stormpike clan, he guards its supply routes from troggs and kobolds.",h="At Algaz Station, Mountaineer Stormpike keeps watch over Loch Modan's northern road into the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Guardian of Algaz Station",b="Mountaineer Stormpike guards the northern road from Algaz Station, where Loch Modan gives way to Dun Algaz. The road descends through the pass into the Wetlands, amid rocky crags and wilderness threats. Stormpike keeps communication open and the way clear for travelers and supply convoys crossing the pass.",sp=0},{t="Contending with Local Menaces",b="Kobolds from nearby digs and troggs from beneath the ground trouble northern Loch Modan. Stormpike calls on passing adventurers to disrupt these threats. Kobolds have entered Silver Stream Mine and taken the Miners' League's stored dwarven tools.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Mountaineer Stormpike?",a="Find Mountaineer Stormpike at Algaz Station in northern Loch Modan. He watches the mountain road north through Dun Algaz toward the Wetlands.",al={"stormpike location","where is stormpike","mountaineer stormpike loc"},gp=true},{q="Who is Mountaineer Stormpike?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike belongs to Ironforge's Stormpike clan. He stands sentry and scouts Loch Modan's northern pass against wilderness dangers.",al={"who is stormpike","mountaineer stormpike lore","who is mountaineer stormpike"},it="identity"},{q="What threats does he deal with at Algaz Station?",a="Troggs and kobolds threaten the hillsides and quarries near Algaz Station. Stormpike works to drive them off so couriers and caravans can travel safely.",al={"algaz station dangers","what is attacking algaz station","loch modan north threats"},it="threat"},{q="What is Algaz Station's purpose?",a="Algaz Station is an Ironforge outpost watching the border between Loch Modan and the rugged tunnels of Dun Algaz. Mountaineers use it as a waystation while patrolling the frontier and keeping the trade road clear.",al={"what is algaz station","algaz station lore","purpose of algaz station"},it="place"},{q="Is he related to the Stormpike Guard in Alterac Valley?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike bears the name of the prominent Stormpike clan, a dwarven lineage known across Ironforge for its fierce warriors and prospectors. His orders keep him on the passes of Loch Modan.",al={"alterac stormpike","stormpike clan connection","is he part of the stormpike guard"},it="ties"},{q="What tasks does Mountaineer Stormpike give to adventurers?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike sends adventurers to recover the Miners' League's gear from Silver Stream Mine. He also asks them to carry his order for a new shield to Furen Longbeard, the dwarven armorsmith in Stormwind.",al={"stormpike quests","mountaineer stormpike tasks","filthy paws quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Mountaineer Stormpike on?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike is fiercely loyal to Ironforge and the Bronzebeard clan, serving as a proud member of the dwarven Mountaineers. He guards the mountain pass on behalf of King Magni Bronzebeard and stands firmly with the Alliance, harboring deep distrust toward the Dark Iron clan.",al={"mountaineer stormpike faction","who does mountaineer stormpike serve","stormpike loyalty"},it="side",add="21d9c7b3"},{q="What does Mountaineer Stormpike want?",a="Stationed along the rugged northern road, Stormpike wants to keep the pass safe from troggs, kobolds, and other threats descending from the hills. He seeks reliable couriers and able fighters to carry out deliveries, clear encroaching vermin, and maintain communications between Algaz Station and the rest of Loch Modan.",al={"what does stormpike want","stormpike goal","mountaineer stormpike purpose"},it="wants",add="1b65a761"},{q="Why is Mountaineer Stormpike here at Algaz Station?",a="Algaz Station guards the vital northern route connecting Loch Modan toward the Wetlands. Stormpike is posted here to watch the pass, coordinate patrols, and ensure supplies and reports travel securely between the scattered mountain outposts and Ironforge's broader defense network.",al={"why is mountaineer stormpike here","why is stormpike at algaz station","stormpike location reason"},it="why_here",add="60d9a34d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you honor a fellow mountaineer by helping Stormpike guard Khaz Modan's interior borders from scavenging vermin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Algaz Station guards the overland route between Ironforge and Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Stormpike's watch helps keep that route open for the Alliance."},kw={"algaz","dun","kobold","loch","modan","mountaineer","station","stormpike","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:algaz-station","zone:lochmodan","quest:307","quest:1339","quest:1338","topic:dwarf","topic:kobold"},src={"Mountaineer Stormpike"}}
E["npc:prospector-ironband"] = {t="npc",n="Prospector Ironband",z="lochmodan",s="At Ironband's Excavation Site, Prospector Ironband leads a search through Khaz Modan's buried past. He directs the Dwarven Explorers' Guild's work in southeastern Loch Modan, seeking the heritage of the dwarven people. Despite setbacks and hostile creatures, he sends reports and relics to Ironforge.",h="At Ironband's Excavation Site, Prospector Ironband leads a search through Khaz Modan's buried past.",sec={{t="Unearthing the Past",b="Prospector Ironband leads the dig at Ironband's Excavation Site in southeastern Loch Modan. Like other field researchers in the Explorers' Guild, he believes Khaz Modan's soil holds truths about the origins of the dwarven race. His camp digs trenches and sifts rubble for ancient relics, stone tablets, and earthen artifacts. The work is slow, but Ironband remains resolute and welcomes capable travelers who can safeguard the operation.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Troubles",b="Troggs and wildlife threaten the excavation in Loch Modan's rugged wilds. They endanger the dig's supplies and equipment, and relics or survey tools may be stolen or wrecked before the Guild can examine them. Ironband relies on visiting Alliance travelers to guard cargo shipments and hold off raiders. He also asks them to look into missing Guild contacts in the neighboring badlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Ironband?",a="Prospector Ironband leads the Dwarven Explorers' Guild's archaeological dig in southeastern Loch Modan. He directs field work to recover relics of titan and earthen history.",al={"ironband lore","who is darteus ironband","prospector ironband"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Prospector Ironband?",a="You can find Prospector Ironband at Ironband's Excavation Site, in the hills of southeastern Loch Modan, just east of the main road toward the southern border.",al={"ironband location","where is ironband","ironband excavation site loc"},gp=true},{q="What is the Explorers' Guild digging for here?",a="The Explorers' Guild digs through ancient stone ruins across Khaz Modan to learn the origins of the dwarven people and uncover artifacts left by the Titans.",al={"why is ironband digging","what are they excavating","ironband dig goals"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Ironband need adventurers to protect shipments?",a="Ironband's dig depends on blastpowder and supplies shipped from Thelsamar across Loch Modan. One earlier powder shipment never arrived, Dark Iron dwarves threaten porters on the road, and troggs harass the camp.",al={"protecting the shipment lore","why defend the goods","ironband supplies"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Agmond and why does Ironband ask about him?",a="Agmond was a dwarf surveyor who went south to scout excavations. When contact was lost, Ironband asked travelers to search the Badlands and learn what had become of him.",al={"find agmond","who is agmond","agmond's fate"}},{q="Is Prospector Ironband related to Bardin Ironband?",a="Darteus Ironband and Bardin Ironband share a surname and both work closely with frontier dwarf operations, which suggests they may be kin. Darteus remains focused on archaeology and Guild reports.",al={"bardin ironband relative","ironband family","darteus and bardin"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Prospector Ironband on?",a="Ironband serves Ironforge and the Alliance through the Dwarven Explorers' Guild. He answers to the guild's leaders and King Magni Bronzebeard, dedicating his efforts to uncovering ancestral titan lore and ancient artifacts across Khaz Modan to enrich the dwarven people.",al={"ironband faction","who does ironband work for","ironband alliance"},it="side",add="8f75b961"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can take pride in Prospector Ironband's work to understand dwarven ancestry, part of King Magni's effort to learn the people's past.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know the pickaxes and trenching used at Ironband's dig. A sharp eye can reveal worked stone and buried layers among the rock.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can help supply and defend Ironband's site, secure southeastern Loch Modan against trogg incursions, and preserve valuable relics for the Alliance."},kw={"agmond","darteus ironband","excavation progress report","excavation site","explorers guild","ironband","loch modan","prospector","protecting the shipment"},rel={"subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site","quest:436","quest:298","quest:309","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf"},src={"Prospector Ironband"}}
E["npc:thorgrum-borrelson"] = {t="npc",n="Thorgrum Borrelson",z="lochmodan",s="Above Thelsamar, Thorgrum Borrelson keeps travelers flying across Loch Modan. His roost links the valley with Ironforge and the nearby mountain passes.",h="Above Thelsamar, Thorgrum Borrelson keeps travelers flying across Loch Modan.",sec={{t="The Roost Above Thelsamar",b="Thorgrum Borrelson keeps the gryphon roost on the bluff above Thelsamar. His trained gryphons carry the Alliance across Loch Modan, where troggs and gnoll packs threaten the roads. They pass through South Gate Pass to the Great Forge in Dun Morogh, then fly onward toward the Wetlands and beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thorgrum Borrelson?",a="Thorgrum Borrelson oversees Alliance gryphon flights from Thelsamar, carrying travelers into and out of Loch Modan.",al={"thorgrum","thelsamar flight master","who is the gryphon master in thelsamar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Thorgrum send travelers?",a="Thorgrum can send travelers from Thelsamar to Ironforge, Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands, Farholde Keep in the Riverglades, and outposts in neighboring territories.",al={"thelsamar flight paths","where can i fly from loch modan"},gp=true},{q="Why is gryphon travel important in Loch Modan?",a="Troggs, gnolls, and Dark Iron scouts threaten Loch Modan's mountain passes. Gryphons let Alliance messengers, scouts, and adventurers cross the region quickly while avoiding those dangers.",al={"why fly in loch modan","loch modan transport"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Thorgrum Borrelson on?",a="Thorgrum is a loyal subject of Ironforge and serves the Alliance. As the local flight master stationed right above Thelsamar, he manages the aerial courier and transit network connecting the mountain kingdom's capital to its surrounding territories, ensuring Alliance messengers and travelers can traverse Khaz Modan swiftly.",al={"thorgrum borrelson faction","who does thorgrum serve","thorgrum alliance"},it="side",add="30011ebf"},{q="What does Thorgrum Borrelson want?",a="Thorgrum's primary concern is keeping the skies open and maintaining steady air links between Loch Modan and other Alliance strongholds. He tends to the roosted gryphons on the ridge above Thelsamar and sees to it that couriers, adventurers, and dispatches reach destinations like Ironforge without delay.",al={"what does thorgrum want","thorgrum borrelson goal","thorgrum duties"},it="wants",add="aebc9bb6"},{q="Why is Thorgrum Borrelson here?",a="Thorgrum is stationed on the bluffs overlooking Thelsamar because the town serves as the heart of Loch Modan. With ground travel through the mountain passes frequently threatened by troggs, kobolds, and hostile wildlife, having a dedicated gryphon roost ensures an unbroken connection between the valley settlement and the Great Forge.",al={"why is thorgrum in loch modan","why is thorgrum above thelsamar","thorgrum location purpose"},it="why_here",add="db7b8a65"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can count on Thorgrum Borrelson to keep an aerial route open to Ironforge's high halls.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can rely on Thorgrum's roost to link the dwarven realm with positions in the Wetlands and Arathi Highlands."},kw={"dun morogh","flight master","gryphon master","ironforge","loch modan","thelsamar","thorgrum borrelson"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","quest:6391","zone:ironforge","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:arathi","topic:dwarf"},src={"Thorgrum Borrelson"}}
E["npc:valstag-ironjaw"] = {t="npc",n="Valstag Ironjaw",z="lochmodan",s="At Menethil Keep, Valstag Ironjaw helps guard the road between Loch Modan and the coast. He warns the garrison of dangers to travelers and supplies.",h="At Menethil Keep, Valstag Ironjaw helps guard the road between Loch Modan and the coast.",sec={{t="Duty at the Keep",b="Valstag Ironjaw serves with the dwarven garrison inside Menethil Keep in Menethil Harbor. Dragonmaw orcs and ravenous wildlife threaten their communications and supplies. So he helps coordinate defenses on the main roads, especially the perilous way through Dun Algaz toward Loch Modan.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Pass",b="Hostile forces crowd the Algaz Gauntlet, putting travelers and supply convoys between Menethil Harbor and Loch Modan at risk. Valstag sends capable adventurers against the brigands and orcs in the passes. He also carries military reports between forward scouts and commanders such as Captain Stoutfist.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Valstag Ironjaw?",a="You can find Valstag Ironjaw inside Menethil Keep, the stone fortress in Menethil Harbor in the western Wetlands.",al={"valstag location","where is valstag ironjaw","valstag ironjaw npc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Valstag play in the Wetlands?",a="Valstag Ironjaw is an Ironforge dwarf at the keep. He helps defend the mountain roads leading back to the dwarven heartlands.",al={"what does valstag do","valstag role"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the pass to Loch Modan such a concern for him?",a="The Algaz Gauntlet links Menethil Harbor's coastal port to Loch Modan and Ironforge. Hostile forces there threaten food, troop movements and supplies.",al={"why algaz gauntlet","valstag loch modan"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Captain Stoutfist?",a="Captain Stoutfist is a senior officer in Menethil Keep. Valstag coordinates with him so military reports and security dispatches reach the garrison command.",al={"captain stoutfist connection","who is stoutfist"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Valstag Ironjaw?",a="Valstag Ironjaw is a stout dwarven defender stationed in Menethil Keep within the port town of Menethil Harbor. Serving the Alliance and his dwarven kin, he helps watch over the perilous trade routes and mountain passes connecting the coastal harbor of the Wetlands to the highlands of Loch Modan.",al={"who is valstag","valstag ironjaw lore","who is valstag ironjaw"},it="identity",add="bcb025ae"},{q="Whose side is Valstag Ironjaw on?",a="Valstag is loyal to Ironforge and the Grand Alliance. Stationed among the defenders of Menethil Harbor, he works in coordination with dwarven military authorities—such as Captain Stoutfist—to safeguard travelers and keep supply lines open against local threats.",al={"valstag ironjaw faction","who does valstag serve","is valstag alliance"},it="side",add="3e0052ae"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you rely on the route Valstag helps keep open between Menethil Harbor and the mountains of Khaz Modan, for trade and travel.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf traveling from Ironforge or Loch Modan, you find Valstag with the forward garrison guarding the western shoreline."},kw={"algaz gauntlet","captain stoutfist","loch modan","menethil harbor","menethil keep","valstag ironjaw","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-keep","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","quest:455","quest:473","npc:captain-stoutfist","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf"},src={"Valstag Ironjaw"}}
E["npc:vidra-hearthstove"] = {t="npc",n="Vidra Hearthstove",z="lochmodan",s="At Thelsamar’s Stoutlager Inn, Vidra Hearthstove cooks blood sausages with game from the surrounding wilderness.",h="At Thelsamar’s Stoutlager Inn, Vidra Hearthstove cooks blood sausages with game from the surrounding...",sec={{t="Kitchen of the Stoutlager",b="Vidra keeps the inn supplied for locals and travelers. Like the innkeeper, she bears the Hearthstove name. Her blood sausages call for fresh game: boar entrails, spider ichor, and bear meat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vidra Hearthstove?",a="Vidra Hearthstove cooks at the Stoutlager Inn, where she lives. Patrons and Mountaineers defending Loch Modan are served her renowned Thelsamar blood sausages.",al={"vidra hearthstove lore","who is vidra","stoutlager cook"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Vidra Hearthstove be found?",a="You can find Vidra inside the Stoutlager Inn, in the center of Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",al={"vidra location","where is vidra hearthstove","stoutlager inn vidra"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What ingredients does she use for Thelsamar Blood Sausages?",a="Vidra's famous recipe calls for bear meat, boar intestines, and spider ichor from wildlife in Loch Modan.",al={"blood sausage ingredients","what is in thelsamar blood sausages","vidra recipe"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Vidra Hearthstove on?",a="Vidra is a loyal dwarven citizen of Khaz Modan and firmly allied with the Alliance. Living and working right in the heart of Thelsamar, she cooks for the local community and welcomes weary travelers who make the trek through Loch Modan.",al={"vidra hearthstove faction","is vidra alliance","vidra hearthstove side"},it="side",add="5e429306"},{q="What does Vidra Hearthstove want?",a="Vidra is dedicated to her culinary craft and keeping the patrons of the Stoutlager Inn well fed. She seeks fresh, hearty ingredients from the wildlife roaming the loch—specifically meat and organs from local beasts—to prepare her famous Thelsamar Blood Sausages.",al={"vidra hearthstove motive","what does vidra want","vidra hearthstove recipe"},it="wants",add="e3ca8182"},{q="Why is Vidra Hearthstove here in Thelsamar?",a="Vidra makes her living inside the Stoutlager Inn, providing home-cooked meals for town residents, tradesfolk, and passing adventurers. With Thelsamar serving as the primary hub of Loch Modan, her kitchen is essential for keeping the local defenses and workers sustained.",al={"why is vidra in stoutlager inn","vidra hearthstove location why","why is vidra here"},it="why_here",add="8f91522d"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, Vidra turns harsh local ingredients into sustaining meals for hungry adventurers and mountain patrols. Her cooking follows the hearty, rustic tradition of Khaz Modan.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf passing through Thelsamar, you can find a comforting taste of home in Vidra's kitchen, where her cooking helps keep town morale high."},kw={"blood sausages","dwarf cook","hearthstove","loch modan","stoutlager inn","thelsamar","vidra hearthstove"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","subzone:stoutlager-inn","quest:418","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf"},src={"Vidra Hearthstove"}}
E["quest:1339"] = {t="quest",n="Mountaineer Stormpike's Task",z="lochmodan",s="At his post in Loch Modan, Mountaineer Stormpike needs a runner for urgent business beyond the valley. Mountaineer Kadrell sends you to find him, since Stormpike cannot leave his watch.",h="At his post in Loch Modan, Mountaineer Stormpike needs a runner for urgent business beyond the valley.",sec={{t="A Watchman in Need of a Runner",b="The northern guard tower is Stormpike’s post, and his watch keeps him from leaving Loch Modan. The Mountaineers are stretched thin by troggs and roaming wildlife. So Kadrell directs capable travelers to guards who cannot abandon their duties. Stormpike needs a messenger for business far beyond the region’s borders.",sp=0},{t="From Tower to Distant Roads",b="You find Stormpike atop the northern guard tower, looking out over the valley. He belongs to the prominent Stormpike clan and has affairs beyond Thelsamar’s frontier defenses. Carrying his message and supplies takes you across regional borders on his behalf. Your road leads from the loch onto the highways of Khaz Modan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Mountaineer Stormpike?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike watches from atop the northern guard tower in Loch Modan, overlooking the surrounding trails.",al={"stormpike location","where is stormpike","find stormpike tower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell patrols near Thelsamar in Loch Modan and directs you to Stormpike’s tower.",al={"who gives mountaineer stormpikes task","quest starter","kadrell location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Stormpike need an adventurer?",a="Stormpike cannot leave his post at the tower. His personal business lies far beyond Loch Modan, so he needs a traveler to carry his message.",al={"why need runner","stormpike problem","what does stormpike want"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after reporting to Stormpike?",a="Reporting to Stormpike completes this first step and opens his follow-up delivery, 'Stormpike's Order', which takes you to another territory.",al={"next quest","what comes after mountaineer stormpikes task","stormpike followup"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this related to the Stormpike Guard in Alterac?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike shares the name and blood of the Stormpike clan, known for the Stormpike Guard and its mining expeditions. His work here is a modest local errand.",al={"stormpike clan connection","alterac valley stormpike","is this the av stormpikes"},it="ties"},{q="Do Horde players have an equivalent quest here?",a="No. Loch Modan is dwarven territory aligned with the Alliance, and its Mountaineers attack Horde travelers on sight.",al={"horde version","can horde do this"},gp=true},{q="Why does Mountaineer Kadrell want this done?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell is simply acting as a watchful lookout and liaison for his fellow guards. Stationed along the road, he knows that Mountaineer Stormpike needs a capable runner for a distant assignment that on-duty guards cannot leave their posts to handle. Spotting an able traveler, Kadrell passes along word so Stormpike can find the help he requires.",al={"why does kadrell send you to stormpike","mountaineer kadrell motive","why talk to stormpike"},it="motive",add="d38a276d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may feel a natural duty to help a fellow dwarf of the famed Stormpike line and honor clan ties across Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help regional mountaineers carry dispatches that keep Ironforge's garrisons supplied and coordinated across the eastern territories."},kw={"guard tower","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineer kadrell","mountaineer stormpike","runner","stormpike's order","thelsamar"},rel={"quest:1338","npc:mountaineer-stormpike","npc:mountaineer-kadrell","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Mountaineer Kadrell",["end"]="Mountaineer Stormpike",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=1339},src={"Mountaineer Stormpike's Task"}}
E["quest:161"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="At Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII suspects sabotage and sends a powder sample north for examination. A courier must carry it through the Wetlands to demolition expert Ashlan Stonesmirk at Dun Modr.",h="At Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII suspects sabotage and sends a powder sample north for...",sec={{t="A Powder of Ill Intent",b="A suspicious barrel near the dam’s eastern ramp held a strange-smelling powder. Hinderweir had seen Dark Iron sappers nearby, and suspects the powder is a refined explosive meant to shatter dwarven masonry. The dam has no specialized equipment to test it. Before he can be certain, he needs a military demolitionist to examine the sample.",sp=0},{t="The Road North",b="The road runs through the Algaz Gate and down into the sodden lowlands of the Wetlands. Hostile wildlife, aggressive dragonkin, and Dark Iron infiltrators make the way dangerous. Hinderweir urges couriers to keep to the cobbled road to Dun Modr. The pillaged dwarven town stands at the southern approach to the Thandol Span, where an Ironforge regiment still keeps watch.",sp=0},{t="The Blast Expert of Dun Modr",b="At Dun Modr, Ashlan Stonesmirk is the regiment’s master of high explosives. Decades of concussive blasts have left him half-deaf. His keen eye and nose confirm the powder is a specialized demolition charge. Its presence points to an orchestrated plot against the heart of dwarven engineering.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the strange smelling powder?",a="The strange-smelling powder is an alchemical explosive charge collected near Stonewrought Dam. Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII suspects saboteurs mean to breach the dam walls with it.",al={"what is the powder","hinderweir powder","strange powder"},it="item"},{q="Why send the powder all the way to Dun Modr?",a="Dun Modr houses the Ironforge military contingent defending the Thandol Span, including Ashlan Stonesmirk. He is a veteran explosives expert with the technical knowledge to identify specialized blast compounds.",al={"why dun modr","why ashlan stonesmirk","why go to wetlands"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Ashlan Stonesmirk located?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk is stationed at Dun Modr’s military camp, in the far northern Wetlands just south of the Thandol Span.",al={"where is stonesmirk","find ashlan","stonesmirk location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Hinderweir warn to stick to the road?",a="Hinderweir warns couriers to stay on the road down from the Algaz Gate because hostile beasts, raptors, gnolls, and Dark Iron saboteurs roam the Wetlands. Travel away from the road is extremely dangerous.",al={"why stick to road","wetlands dangers","road to wetlands"},it="danger"},{q="Who is sabotaging the Stonewrought Dam?",a="The explosives belong to the Dark Iron dwarves, who seek to undermine Bronzebeard infrastructure and collapse Stonewrought Dam, drowning the valleys below.",al={"who made the powder","dam saboteurs","dark threat culprit"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Why is Ashlan Stonesmirk hard of hearing?",a="Frontline work as a military sapper and explosives specialist has left Ashlan with chronic ringing in his ears and severe hearing loss from blast concussions.",al={"stonesmirk deaf","why can't ashlan hear"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII want this done?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir is responsible for the integrity of the Stonewrought Dam, one of Khaz Modan's greatest engineering marvels. Suspecting that the strange powder discovered nearby is an explosive meant to sabotage the structure, he needs an expert analysis to understand the exact threat confronting the dam before disaster strikes.",al={"why does hinderweir need this","hinderweir motivation","why send the powder"},it="motive",add="4fa83212"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Stonewrought Dam is one of the crowning jewels of Bronzebeard engineering. A plot to shatter its masonry threatens the pride and safety of all Khaz Modan.",["profession:Engineering"]="Identifying high-grade explosive residues takes a sapper’s practiced eye. Even ordinary powders can reveal an enemy saboteur’s technical skill.",["faction:Alliance"]="The highway through Loch Modan and the Wetlands is a critical military lifeline between Ironforge and the northern Alliance holdings across the Thandol Span."},kw={"ashlan stonesmirk","dark threat looms","dun modr","explosive powder","hinderweir","stonewrought dam","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","npc:ashlan-stonesmirk","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","zone:lochmodan","quest:631"},m={start="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",["end"]="Ashlan Stonesmirk",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=161},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (3)"}}
E["quest:1655"] = {t="quest",n="Bailor's Ore Shipment",z="lochmodan",s="In Loch Modan, Bailor's Ore Shipment is bound for Jordan Stilwell's sanctified weapon. Mo'grosh ogres plundered the alloy on the road from the Wetlands.",h="In Loch Modan, Bailor's Ore Shipment is bound for Jordan Stilwell's sanctified weapon.",sec={{t="An Ambushed Caravan",b="Jordan Stilwell awaits ore refined by his old friend Bailor Stonehand, but the shipment never reaches Ironforge. As the caravan travels south from the Wetlands into Loch Modan, Mo'grosh ogres ambush it and slaughter its guards. One wounded guard reaches a camp, then dies soon after. The shipment is left in ogre territory.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Alloy",b="Bailor Stonehand camps in Loch Modan and sends paladins across the Loch toward the northeastern hills. The stolen crate of alloy lies abandoned among the Mo'grosh camps. Recovering it means entering hostile territory, and will let Bailor keep his agreement with Jordan Stilwell.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bailor Stonehand?",a="Bailor Stonehand is a dwarven artisan who works in Loch Modan and an old friend of Jordan Stilwell. He prepares and supplies the specialized alloy Jordan needs for his craft.",al={"bailor stonehand","who is bailor","bailor"},it="identity"},{q="Who stole Jordan's ore shipment?",a="Mo'grosh ogres ambushed the caravan on its journey from the Wetlands into Loch Modan. They killed its escorts and carried the cargo to their camps.",al={"who stole the ore","who took the shipment","ore thieves"},it="threat"},{q="Where did the ambush take place?",a="The caravan was ambushed along the mountain road from the Wetlands into Loch Modan, before it reached local settlements.",al={"ambush location","where was caravan attacked"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where are the Mo'grosh ogres located?",a="Mo'grosh ogres have fortified camps in the rugged hills northeast of the Loch, across the water from the western settlements.",al={"where are mogrosh","ogre camp location","where is shipment"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this shipment needed?",a="Jordan Stilwell needs the alloy to forge a holy weapon for paladins undertaking the Test of Righteousness.",al={"why need ore","what is shipment for","purpose of ore"},it="item"},{q="What happened to the caravan guards?",a="Nearly all the guards died in the ambush. The lone guard who reached help died a few days later, before a healer could save him.",al={"caravan guards","survivors of caravan"},it="history"},{q="Why does Bailor Stonehand want this done?",a="Bailor made a bargain with his old friend Jordan Stilwell to supply a special shipment of refined alloy. When the caravan carrying it out of the Wetlands was ambushed, Bailor lost the goods and the last surviving guard succumbed to his wounds. Bailor prides himself on honoring his deals, but with his transport destroyed and the ogres holding the alloy, he needs someone capable of recovering the stolen cargo so Jordan receives what was promised.",al={"why help bailor","bailor motive","why does bailor want the ore"},it="motive",add="f726d253"},{q="Who are the Mo'grosh ogres?",a="The Mo'grosh are a brutish clan of ogres who have pushed into the northeastern highlands of Loch Modan, carving out a stronghold known as the Mo'grosh Stronghold. Aggressive and opportunistic, they regularly raid mountain passes and trade routes connecting Loch Modan to the Wetlands, slaughtering travelers and pillaging supply wagons for raw goods, weapons, and food.",al={"mogrosh ogres","who took the ore","ogres in loch modan"},it="target",add="8c6c3897"},{q="Why does Bailor need an adventurer instead of the local guards?",a="The local dwarf guards and mountaineers are stretched thin holding back trogg uprisings and maintaining defensive perimeters across the Loch. The caravan guards assigned to escort Bailor's alloy were completely wiped out in the ambush, and the sole survivor died before relief could arrive. Bailor has neither the troops to spare nor the muscle to storm an ogre stronghold alone, leaving an able adventurer as his only recourse.",al={"why doesn't bailor send guards","why me bailor","why not ironforge guards"},it="why_me",add="6bcba9e0"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face dangerous brutes and recover materials for your sacred warhammer during the Test of Righteousness.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Bailor's custom alloy meets the exacting metalworking requirements Jordan Stilwell sets for his legendary armaments.",["faction:Alliance"]="Mo'grosh ogres in northeastern Loch Modan threaten supply lines and caravans passing through the Wetlands pass."},kw={"bailor","jordan stilwell","loch modan","mo'grosh","ogres","ore","shipment","stonehand","test of righteousness"},rel={"npc:bailor-stonehand","quest:1653","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Bailor Stonehand",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1655,ri={"Jordan's Ore Shipment"}},src={"Bailor's Ore Shipment"}}
E["quest:199"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="At the Stonewrought Dam, sabotage threatens the barrier that holds back Loch Modan's waters. You find a barrel near the shore and bring its strange smelling powder to Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII.",h="At the Stonewrought Dam, sabotage threatens the barrier that holds back Loch Modan's waters.",sec={{t="A Suspicious Discovery",b="Whispers of sabotage have reached the shore around the Stonewrought Dam. Near the water's edge, a barrel lies where it does not belong. Inside is strange, pungent powder, far from the dam's maintenance supplies.",sp=0},{t="Alarm at the Dam",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is alarmed when you bring him a sample. His reaction confirms Loch Modan's worst fears: an outside force is plotting against the dam. Now the inquiry is urgent, for the region's defense.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the strange smelling powder?",a="The strange smelling powder in the barrel is an explosive or alchemical agent planted near the Stonewrought Dam's base. It is evidence that an enemy plots to destroy or compromise the barrier.",al={"strange powder","what is in the barrel","suspicious barrel powder"},it="item"},{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is the dwarven master engineer responsible for the Stonewrought Dam's maintenance, integrity, and safety in Loch Modan.",al={"who is hinderweir","chief engineer hinderweir","dam engineer"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the suspicious barrel found?",a="The suspicious barrel is hidden along the shoreline near the Stonewrought Dam's foundation in northern Loch Modan.",al={"barrel location","where is the barrel","barrel loch modan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Stonewrought Dam being targeted?",a="The Stonewrought Dam holds back Loch Modan's vast reservoir. If it breaks, catastrophic flooding would tear through the Wetlands below, crippling Alliance trade routes and devastating dwarven holdings across Khaz Modan.",al={"why destroy the dam","dam sabotage","threat to loch modan"},it="threat"},{q="Who left the suspicious barrel here?",a="Agents seeking to destabilize dwarven lands placed the barrel. Chief Engineer Hinderweir has begun a broader investigation into who is behind the plot.",al={"who planted the barrel","saboteurs","who put the powder"},it="origin"},{q="What should I do after collecting the powder?",a="Take the sample to Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII atop the Stonewrought Dam so he can inspect it and prepare a response.",al={"what next","turn in powder","who to talk to"},it="next_step",gp=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Stonewrought Dam as one of the Ironforge dwarves' greatest architectural feats. Any threat to it endangers the safety and pride of Khaz Modan.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you appreciate the precision of dwarven civil works. That makes the chemical nature of this crude sabotage especially concerning.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you recognize the danger of volatile powders deliberately planted at the stress points of a major dam."},kw={"a dark threat looms","hinderweir","loch modan","sabotage","stonewrought dam","strange smelling powder","suspicious barrel"},rel={"quest:161","npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Suspicious Barrel",["end"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=199},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (2)"}}
E["quest:2038"] = {t="quest",n="Bingles' Missing Supplies",z="lochmodan",s="On Loch Modan’s southeastern shore, Bingles Blastenheimer is stranded after troggs steal his gear. You can recover his tools and Blastencapper explosives so he can repair his gyrocopter and return to the fight for Gnomeregan.",h="On Loch Modan’s southeastern shore, Bingles Blastenheimer is stranded after troggs steal his gear.",sec={{t="A Damp Descent",b="Bingles Blastenheimer crashes his gyrocopter into Loch Modan’s cold waters. He drags himself ashore, dazed, and troggs from the lake’s central islands swarm him. They steal his most valuable belongings.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Ingenuity Under Siege",b="Troggs scatter Bingles’ gear among their island camps. The stolen things include a wrench, screwdriver, and hammer, along with his volatile, high-yield invention, the Blastenheimer Blastencapper. Left among troggs, the explosives put travelers in immediate danger.",sp=0},{t="For Gnomeregan",b="Bingles fights to free Gnomeregan, his homeland, from subterranean troggs and irradiated leper gnomes. He imagines a decisive aerial assault, but without his tools and Blastencappers he cannot rebuild his flying machine. His campaign remains grounded in the reeds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Bingles Blastenheimer stranded in Loch Modan?",a="Bingles Blastenheimer is stranded in Loch Modan after crashing his gyrocopter. He struggles ashore on the southeastern bank, where troggs from nearby islands ambush him and steal his tools and experimental explosives.",al={"why is bingles here","how did bingles crash","bingles crash"},it="why_here"},{q="What supplies were stolen by the troggs?",a="The troggs steal Bingles’ wrench, screwdriver, hammer, and specialized explosive, the Blastenheimer Blastencapper.",al={"what did troggs steal","bingles supplies","what items bingles"},it="item"},{q="Where did the troggs take Bingles' gear?",a="The troggs take Bingles’ gear to their camps on islands in the northern part of the Loch. They scatter the tools and explosives along the rocky shores.",al={"where are bingles tools","trogg island location","where is blastencapper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Blastencapper?",a="The Blastenheimer Blastencapper is an explosive device Bingles designed for air strikes against the enemies occupying Gnomeregan.",al={"what is blastencapper","blastenheimer blastencapper","bingles explosive"},it="item"},{q="What movement is Bingles referring to?",a="Bingles refers to reclaiming Gnomeregan. He hopes to lead an aerial bombardment against the subterranean troggs and leper gnomes holding the gnomish capital.",al={"what movement","for gnomeregan","bingles cause"},it="purpose"},{q="Why can't Bingles retrieve the supplies himself?",a="Bingles cannot retrieve the supplies because he is alone and unarmed after the crash, and his gyrocopter is out of reach. Crossing open water to face aggressive troggs without weapons or aircraft would be suicide for a lone engineer.",al={"why doesnt bingles get them","why bingles waiting"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Bingles Blastenheimer want his supplies recovered?",a="Bingles crashed his flying machine into the Loch while testing it, but losing his equipment endangers more than just his salvage. He crafted specialized tools and proprietary Blastenheimer Blastencapper explosives specifically for the gnomish airborne offensive to reclaim Gnomeregan. Without his tools to rebuild and his ordnance to deliver, the effort to bomb the troggs and leper gnomes occupying his homeland cannot proceed.",al={"bingles motive","why does bingles need his tools","why help bingles"},it="motive",add="008fc445"},{q="Who took Bingles' supplies and why are they here?",a="Troggs infesting the islands of Loch Modan ambushed Bingles shortly after he crashed and scavenged his gear. These primitive subterranean brutes were unearthed during the dwarven excavations across Khaz Modan. Driven by violent territorial instinct and a knack for seizing shiny mechanical oddities, they hauled Bingles' toolkit and volatile explosives back to their lakeside encampments.",al={"who stole bingles tools","troggs loch modan bingles","why are troggs on the islands"},it="target",add="0d3e655b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, each tool you recover brings your people closer to an aerial counteroffensive against the troggs and leper gnomes suffocating Gnomeregan.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the troggs on the Loch’s islands threaten local trade and travel. Any blow against their camps helps the Mountaineers.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know specialized tools and volatile explosives like the Blastenheimer Blastencapper are dangerous in trogg hands and an affront to craftsmanship.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, helping a fellow pilot in Loch Modan secures the waterways and aids the wider effort to reclaim Khaz Modan’s lost territories."},kw={"bingles","blastencapper","blastenheimer","gnomeregan","gyrocopter","hammer","loch modan","screwdriver","the loch","trogg","wrench"},rel={"npc:bingles-blastenheimer","quest:2039","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","topic:trogg","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome","topic:leper-gnome"},m={start="Bingles Blastenheimer",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=2038,ri={"Bingles' Blastencapper","Bingles' Hammer","Bingles' Screwdriver","Bingles' Wrench"}},src={"Bingles' Missing Supplies"}}
E["quest:217"] = {t="quest",n="In Defense of the King's Lands",z="lochmodan",s="Captain Rugelfuss sends you into Stonesplinter Valley to stop the attacks on the King’s Lands. Scouts have traced them to Grawmug, chieftain of the Stonesplinter troggs. His death may break the pack’s resolve and help reclaim southern Loch Modan.",h="Captain Rugelfuss sends you into Stonesplinter Valley to stop the attacks on the King’s Lands.",sec={{t="Decapitating the Swarm",b="Captain Rugelfuss’s scouts have found that the Stonesplinter troggs follow Chieftain Grawmug. Their attacks threaten the King’s Lands in southern Loch Modan. You are sent into their lair to kill Grawmug and his personal bruisers. Breaking the pack’s cohesion may stop its advance.",sp=0},{t="Into Stonesplinter Lair",b="Grawmug holds a cavern in the southeastern cliffs of Stonesplinter Valley. His trusted brutes, Gnasher and Brawler, stand beside him, making the three a danger to a lone soldier. Defeating them could throw the remaining troggs into disarray. That would give the beleaguered Mountaineers time to fortify the roads and drive the beasts back underground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grawmug?",a="Grawmug is the trogg chieftain leading the Stonesplinter troggs in southern Loch Modan. Dwarven scouts traced the organized assaults troubling the valley to him. Gnasher and Brawler guard his side.",al={"grawmug lore","who is the trogg leader","chieftain grawmug"},it="target"},{q="Where are Grawmug and his guards located?",a="Grawmug, Gnasher, and Brawler are deep in a cave on the southeastern edge of Stonesplinter Valley in Loch Modan.",al={"grawmug location","where is grawmug","where to find grawmug"},gp=true},{q="Who is Captain Rugelfuss?",a="Captain Rugelfuss is the dwarven officer stationed at the Southern Guard Tower in Loch Modan. He oversees the defense against the trogg incursions and gives orders to protect the King’s Lands.",al={"rugelfuss","captain rugelfuss role","who gives defense of the kings lands"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why must Grawmug's guards be slain as well?",a="Gnasher and Brawler are Grawmug’s personal enforcers and stay at his side. They must be defeated with their leader to break the troggs’ command.",al={"why kill gnasher and brawler","gnasher and brawler","grawmug bodyguards"}},{q="What happens after Grawmug is eliminated?",a="Grawmug’s death could bring relief to Loch Modan. Without him to coordinate their raids, the Stonesplinter troggs may lose their organization. That would give the local dwarven militia a better chance to hold the borders and push the beasts underground.",al={"outcome of killing grawmug","troggs after grawmug dies","did we save loch modan"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are troggs invading Loch Modan?",a="Troggs have long lived in subterranean chambers beneath Khaz Modan. Excavations and unsealed caverns have let them reach the surface, where they displace settlements and attack travelers on the King’s roads.",al={"why are troggs here","trogg invasion loch modan","stonesplinter trogg origin"},it="history"},{q="Why does Captain Rugelfuss want Grawmug killed?",a="Captain Rugelfuss sees Grawmug as the mastermind driving the trogg incursions threatening Loch Modan. The dwarven garrisons have been struggling to hold back the subterranean swarms, and Rugelfuss believes that decapitating their leadership—specifically eliminating Grawmug alongside his elite bodyguards—will break their momentum and give the dwarves a fighting chance to drive them back underground.",al={"rugelfuss motive","why kill grawmug","purpose of in defense of the kings lands"},it="motive",add="440a3b53"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, driving troggs from Khaz Modan’s ancient soil defends your homeland and honors it. You help keep the mountain holds clear of subterranean scourges.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, defending Loch Modan helps preserve the overland connection between Ironforge and the eastern frontiers. It also helps keep supply lines secure for Alliance forces."},kw={"brawler","gnasher","grawmug","kings lands","loch modan","rugelfuss","stonesplinter","trogg"},rel={"npc:captain-rugelfuss","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","zone:lochmodan","topic:trogg","topic:alliance"},m={start="Captain Rugelfuss",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=217},src={"In Defense of the King's Lands (Classic 4)"}}
E["quest:224"] = {t="quest",n="In Defense of the King's Lands",z="lochmodan",s="At the southern watchtower, Mountaineer Cobbleflint calls for help as Stonesplinter troggs press toward the Valley of Kings. Ironforge’s forces serve on distant fronts.",h="At the southern watchtower, Mountaineer Cobbleflint calls for help as Stonesplinter troggs press toward the...",sec={{t="A Thin Line in the Valley of Kings",b="Cobbleflint and the guards are too few to stop the growing trogg invasion beneath the great dwarven monuments. King Magni Bronzebeard has sent much of his regular army abroad to support the Alliance. Local patrols and hired blades must keep the province from being overrun.",sp=0},{t="The Stonesplinter Incursion",b="Stonesplinter Valley cuts through Loch Modan’s southern peaks, where troggs have burrowed up from the depths. Their scouts reconnoiter the roads while warriors build camps along the valley floor. If left unchecked, their parties threaten the roads to the southern passes. The Mountaineers must fight them without pause.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the garrison in Loch Modan so undermanned?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard has sent much of Ironforge’s military to distant Alliance battlefields and outposts across Azeroth. Loch Modan and other home territories rely mainly on light Mountaineer patrols, which call on travelers to help hold back regional invasions.",al={"why so few guards","where are ironforge soldiers","why undermanned"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is Mountaineer Cobbleflint?",a="Mountaineer Cobbleflint is a dwarven sentry at the southern guard tower in the Valley of Kings. He coordinates security along Loch Modan’s southern boundary and directs attacks against the trogg tribes.",al={"cobbleflint","who gives quest","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Stonesplinter Valley located?",a="Stonesplinter Valley lies south of Thelsamar. Its entrance is near the main road, before the massive dwarven statues in the Valley of Kings, and the troggs keep several camps along its rocky floor.",al={"stonesplinter location","where are troggs","find stonesplinter valley"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What makes troggs such a severe threat to the dwarves?",a="Troggs tunnel through solid rock and can bypass surface walls and fortifications. They may burst up beneath roads, settlements, and mines, putting Ironforge’s security at risk.",al={"trogg threat","why fight troggs","are troggs dangerous"},it="threat"},{q="Who do I speak to after helping Cobbleflint?",a="After you thin the Stonesplinter troggs and scouts, Cobbleflint sends you to Mountaineer Gravelgaw. He is just inside the adjacent watchtower and manages the next patrol along the valley front.",al={"next quest","where to go after","gravelgaw"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Are the Stonesplinter troggs organized?",a="The Stonesplinter clan sends specialized scouts to reconnoiter the roads while foot soldiers hold defensive camps throughout the ravine.",al={"trogg scouts","are troggs smart","stonesplinter structure"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Mountaineer Cobbleflint want the troggs culled?",a="Mountaineer Cobbleflint views the trogg infestation as the single greatest threat facing Loch Modan and Ironforge itself. The creatures have been tunneling up from every crevice, threatening the Valley of Kings and surrounding lands. Because the regular dwarven army is deployed on distant battlefields, Cobbleflint must rely on bold volunteers to thin their swarming numbers before the local towers and settlements are entirely overwhelmed.",al={"why kill troggs","cobbleflint motive","why does cobbleflint need troggs killed"},it="motive",add="abec66b9"},{q="What are the Stonesplinter troggs doing in Loch Modan?",a="The Stonesplinter troggs are savage subterranean mutants who have tunneled up into the southern reaches of the Loch, establishing camps throughout Stonesplinter Valley. Their scouts continually probe dwarven territory, searching for weaknesses along the valley roads and near the southern guard tower. Left unchecked, their rapid emergence threatens to sever travel routes and overrun the region.",al={"who are the troggs","why are stonesplinter troggs here","stonesplinter troggs target"},it="target",add="515fdd78"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, answering Cobbleflint’s call helps defend King Magni’s ancestral valleys from subterranean pests while the army fights elsewhere.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, helping secure the Valley of Kings answers Ironforge’s call while dwarven troops serve on distant allied fronts.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can use the crags and outcroppings of Stonesplinter Valley to target trogg sentries and scouts from high ground."},kw={"cobbleflint","gravelgaw","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineer","stonesplinter","trogg","valley of kings"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:valley-of-kings","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","quest:217","topic:trogg","quest:267","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance"},m={start="Mountaineer Cobbleflint",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=224},src={"In Defense of the King's Lands (Classic)"}}
E["quest:237"] = {t="quest",n="In Defense of the King's Lands",z="lochmodan",s="In southern Loch Modan, Mountaineer Gravelgaw calls for help against the Stonesplinter troggs. With dwarven forces committed to the Alliance front, local outposts rely on volunteers to hold the line.",h="In southern Loch Modan, Mountaineer Gravelgaw calls for help against the Stonesplinter troggs.",sec={{t="A Thin Defense",b="The Mountaineers guarding the southern pass into Dun Morogh are stretched thin. King Magni Bronzebeard has sent much of Ironforge's strength to the wider Alliance front, leaving the Valley of Kings towers short of regular infantry. So Mountaineer Gravelgaw calls on volunteers to strike Stonesplinter Valley and keep the troggs at bay. Reinforcements may never come.",sp=0},{t="Stonesplinter Shamans and Brawlers",b="The Stonesplinter troggs are neither mindless nor aimless. Their war bands fight with brute force and crude elemental magic. Gravelgaw wants their veteran Skullthumpers and their Seers, who lead with mystic power, driven from the fight. Without those leaders, the tribe's southern camps lose their order and cannot mass against the Ironforge road.",sp=0},{t="Grim Tidings from the Front",b="When you report back, Gravelgaw has grim news. The promised dwarven reinforcements are not coming. Heavy losses on the distant Alliance front have drained Ironforge's reserves, leaving local Mountaineers and passing sellswords to defend Loch Modan.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Mountaineer Gravelgaw located?",a="Mountaineer Gravelgaw is at the southern guard tower along the road through the Valley of Kings. He guards the pass between Loch Modan and Dun Morogh.",al={"gravelgaw location","where is gravelgaw","turn in gravelgaw"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the dwarven Mountaineers so undermanned?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard has sent most of Ironforge's standing military to the wider Alliance front. As losses mount there, Loch Modan's border posts are left with skeleton crews and must rely on passing volunteers.",al={"why no dwarven guards","where are the reinforcements","ironforge army loch modan"},it="why_me"},{q="Where can the Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and Seers be found?",a="The Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and Seers gather mainly in the southern camps of Stonesplinter Valley, east of the Valley of Kings. Some also haunt the northernmost island in The Loch.",al={"stonesplinter skullthumper location","stonesplinter seer location","where are the troggs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why target Skullthumpers and Seers specifically?",a="Skullthumpers are the Stonesplinter tribe's shock troops, while Seers wield crude magic and direct the lesser troggs. Defeating both takes away the tribe's force and coordination.",al={"why kill seers","why skullthumpers","trogg targets"},it="target"},{q="Where does Gravelgaw send you next?",a="Gravelgaw sends you to Mountaineer Wallbang in the southern guard tower of the Valley of Kings, to help with the valley's defense.",al={"next quest gravelgaw","who is wallbang","after defense of the king's lands"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Mountaineer Gravelgaw want this done?",a="Mountaineer Gravelgaw is trying to buy precious time for Loch Modan's defenders. The Stonesplinter troggs are pressing relentlessly into the southern valley, while dwarven troops are desperately needed across distant Alliance battlefields. By thinning out the invading force, he hopes to keep the southern passes secure until reinforcements can arrive from Ironforge.",al={"why kill troggs","gravelgaw motive","in defense of the kings lands motive"},it="motive",add="c78d8208"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, defending the Valley of Kings is personal. It honors Ironforge's greatest rulers, and troggs defile that ground while your kin bleed on distant battlefields. It is a bitter pill to swallow.",["faction:Alliance"]="This mission shows the cost of the wider Alliance war. While its forces secure distant lands, the homelands of its own members are left vulnerable to local threats."},kw={"gravelgaw","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineer","seer","skullthumper","stonesplinter","troggs","valley of kings"},rel={"quest:217","quest:563","zone:lochmodan","subzone:valley-of-kings","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","subzone:the-loch","topic:trogg","topic:alliance"},m={start="Mountaineer Gravelgaw",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=237},src={"In Defense of the King's Lands (Classic 2)"}}
E["quest:250"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII fears Dark Iron sappers near the eastern ramp threaten the Stonewrought Dam. With much of its garrison sent to the Alliance Front, you investigate the danger.",h="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII fears Dark Iron sappers near the eastern ramp threaten the Stonewrought Dam.",sec={{t="A Vulnerable Wonder",b="The Stonewrought Dam holds back Loch Modan's waters. Ironforge engineers raised it as a great work, yet much of its security detail has gone to the Alliance Front. Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII and his small crew now have little protection if an attack comes.",sp=0},{t="Echoes from the North",b="Dark Iron dwarves struck the Thandol Span and pillaged Dun Modr in the Wetlands. Now known sappers lurk near the dam's eastern ramp. Hinderweir fears the clan has turned to Loch Modan's lifeline, and means to demolish it.",sp=0},{t="The Suspicious Cask",b="A suspicious barrel lies among the rocks where the sappers gathered. Inside is volatile powder with a strange smell. The barrel points to preparations to blast the Stonewrought Dam's foundation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Chief Engineer Hinderweir worried about the dam?",a="Dark Iron forces struck the Thandol Span and pillaged Dun Modr in the Wetlands. When Hinderweir saw their sappers near the Stonewrought Dam's eastern ramp, he feared the dam was their next target.",al={"why hinderweir worried","threat to stonewrought dam","why attack the dam"},it="motive"},{q="Where did the dam's garrison go?",a="Most of the Stonewrought Dam's security forces were reassigned to the Alliance Front. Hinderweir's top inspector went with them, leaving the dam thinly defended.",al={"why are there no guards at the dam","dam security detail","where are the soldiers"},it="why_me"},{q="What do you find at the eastern ramp?",a="Near the eastern ramp, you find a suspicious barrel filled with strange-smelling powder. Its presence confirms the Dark Irons are preparing to sabotage the dam.",al={"what is the clue","suspicious barrel clue","what are the sappers doing"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the strategic significance of the Stonewrought Dam?",a="The Stonewrought Dam controls Loch Modan's reservoir. If it breaks, the flood would devastate the Wetlands and drain the heart of dwarven territory.",al={"why destroy the dam","what happens if the dam breaks","dam lore"},it="place"},{q="What was the attack on Dun Modr mentioned by Hinderweir?",a="Dun Modr was a fortified dwarven outpost in the northern Wetlands, near the Thandol Span. Dark Iron infiltrators overwhelmed the town and struck the span, cutting important overland supply routes.",al={"dun modr attack","what happened at dun modr","thandol span destruction"},it="history"},{q="Who are the Dark Iron dwarves targeting Loch Modan?",a="The Dark Iron clan has long been bitter rivals of the Bronzebeard dwarves, ever since the War of the Three Hammers. From Blackrock Mountain and the Searing Gorge, they often sabotage Bronzebeard infrastructure and border defenses.",al={"who are the dark irons","dark iron sappers motive","why do dark irons hate ironforge"},it="threat"},{q="Why are Dark Iron sappers at the Stonewrought Dam?",a="Following their attacks on the Thandol Span and the town of Dun Modr to the north, Dark Iron dwarves have crept south into Loch Modan. Chief Engineer Hinderweir spotted their sappers sneaking around the eastern ramp of the Stonewrought Dam, suspecting they intend to sabotage the massive structure next.",al={"dark iron sappers dam","why are dark irons at the dam","dark iron sappers loch modan"},it="target",add="f99be494"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Stonewrought Dam as a masterwork of dwarven craft and pride. Dark Iron kin threaten it, and you defend your homeland.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see the dam's immense scale and the danger of sappers using volatile chemical explosives against its load-bearing foundations.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit, you help guard vital supply hubs and regional works while frontline armies are spread thin across the continent."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","hinderweir","loch modan","sappers","stonewrought dam","suspicious barrel","thandol span"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:lochmodan","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","quest:631","topic:alliance"},m={start="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",["end"]="Suspicious Barrel",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=250},src={"A Dark Threat Looms"}}
E["quest:255"] = {t="quest",n="Mercenaries",z="lochmodan",s="In Thelsamar, Magistrate Bluntnose hires passing fighters as Mo'grosh ogres press into northeastern Loch Modan. Ironforge has promised soldiers for the valley's defense, but they are months away. Settlements, excavations, and the Stonewrought Dam remain exposed.",h="In Thelsamar, Magistrate Bluntnose hires passing fighters as Mo'grosh ogres press into northeastern Loch...",sec={{t="Ironforge's Slow Wheels",b="Ironforge took two months to promise a handful of soldiers for Loch Modan's local defense. Another two months will pass before they arrive. Thelsamar's guards are stretched thin as hostile forces gather beyond the valley. Magistrate Bluntnose cannot wait for reinforcements.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in the Hills",b="Mo'grosh ogres have fortified a camp in the hills northeast of the loch. Their growing presence threatens Thelsamar, the Ironband Excavation Site, and the Stonewrought Dam. If the dam is attacked or damaged, destruction downstream would be catastrophic.\n\nWithout official mountaineer detachments, Bluntnose hires independent fighters to thin the ogre ranks. He hopes to buy the valley time against both ogres and troggs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Magistrate Bluntnose hiring mercenaries instead of using guards?",a="Ironforge has been slow to answer Loch Modan's pleas for help. Two months passed before the Senate approved sending even a handful of soldiers for the valley's defense, and another two months will pass before they arrive. With Thelsamar, the dam, and local dig sites facing immediate threats, Bluntnose hires independent fighters.",al={"why hire mercenaries","thelsamar guards","ironforge help"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are the Mo'grosh ogres located?",a="The Mo'grosh ogres are at the Mo'grosh Stronghold in the rugged bluffs and hills northeast of Loch Modan's great lake.",al={"ogre location","where are mogrosh","mogrosh camp"},gp=true},{q="Why is the Stonewrought Dam considered in danger?",a="The Stonewrought Dam regulates the entire lake and is an architectural jewel of the dwarves. It has almost no military defense, and a Mo'grosh camp lies nearby. Bluntnose fears an organized attack could damage or sabotage the structure and unleash catastrophic floods.",al={"why protect dam","ogres and the dam"},it="threat"},{q="What other threats does Thelsamar face alongside the ogres?",a="Troggs have erupted across the loch from underground ruins and excavations. Bluntnose sees them as a massive threat, but the nearby ogre stronghold forces him to hire fighters to push back the Mo'grosh. Then the local guard can focus on the trogg incursions.",al={"other threats loch modan","trogg threat"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Magistrate Bluntnose want the Mo'grosh ogres killed?",a="Magistrate Bluntnose fears for the survival of Thelsamar and the surrounding region. The Mo'grosh ogres have established a strong camp northeast of the lake, leaving the town, the local excavation site, and the Stonewrought Dam vulnerable to catastrophic assault while Ironforge delays sending defensive troops. By driving the ogres back, he hopes to remove an imminent menace and free up local attention to deal with the rampant trogg infestations.",al={"magistrate bluntnose motive","why kill mogrosh ogres","bluntnose why mercenaries"},it="motive",add="bfea2c9c"},{q="Who are the Mo'grosh ogres threatening Loch Modan?",a="The Mo'grosh are a brutish clan of ogres who have pushed into northeastern Loch Modan, claiming the rugged hills beyond the lake. Their enforcers and brutes project formidable physical might right next to vulnerable dwarven territory. Their growing presence poses an immediate physical threat to travelers, the Stonewrought Dam, and nearby dwarven settlements, taking advantage of the region's stretched defenses.",al={"who are the mogrosh","mogrosh ogres loch modan","what are the mogrosh ogres"},it="target",add="5f9f9ec0"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, the Stonewrought Dam is a crown jewel of dwarven engineering. Seeing it left unguarded because of Ironforge red tape makes Bluntnose's call to arms personal, whether you are a mountaineer or a traveler from the capital.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know Loch Modan is a vital corridor between Khaz Modan and the northern kingdoms. Ogre raids that throw it into chaos threaten Alliance supply lines across the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"loch modan","magistrate bluntnose","mercenaries","mo'grosh","ogre","stonewrought dam","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","zone:ironforge","topic:trogg","topic:light"},m={start="Magistrate Bluntnose",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=255},src={"Mercenaries"}}
E["quest:256"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Chok'sul",z="lochmodan",s="In northeastern Loch Modan, Chok'sul's ogres threaten the settlements and the works that sustain the valley. Magistrate Bluntnose wants the warlord dead before more lives are lost.",h="In northeastern Loch Modan, Chok'sul's ogres threaten the settlements and the works that sustain the valley.",sec={{t="A Threat to the Loch",b="Ogres now threaten northeastern Loch Modan, where troggs and wild beasts have long tested the valley's borders. They have made camps in the rugged hills and moved beyond simple scavenging. Local scouts and town authorities report raids that are focused, persistent, and dangerous.",sp=0},{t="The Price on Chok'sul's Head",b="Magistrate Bluntnose believes Chok'sul directs attacks on Thelsamar, a nearby dwarven excavation site, and the Stonewrought Dam. Fearing for civilian lives and the valley's great engineering work, he offers a bounty for the ogre chieftain's death by any means. Chok'sul's severed head is required as proof.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who posted the bounty on Chok'sul?",a="Magistrate Bluntnose, Thelsamar's chief civic official, posted the bounty on the town's behalf to protect the region from organized raids.",al={"who wants choksul dead","who posted choksul bounty","thelsamar wanted poster"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is Chok'sul considered such a high priority target?",a="Chok'sul is believed to direct ogre attacks on Thelsamar, the Ironforge archaeological excavations, and the Stonewrought Dam, putting dwarven lives and vital kingdom works at risk.",al={"why kill choksul","what did choksul do","choksul threat"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Chok'sul be found?",a="Chok'sul can be found in an ogre encampment among the rugged hills in Loch Modan's northeastern corner.",al={"choksul location","where is choksul","ogre camp loch modan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What proof does Magistrate Bluntnose require?",a="Magistrate Bluntnose requires Chok'sul's severed head as proof for the bounty and Ironforge's gratitude. Bring it directly to him in Thelsamar.",al={"choksul head","bounty proof","turn in choksul"},it="item"},{q="Why would ogres attack the Stonewrought Dam?",a="The Stonewrought Dam holds back Loch Modan's vast lake and is a great work of dwarven engineering. Sabotage could flood the wetlands and devastate dwarven supply lines, making it a valuable target for hostile forces.",al={"why attack the dam","stonewrought dam under attack"},it="threat"},{q="Are there other ogres working with Chok'sul?",a="Yes. Chok'sul commands an encampment of ogres in the northeastern hills and directs raids across the surrounding territory.",al={"choksul clan","loch modan ogres","choksul followers"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Chok'sul?",a="Chok'sul is an ogre brute who has taken charge of the ogre encampment in northeastern Loch Modan. Believed to be the cunning coordinator behind coordinated raids striking Thelsamar, the Stonewrought Dam, and the local dwarven excavation site, he poses the greatest organized threat to the valley's security.",al={"who is choksul","choksul target","about choksul"},it="target",add="761222eb"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see attacks on the Stonewrought Dam and nearby archaeological digs threaten your people's pride, heritage, and the security of Ironforge's lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you depend on Loch Modan as an agricultural and supply route into Dun Morogh. The safety of Thelsamar matters to Alliance military efforts.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know the Stonewrought Dam is among the greatest works of dwarven civil engineering. Letting ogres damage it is unthinkable."},kw={"bluntnose","bounty","chok'sul","choksul","loch modan","ogre","stonewrought dam","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:lochmodan","zone:ironforge"},m={start="WANTED",["end"]="Magistrate Bluntnose",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=256,ri={"Chok'sul's Head"}},src={"WANTED: Chok'sul"}}
E["quest:257"] = {t="quest",n="A Hunter's Boast",z="lochmodan",s="At Farstrider Lodge, Daryl the Youngling sets you a timed hunt in Loch Modan: bring down six mountain buzzards within fifteen minutes.",h="At Farstrider Lodge, Daryl the Youngling sets you a timed hunt in Loch Modan: bring down six mountain...",sec={{t="A Young Marksman's Arrogance",b="Daryl calls himself Daryl the Bold and dismisses travelers as greenhorns who cannot match his hunting skill. Then he points you toward the mountain buzzards scavenging around the lodge's nearby crags and hillsides.",sp=0},{t="Thinning the Scavengers",b="The hunt tests your speed, patience, and aim against the buzzards' quick flight. Bring down all six before time runs out, and Daryl grudgingly gives up one of his ranged weapons. He offers you further hunting dares, too.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this hunting challenge take place?",a="The challenge begins at Farstrider Lodge in southeastern Loch Modan. Mountain buzzards roam the nearby crags and open ridges across the zone.",al={"quest location","where is daryl","where are buzzards"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Daryl the Youngling?",a="Daryl the Youngling is a boastful young human staying at Farstrider Lodge. He calls himself Daryl the Bold and taunts travelers with timed hunts to prove his imagined superiority.",al={"who is daryl","daryl the bold lore","daryl farstrider"},it="identity"},{q="Why is there a time limit on the hunt?",a="The fifteen-minute limit is part of Daryl's wager. He believes an ordinary traveler cannot bring down wild buzzards under pressure.",al={"why 15 minutes","timer on quest","timed trial"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after beating Daryl's challenge?",a="Daryl is shocked when you succeed, but refuses to admit defeat. He honors his wager with a weapon, then offers another hunt, A Hunter's Challenge, for larger game.",al={"what comes next","boast followup","hunter chain"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why hunt mountain buzzards specifically?",a="Mountain buzzards gather around Loch Modan's rocky slopes. Their quick flight tests an archer's or rifleman's field discipline.",al={"why buzzards","buzzard purpose","loch modan buzzards"},it="target"},{q="Does this quest tie into the rest of Farstrider Lodge's tasks?",a="Daryl's hunts lead into a wider series for the lodge. It ends with a hunt for Ol' Sooty, the bear that scarred Daryl, as part of Vyrin Swiftwind's plan to get back at him.",al={"vyrin connection","lodge story","farstrider storyline"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Why does Daryl the Youngling challenge you to hunt buzzards?",a="Daryl thinks very highly of his own skills and wants to show off. Calling himself 'Daryl the Bold,' he looks down on travelers passing through Farstrider Lodge and expects you to fail. He stakes his own hunting weapon on a steep fifteen-minute wager simply to prove that an outsider cannot match his prowess.",al={"why does daryl want this done","daryl motive","why hunting challenge daryl"},it="motive",add="4c8cb4f1",nx={8}},{q="Why doesn't Daryl hunt the buzzards himself?",a="Daryl isn't asking for assistance or seeking to thin out the buzzards for protection; he is offering a boastful sporting wager. He considers the task beneath his own abilities and assumes an unproven adventurer cannot fell six birds within fifteen minutes, letting him boast when you inevitably come up short.",al={"why me daryl","why doesnt daryl hunt buzzards","why ask me daryl"},it="why_me",add="3b45bb0a"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can outshoot a boastful novice on his home ground and claim a reliable bow or gun.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the lodge's seasoned hunters and can answer this young human's empty bravado with quiet skill.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can take shelter at Farstrider Lodge, an outpost along Loch Modan's southeastern roads, and set out on hunts through the rugged valleys."},kw={"a hunter's boast","daryl the bold","daryl the youngling","farstrider lodge","hunting challenge","loch modan","mountain buzzards","timed quest"},rel={"npc:daryl-the-youngling","subzone:farstrider-lodge","quest:258","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Daryl the Youngling",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=257},src={"A Hunter's Boast"}}
E["quest:258"] = {t="quest",n="A Hunter's Challenge",z="lochmodan",s="At Farstrider Lodge, Daryl the Youngling dares you to kill five elder mountain boars within twelve minutes. He expects Loch Modan's rough highlands and dangerous wildlife to make you fail.",h="At Farstrider Lodge, Daryl the Youngling dares you to kill five elder mountain boars within twelve minutes.",sec={{t="A Youth's Boast",b="Daryl the Youngling lives among Farstrider Lodge's seasoned huntsmen, but he lacks their quiet patience. He covers his youth with bluster and long hunting tales, including rambling accounts of how he earned his “famous” scar. He refuses to admit that anyone else is skilled. He also keeps getting his fellow hunters' names wrong and sets strict trials for newcomers, hoping to humble them and restore his standing among the lodge's residents.",sp=0},{t="The Highland Hunt",b="Elder mountain boars roam Loch Modan's crags and hillsides. They are massive and thick-skinned, and grow dangerous when provoked. Daryl gives you twelve minutes to find and kill five. If you finish in time, the loudmouthed youngster retreats awkwardly and pretends he knows nothing of the extravagant wager he made so casually.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Daryl the Youngling?",a="Daryl is a young, boastful human huntsman at Farstrider Lodge in southeastern Loch Modan. Desperate to seem as formidable as the older veterans around him, he boasts of his skill, invents grand tales, and challenges passing adventurers to difficult hunts.",al={"who is daryl","daryl youngling lore","farstrider lodge daryl"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the elder mountain boars located?",a="Elder mountain boars roam the foothills, meadows, and ridges around Farstrider Lodge and across southern and eastern Loch Modan. They graze on the high ground between the lodge and the central loch.",al={"elder mountain boar location","where to find boars","boar hunt area"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this hunt timed?",a="Daryl gives you only twelve minutes because he expects you to fail. The deadline is tight, and he hopes it will embarrass you and prove your earlier hunting successes were beginner's luck.",al={"why twelve minutes","why is it timed","hunter challenge timer"}},{q="What bet did Daryl make?",a="Daryl wagers the shirt off his back if you kill five elder mountain boars in time. When you return victorious, he quickly pretends he cannot remember making the bet.",al={"daryl's bet","shirt off his back","what did daryl wager"},it="motive"},{q="How does this compare to Coldridge Valley boars?",a="The elder mountain boars of Loch Modan are tougher and more aggressive than the smaller boars novice dwarves hunt in Coldridge Valley. Their hides are thicker, and their tusks are dangerous, honed on highland granite.",al={"coldridge boars vs mountain boars","coldridge comparison"}},{q="Where does this hunting chain lead next?",a="After you finish Daryl's challenge and silence his boasting, attention at the lodge turns to more serious business: a confrontation with the dangerous elder bear Ol' Sooty in Vyrin's Revenge.",al={"what quest is next","after a hunters challenge","hunting questline"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What are the elder mountain boars?",a="Elder mountain boars are seasoned, tough beasts native to the crags and hills surrounding Loch Modan. Unlike the smaller boars wandering places like Coldridge Valley, these creatures are far hardier and more dangerous to corner. Daryl singles them out specifically to push your tracking and combat skills to their limit, expecting you to fail under a tight deadline.",al={"elder mountain boars loch modan","why elder boars","who are the boars"},it="target",add="4ae04a68"},{q="Why does Daryl send you on this hunt instead of hunting himself?",a="Daryl the Youngling prefers holding court at Farstrider Lodge, recounting grandiose tales of how he got his famous scar rather than trudging back into the wilderness. Convinced of his own superior skill, he issues these escalating trials purely to humble you and preserve his self-appointed prestige among the hunters.",al={"why daryl not hunt","why does daryl need me","why doesn't daryl hunt"},it="why_me",add="33153764"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking five elder mountain boars through the highland brush and dispatching them within a strict time limit tests your handling of the quarry.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf who came up through Coldridge Valley, you will recognize Daryl's comparison, though his patronizing manner may be harder to stomach.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to Farstrider Lodge as a staging ground for woodsmen guarding Loch Modan's eastern border from wild beasts and highland threats."},kw={"boar","coldridge","daryl","elder mountain boar","farstrider lodge","hunting","loch modan","youngling"},rel={"npc:daryl-the-youngling","subzone:farstrider-lodge","quest:257","zone:lochmodan","subzone:coldridge-valley"},m={start="Daryl the Youngling",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=258},src={"A Hunter's Challenge"}}
E["quest:263"] = {t="quest",n="In Defense of the King's Lands",z="lochmodan",s="At the Southern Guard Tower, Mountaineer Wallbang calls travelers to defend Loch Modan from the Stonesplinter troggs. With Ironforge's reserves sent to distant fronts, the southern pass is thinly held. Wallbang sends seasoned recruits into Stonesplinter Valley against the clan's shamans and bonesnappers.",h="At the Southern Guard Tower, Mountaineer Wallbang calls travelers to defend Loch Modan from the Stonesplinter...",sec={{t="A Thin Dwarven Line",b="Loch Modan's defenses are stretched thin. Ironforge's regular reserves have been summoned to distant fronts across Azeroth, leaving the Southern Guard Tower short-handed. Mountaineer Wallbang and his few comrades face constant pressure from the Stonesplinter clan. They depend on Alliance travelers passing through to help hold the southern pass.",sp=0},{t="Targeting the Stonesplinter Vanguard",b="The fight reaches beyond stray scouts to the Stonesplinter clan's strength. Its bonesnappers bring brutal force, while its shamans use earthen magic to rally their kin. Slaying twenty of these foes weakens the clan's incursions into the lowlands. It also serves King Magni Bronzebeard's defense of the realm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mountaineer Wallbang?",a="Mountaineer Wallbang is an Ironforge dwarf stationed at the Southern Guard Tower in Loch Modan. He watches for troggs spilling out of the mountains and coordinates the militia to keep the main southern road secure.",al={"wallbang","who is wallbang","mountaineer wallbang lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Mountaineers asking travelers for help?",a="Ironforge's military reserves have been called away to battlefronts across the kingdom and beyond. Border outposts such as Loch Modan's southern watchtowers are badly undermanned against local threats.",al={"why do dwarves need help","where are ironforge guards","why no reserves"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are these troggs located?",a="The Stonesplinter troggs gather in Stonesplinter Valley, in the rugged hills southwest of The Loch. Smaller bands of shamans and bonesnappers also haunt the northern islands in the lake.",al={"where are stonesplinter troggs","stonesplinter shaman location","where is stonesplinter valley"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What makes the Stonesplinter clan a threat?",a="Troggs multiply rapidly and can overrun settled lands in subterranean swarms. Stonesplinter shamans wield crude elemental magic, while bonesnappers attack dwarven scouts. Nearby settlements and trade paths are at risk.",al={"why are troggs dangerous","stonesplinter threat"},it="threat"},{q="What does Mountaineer Wallbang do after this task?",a="Wallbang is satisfied that you have proved yourself a fighter in King Magni's service. He sends you to report to Captain Rugelfuss for further orders in Loch Modan's defense.",al={"what next after wallbang","who is the captain"},it="next_step"},{q="Who rules Ironforge during this crisis?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard rules the dwarven kingdom from the High Seat in Ironforge. Efforts to safeguard Loch Modan are made in his name and to defend his lands.",al={"who is the dwarven king","king of ironforge"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Mountaineer Wallbang want these troggs killed?",a="The trogg problem across Loch Modan continues to worsen, threatening the security of Ironforge's sovereign territory. With the Mountaineer reserves called away to distant fronts, Wallbang and his comrades at the southern guard tower are stranded without reinforcements. He needs the trogg ranks culled to protect the valley and hold the line in the King's name.",al={"why kill stonesplinter troggs","wallbang motive","why does wallbang want troggs dead"},it="motive",add="20cd043f"},{q="Who are the Stonesplinter Shaman and Bonesnappers?",a="They are the specialized vanguards of the Stonesplinter trogg clan encroaching on Loch Modan. The Bonesnappers serve as the clan's brutal, heavy-hitting enforcers, while their Shaman channel raw, primal magics. Together, they form the core strength driving the troggs out of the depths and into dwarven lands.",al={"stonesplinter shaman","stonesplinter bonesnapper","who are the trogg targets"},it="target",add="c0ccff20"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, answering Wallbang's call means defending Loch Modan's homesteads while your kin's standing armies are sent abroad.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, helping the Southern Guard Tower protects vital trade and travel routes linking Dun Morogh to the eastern wetlands and Stormwind.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, facing the Stonesplinter trogg spellcasters shows you crude earth magic shaped by savage instincts."},kw={"bonesnapper","ironforge","loch modan","magni","mountaineer","shaman","stonesplinter","trogg","wallbang"},rel={"quest:217","zone:lochmodan","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","topic:trogg","zone:ironforge","subzone:the-loch","topic:alliance"},m={start="Mountaineer Wallbang",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=263},src={"In Defense of the King's Lands (Classic 3)"}}
E["quest:267"] = {t="quest",n="The Trogg Threat",z="lochmodan",s="At Loch Modan’s Southern Gate, Captain Rugelfuss faces a growing trogg threat with too few defenders. The Ironforge Reserve has been called away to Alliance battlefronts, leaving him to hold the pass while troggs threaten the nearby hills.",h="At Loch Modan’s Southern Gate, Captain Rugelfuss faces a growing trogg threat with too few defenders.",sec={{t="A Depleted Frontier",b="Dwarven mountaineers and the Ironforge Reserve have gone to reinforce Alliance battlefronts. Captain Rugelfuss now has only a small garrison. Strict orders keep him at the gate, unable to lead an attack into the highlands. Settlers and travelers there remain exposed to ambushes.",sp=0},{t="Stemming the Tide",b="Troggs in the nearby crags threaten Khaz Modan. Left unchecked, their numbers grow quickly, and they could overrun dwarven outposts. Rugelfuss calls for help to buy time and thin their ranks. Strike at the troggs in their hillside warrens, then bring back their stone teeth as proof.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Rugelfuss?",a="Captain Rugelfuss is a dwarven military officer in the guard tower at Loch Modan’s Southern Gate. With only a small garrison, he must secure the pass against intruders.",al={"captain rugelfuss","who gives the trogg threat","rugelfuss"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Southern Gate understaffed?",a="The Ironforge Reserve has been sent to fight on distant Alliance battlefronts. Only a small force remains at the gate, bound to its defensive post and unable to strike back.",al={"why are there no guards","ironforge reserve absent","where are the dwarven soldiers"},it="why_me"},{q="What are Trogg Stone Teeth?",a="Trogg Stone Teeth are the troggs’ naturally petrified, stone-like teeth, a mark of their subterranean, earthen heritage. Rugelfuss requires them as proof that troggs have been slain.",al={"trogg stone tooth","stone teeth","why trogg teeth"},it="item"},{q="Where are the troggs located?",a="Troggs live in the rocky hills, ravines and excavation sites beside the road near Loch Modan’s Southern Gate.",al={"where to find troggs","trogg locations loch modan","where are troggs for this quest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the troggs such a threat right now?",a="Troggs multiply quickly and attack fiercely to defend their territory. With troops diverted, they can overrun inhabited lands and threaten the passes linking Loch Modan to neighboring territories.",al={"why are troggs dangerous","trogg problem","what do troggs want"},it="threat"},{q="How does completing this quest aid King Magni Bronzebeard?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard is responsible for the safety of all Khaz Modan. Thinning the troggs while Ironforge’s armies fight abroad helps protect internal supply lines and vulnerable frontier settlements.",al={"magni bronzebeard connection","does magni care","why help ironforge"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Captain Rugelfuss want this done?",a="With the Ironforge Reserve deployed to the Alliance front, Captain Rugelfuss lacks the manpower to secure the region. His regiment is pinned down holding the southern guard tower against potential invasion. If the troggs gathering in the nearby hills are left unchecked, they could easily overwhelm the outpost and overrun Loch Modan.",al={"rugelfuss motive","why fight troggs","captain rugelfuss purpose"},it="motive",add="5b5ee45d"},{q="Why are the troggs infesting the hills near the Southern Gate?",a="The troggs have surfaced throughout dwarven lands, encroaching aggressively onto settlements and travel routes. Finding the surrounding crags ripe for invasion, they prowl the ridges near the Southern Gate, waiting to strike at vulnerable defenses left depleted by the ongoing troop shortages.",al={"who are the troggs","trogg targets","why are troggs here"},it="target",add="ba878bae"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, thinning the troggs near the Southern Gate is a direct duty to Khaz Modan. King Magni Bronzebeard himself will praise you for it.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how commitments in distant lands have left local garrisons like Loch Modan without their defensive reserves."},kw={"captain rugelfuss","ironforge reserve","khaz modan","loch modan","magni bronzebeard","southern gate","trogg","trogg stone tooth"},rel={"npc:captain-rugelfuss","topic:trogg","zone:lochmodan","npc:magni-bronzebeard","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance"},m={start="Captain Rugelfuss",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=267,ri={"Trogg Stone Tooth"}},src={"The Trogg Threat (Classic)"}}
E["quest:273"] = {t="quest",n="Resupplying the Excavation",z="lochmodan",s="Jern Hornhelm sends you from Thelsamar after a slow wagon carrying blastpowder to Ironband's Excavation Site. Its three dwarven haulers travel south along the Loch's shore.",h="Jern Hornhelm sends you from Thelsamar after a slow wagon carrying blastpowder to Ironband's Excavation Site.",sec={{t="A Heavy Cargo along the Shore",b="In southern Loch Modan, Ironband's Excavation Site needs blastpowder to break through hard rock. The powder comes first to Thelsamar, where Jern Hornhelm arranges for Huldar, Miran, and Saean to haul three volatile barrels south. The heavy load slows their pack team along the lakeside road, giving you time to catch them and help on the way.",sp=0},{t="Treachery in the Shadows",b="Huldar's wagon lies ambushed on the southern road. Dark Iron dwarves attacked to sabotage the Bronzebeard expedition's archaeological work. Saean had worked beside Huldar for nearly a year, yet helped arrange the ambush as a Dark Iron sympathizer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Resupplying the Excavation?",a="Jern Hornhelm sends you from Thelsamar after you bring him the blastpowder. He asks you to follow the road south along the Loch and catch up with the supply team.",al={"who gives resupplying the excavation","quest starter resupplying the excavation","where to start resupplying the excavation"},gp=true},{q="Where can Huldar and the wagon be found?",a="Huldar and the wagon are south of Thelsamar, along the road following the Loch's western and southern shores toward Ironband's Excavation Site.",al={"find huldar","huldar location","where is the wagon loch modan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is blastpowder being sent to Ironband?",a="Prospector Ironband and his team dig for ancient relics at the southern excavation site. They need blastpowder to break heavy stone and blast through underground layers.",al={"why ironband needs powder","ironband blastpowder","why blastpowder to excavation"},it="purpose"},{q="Who ambushed Huldar's wagon?",a="Jern expects Huldar's team on the usual road south of Thelsamar, following the Loch. You learn who attacked the wagon when you reach Huldar.",al={"who attacked the wagon","wagon ambush loch modan","who attacked huldar"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="What role did Saean play in the attack?",a="Saean travels with Huldar and Miran to carry the heavy blastpowder barrels. You learn his part in the attack when you catch up with the team.",al={"who is saean","saean betrayal","what did saean do"},sp=1},{q="What quest comes next after finding Huldar?",a="Speaking with Huldar completes this part of the journey. His account of the shipment points you toward what comes next.",al={"next quest after resupplying the excavation","quest after huldar"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Jern Hornhelm send you after Huldar?",a="Jern Hornhelm realizes you arrived to deliver blastpowder just after Huldar and his crew set off with the heavy wagon toward Ironband's Excavation. Because the wagon is heavily weighed down with barrels, Jern knows they will be traveling slowly along the southern road hugging the Loch. He sends you ahead to catch up with them so you can lend a hand with the vital shipment.",al={"jern hornhelm motive","why catch up to huldar","why does jern send you"},it="motive",add="72005fbc"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a Bronzebeard dwarf, you help keep Ironband's work supplied by protecting the blastpowder shipment on Loch Modan's dangerous roads.",["profession:Mining"]="You know the danger of moving volatile blasting powder over rough ground. The shipment is vital to the excavators in the south."},kw={"blastpowder","huldar","ironband","jern hornhelm","loch modan","miran","resupplying the excavation","saean","thelsamar"},rel={"npc:jern-hornhelm","npc:huldar","quest:454","quest:302","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Jern Hornhelm",["end"]="Huldar",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=273},src={"Resupplying the Excavation (Classic)"}}
E["quest:278"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="Dark Iron explosives threaten the Stonewrought Dam, and Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII needs your help. He asks you to gather rare reagents from Loch Modan so he can make a mixture to neutralize them.",h="Dark Iron explosives threaten the Stonewrought Dam, and Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII needs your help.",sec={{t="A Volatile Recipe",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII needs three ingredients for his mixture. Forest Lurker venom, a tear from a crocolisk in the Loch, and a Mo'grosh crystal each bring a different reaction. Together, they can render the dwarven charges inert.",sp=0},{t="Perilous Gathering",b="The ingredients lie in dangerous parts of Loch Modan. Forest Lurker spiders and crocolisks threaten travelers, while Mo'grosh ogres guard their mined crystals in a stronghold to the northeast. Reaching the crystals means facing the ogres in their encampments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Engineer Hinderweir need these specific reagents?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII needs the reagents to make a compound that can defuse Dark Iron explosives. Lurker venom, crocolisk secretions, and Mo'grosh crystals provide the reactions needed to render the saboteurs' charges inert.",al={"why spider venom","why crocolisk tear","defusing mixture reagents"},it="item"},{q="Where do Mo'grosh crystals come from?",a="Mo'grosh ogres mine and hoard the crystals in the northeastern hills of Loch Modan. Reaching one means entering their heavily defended territory.",al={"where are crystals","mogrosh crystal location","who has the crystal"},it="origin"},{q="What is the dark threat menacing Loch Modan?",a="Dark Iron dwarf infiltrators seek to destroy the Stonewrought Dam. Its destruction would flood the Wetlands below, cut Alliance supply lines, and devastate the region.",al={"what dark threat","who is attacking the dam","dark threat looms story"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is the dwarven engineer who oversees the Stonewrought Dam's operations and integrity. He directs its maintenance and local defenses against sabotage.",al={"who is hinderweir","chief engineer hinderweir"},it="identity"},{q="Where can the indigenous creatures be found?",a="Forest Lurker spiders roam the wooded wilderness around the valley. Crocolisks live in and around the Loch's shores.",al={"where are lurkers","crocolisk location","where to find spiders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why don't the Ironforge guards gather these items themselves?",a="Mountaineers and local guards are stretched thin defending towns like Thelsamar and watching for Dark Iron scouts. Specialized searches and forays into ogre territory fall to capable travelers.",al={"why help hinderweir","where are ironforge guards"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII want these items collected?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII fears an imminent Dark Iron dwarf assault on the Stonewrought Dam. To counter any demolition efforts, he needs you to gather volatile and specialized reagents—Lurker Venom, a Crocolisk Tear, and a rare Mo'grosh Crystal—so he can brew a neutralizing mixture to defuse the enemy's explosives before Loch Modan is devastated.",al={"why does hinderweir want this done","why collect reagents hinderweir","hinderweir motive dark threat"},it="motive",add="0370975a"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate Hinderweir's ingenuity in making a chemical counter-agent to stabilize volatile demolition charges in the field.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Khaz Modan, you have a vital duty to stop Dark Iron sabotage at the Stonewrought Dam and protect your ancestral lands and their great works.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know the dam's destruction would sever critical overland supply routes between Ironforge and the northern kingdoms."},kw={"crocolisk tear","dark iron","hinderweir","loch modan","lurker venom","mo'grosh crystal","stonewrought dam"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch"},m={start="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=278,ri={"Crocolisk Tear (Classic)","Lurker Venom","Mo'grosh Crystal"}},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (5)"}}
E["quest:280"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="Dark Iron saboteurs threaten the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan. Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII needs the charge disarmed before the loch floods the lowlands.",h="Dark Iron saboteurs threaten the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Sabotage Beneath the Surface",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII saw Dark Iron Insurgents swim toward the Stonewrought Dam with a keg of explosive Seaforium. No Mountaineers were nearby to stop them. The infiltrators fastened the keg against the dam’s underwater foundation. If the dam breaks, the loch will flood the lowlands and cripple dwarven trade and travel.",sp=0},{t="A Volatile Neutralizer",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII has mixed reactive ingredients into a disarming solution and sends a diver to the submerged keg. The diver must unscrew it and stir the solution into the explosive powder. The mixture halts the countdown with a faint fizz underwater, stabilizing the charge before it can tear through the dam.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this quest?",a="You dive beneath Loch Modan to the Stonewrought Dam’s foundation. There, you find the planted keg of Seaforium and stir in Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII’s mixture to stop the blast.",al={"quest objective","what do i do here","a dark threat looms 6 goal"},it="purpose"},{q="Who planted the explosive keg?",a="Dark Iron Insurgents planted the keg. They slipped into Loch Modan’s waters earlier in the day while local Mountaineers were absent, then fastened the charge against the dam’s underwater face.",al={"who put the bomb here","who planted seaforium","dark threat looms culprits"},it="threat"},{q="What happens if the dam is destroyed?",a="The Stonewrought Dam holds back Loch Modan. If it shatters, the water will flood the Wetlands and nearby valleys, washing away roads, towns, and lives.",al={"why save the dam","what happens if the bomb goes off","dam explosion stakes"},it="conflict"},{q="Who concocted the disarming mixture?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII made the chemical neutralizer from gathered reagents. It can neutralize the Seaforium without triggering an accidental blast.",al={"who made the mixture","hinderweir role","who made the chemical"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the explosive keg located?",a="The keg rests underwater against the Stonewrought Dam’s deep base, on its southern, lake-facing side.",al={"where is the bomb","keg location","powder keg underwater"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of explosive was used?",a="The saboteurs used Seaforium, a volatile demolition compound packed into a sealed, waterproof keg.",al={"what is the bomb made of","bomb type","what explosive"},it="item"},{q="Why does Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII want this done?",a="As the chief engineer overseeing the Stonewrought Dam, Hinderweir takes personal responsibility for its structural integrity. Dark Iron insurgents have planted a potent Seaforium explosive right at the foundation. If the dam breaches, the catastrophic deluge from the Loch would drown the valleys below and destroy one of the greatest architectural wonders of the dwarven people.",al={"why does hinderweir care","hinderweir motivation","why stop the explosion"},it="motive",add="8859d649"},{q="Why does Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII need you instead of the Mountaineers?",a="When the Dark Iron saboteurs made their approach, no Mountaineers were nearby to intercept them, and time is desperately short. The charge could detonate at any moment, and Hinderweir had to stay behind to urgently brew the disarming mixture from raw components. You are the only capable hand present who can plunge underwater and neutralize the explosive immediately.",al={"why cant the guards do this","why me hinderweir","where are the mountaineers"},it="why_me",add="34eba16d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Stonewrought Dam as a monument to dwarven skill and pride. Protecting it from Dark Iron treachery matters to Ironforge.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can grasp the chemistry of Hinderweir’s neutralizer and the devastation a Seaforium breach could bring to dwarven engineering.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how Seaforium and disarming chemicals bring demolitions and counter-explosive chemistry to their most dangerous edge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know the Stonewrought Dam protects vital routes linking Khaz Modan with the northern Alliance territories."},kw={"dam","dark iron","disarming","explosive","hinderweir","insurgents","keg","seaforium","stonewrought"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",["end"]="Explosive Charge",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=280},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (6)"}}
E["quest:283"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII needs you at Stonewrought Dam, where Dark Iron saboteurs have planted a charge. Disarm it before the valley below is in danger.",h="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII needs you at Stonewrought Dam, where Dark Iron saboteurs have planted a charge.",sec={{t="Averted Catastrophe",b="The Stonewrought Dam holds back the waters of the Loch above the lowlands of the Wetlands. Dark Iron saboteurs have planted an explosive charge inside it, putting the valley below at risk. You apply the Disarming Mixture, and the volatile keg fizzles harmlessly. The immediate danger to the dam and the lives downstream has passed.",sp=0},{t="Hinderweir's Relief",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII welcomes your report with relief. He calls your intervention a victory for the Kingdom of Ironforge and the Alliance. Dark Iron infiltrators have reached deep into Khaz Modan, and their bitter cousins remain determined to ruin Ironforge's achievements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was the goal of this quest chain?",a="The chain seeks to uncover and stop a Dark Iron dwarf plot to detonate explosives and destroy the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"a dark threat looms summary","stonewrought dam quest goal","why defuse bomb"},it="purpose"},{q="Who planted the explosive charge?",a="Dark Iron dwarven saboteurs planted the explosive keg inside the Stonewrought Dam to destroy it.",al={"who put the bomb here","who attacked the dam","dark irons dam"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is the dwarven overseer responsible for the Stonewrought Dam's maintenance, operation, and defense in Loch Modan.",al={"who is hinderweir","hinderweir lore","engineer at the dam"},it="in_charge"},{q="What would have happened if the dam broke?",a="If the Stonewrought Dam broke, Loch Modan's reservoir would drain violently and flood the Wetlands downstream, washing away roads, settlements, and vital transit routes.",al={"what if dam destroyed","consequences of dam breaking","dam explosion"},it="danger"},{q="How was the explosive disarmed?",a="You pour a specially concocted Disarming Mixture over the explosive charge, and the powder keg fizzles out safely before it can detonate.",al={"how was bomb stopped","disarming mixture","how do you defuse the charge"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Is the Stonewrought Dam safe now?",a="The immediate detonation has been prevented and the dam saved. Hinderweir says its defense is secure only for the time being, as Dark Iron agents continue to menace the region.",al={"is the dam secure","are the dark irons gone","dam safe forever"},sp=1,it="today"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can take pride in the Stonewrought Dam, a great work of dwarven stonecraft. Protecting it preserves Ironforge's pride against Dark Iron malice.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know the importance of countermeasures and explosive theory when neutralizing an unstable demolition device inside a colossal civil project.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help preserve key land corridors between Ironforge and the northern lands of Arathi and Lordaeron."},kw={"dark iron","disarming mixture","explosive charge","hinderweir","loch modan","sabotage","stonewrought dam"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:lochmodan","topic:alliance"},m={start="Explosive Charge",["end"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=283},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (7)"}}
E["quest:298"] = {t="quest",n="Excavation Progress Report",z="lochmodan",s="At Ironband's Excavation Site, Prospector Ironband needs you to carry his dispatches and powder orders to Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar.",h="At Ironband's Excavation Site, Prospector Ironband needs you to carry his dispatches and powder orders to...",sec={{t="A Dispatch to Thelsamar",b="Ironband's dispatches tell of his dig and renew its supply requests. The work needs picks, workers, and blasting powder to break through bedrock. Ironband relies on runners to keep Jern Hornhelm informed.",sp=0},{t="Missing Munitions",b="The dispatch reveals that aggressive troggs are harassing the dig. Powder could break stone or blast troggs. Yet Ironband's renewed request gives Jern Hornhelm pause: he sent a large shipment weeks ago, and wonders what happened to it along the rugged mountain paths.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this report to you?",a="Prospector Ironband gives you the report at Ironband's Excavation Site in Loch Modan's southeastern hills. He supervises the archaeological dig there.",al={"quest giver","who starts excavation progress report","ironband location"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Jern Hornhelm?",a="Jern Hornhelm is a dwarven Explorers' League contact in Thelsamar. He coordinates supplies and local logistics for archaeological expeditions across Loch Modan.",al={"where is jern hornhelm","who is the recipient","thelsamar contact"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Prospector Ironband need more blastpowder?",a="Ironband needs blastpowder to clear solid rock for his excavation. The dig site is also swarming with hostile troggs, so explosives matter for defense as well.",al={"why blastpowder","what does ironband want powder for"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to the previous shipment of powder?",a="Jern Hornhelm sent blastpowder weeks ago, but it never reached the excavation. Its disappearance points to trouble along the routes between Thelsamar and the outlying sites.",al={"where did the powder go","missing blastpowder"}},{q="What follows after delivering the progress report?",a="After reviewing Ironband's situation and the missing powder, Hornhelm sends you to report the expedition's status to his superiors in Ironforge.",al={"next quest","what comes after","report to ironforge"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are troggs attacking the excavation site?",a="Dwarven excavations can uncover underground chambers and disturb trogg dens. Troggs see miners as intruders and swarm those digging into the earth.",al={"trogg attack reason","why troggs hate ironband"},it="hostile"},{q="Why does Prospector Ironband need you to deliver the report?",a="Prospector Ironband and his fellow excavators are pinned down at the dig site by relentless trogg assaults. With his crew entirely occupied defending their archaeological work and fighting to survive, Ironband cannot spare anyone to make the trek back down the road to Thelsamar. An outside traveler like you provides a swift, reliable courier to carry his words through the dangerous wilderness.",al={"why send me","why not go himself","why deliver the report"},it="why_me",add="0b7d15ff"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you help Ironband pursue the Explorers' League's historical work and protect your kin from trogg attacks.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know reliable blasting powder is needed to break dense bedrock and tunnel into ancient strata.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep supply lines open between Thelsamar and remote outposts across Loch Modan's mountains."},kw={"blastpowder","excavation progress report","explorers' league","jern hornhelm","loch modan","prospector ironband","thelsamar","trogg"},rel={"npc:prospector-ironband","npc:jern-hornhelm","subzone:thelsamar","quest:301","topic:trogg","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Prospector Ironband",["end"]="Jern Hornhelm",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=298},src={"Excavation Progress Report"}}
E["quest:307"] = {t="quest",n="Filthy Paws",z="lochmodan",s="In Silver Stream Mine, Filthy Paws supplies wait in danger. The Miners' League stored its equipment there after the ore ran dry, but kobolds now fill the tunnels. Mountaineer Stormpike wants the tools recovered before his warriors attack.",h="In Silver Stream Mine, Filthy Paws supplies wait in danger.",sec={{t="A Depleted Depot",b="Silver Stream Mine lies in northern Loch Modan, east of Algaz Station. Its silver ran out long ago, so the dwarven Miners' League turned the empty shafts into a depot for spare excavation gear, picks, and staging materials. Across Khaz Modan, sturdy tunnels make good storehouses, provided they stay guarded and locked against the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Paws in the Depot",b="As dwarven watchfulness across Loch Modan has thinned, kobolds have slipped into the mine. Dark shafts and gleaming iron tools drew the scavengers, and soon the depot became their warren. Mountaineer Stormpike is ready to lead warriors inside and drive them out, but their heavy boots and sweeping blows could smash the crates. You can slip or fight your way in to recover the League's supplies before the assault begins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was gear left in the mine if it had already run dry?",a="After the ore ran dry, the Miners' League made Silver Stream Mine a central depot. Its dry, solid tunnels sheltered bulky tools and supplies until they were needed elsewhere.",al={"why is gear in silver stream mine","why tools in mine","miners league depot"},it="history"},{q="Why doesn't Mountaineer Stormpike clear the mine himself?",a="Stormpike is under orders to wait. The Miners' League also wants its gear recovered first, since warriors rushing through narrow, dark shafts could smash the crated tools in the fight.",al={"why stormpike not going","why mountaineers waiting","stormpike quest reason"},it="why_me"},{q="Where is the Silver Stream Mine located?",a="Silver Stream Mine lies in northern Loch Modan, east of Algaz Station and southwest of the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"silver stream mine location","where is silver stream mine","where filthy paws takes place"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What makes kobolds so interested in dwarven tools?",a="Kobolds scavenge beneath the earth and covet metal picks, shovels, candles, and finished ironwork. A storehouse of dwarven tools makes burrowing easier and is hard for them to resist.",al={"why do kobolds want gear","kobold tool theft","kobolds silver stream mine"}},{q="Is the Silver Stream Mine dangerous to explore alone?",a="Narrow passages and dense clusters of kobolds make the mine dangerous. Mountaineer Stormpike warns that you may want companions with you.",al={"is filthy paws hard","silver stream mine difficulty","can i solo filthy paws"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Who owns the supplies stored in the mine?",a="The supplies belong to the Ironforge Miners' League, the trade guild overseeing quarrying, mining, and subterranean resources across the dwarven kingdom.",al={"who owns the gear","miners league crates","who runs miners league"}},{q="Why does Mountaineer Stormpike want the miners' gear recovered?",a="The Miners' League converted the depleted Silver Stream Mine into a storehouse, but kobolds have infested the tunnels and seized the equipment. While the Mountaineers plan to scour the vermin out soon, the League insists that their valuable tools be extracted first. Stormpike is sending you in ahead of the military sweep so heavy-handed dwarf warriors do not smash the delicate gear in the upcoming assault.",al={"why does stormpike want gear","stormpike filthy paws motive","why recover miners gear"},it="motive",add="c638d192"},{q="What is the Miners' Gear used for?",a="The gear consists of quality dwarven tools and supplies belonging to the Miners' League. After the Silver Stream Mine ran dry of ore, the League repurposed its chambers as a secure depot to stockpile working equipment. The League needs these valuable implements retrieved intact before combat ruins them.",al={"what is miners gear","miners gear purpose","what are the dwarven tools for"},it="item",add="e40e35ce"},{q="Who has taken over the Silver Stream Mine?",a="A pack of kobolds has overrun the old mine tunnels. Naturally drawn to subterranean dwellings and shiny metal, these pests moved into the depleted shafts and began rifling through the stored equipment, defiling dwarven tools with their paws.",al={"who is in silver stream mine","filthy paws enemies","what took over the mine"},it="target",add="31be8455"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may see kobolds defiling the Miners' League's craft as an insult calling for swift reclamation and sharp steel.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know the worth of high-grade dwarven gear and what is lost when useful tools rust in the paws of cave vermin.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know clearing supply depots helps keep vital infrastructure open while dwarven defenses are stretched thin across Khaz Modan."},kw={"filthy paws","kobold","loch modan","miners gear","miners' league","mountaineer stormpike","silver stream mine","thelsamar"},rel={"npc:mountaineer-stormpike","subzone:silver-stream-mine","topic:kobold","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Mountaineer Stormpike",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=307,ri={"Miners' Gear"}},src={"Filthy Paws (Classic)"}}
E["quest:309"] = {t="quest",n="Protecting the Shipment",z="lochmodan",s="In southern Loch Modan, Miran carries blasting powder toward Ironband's Excavation Site. Prospector Ironband needs it for his dig, but failed supply lines and threats to the courier wagons have left Miran stranded.",h="In southern Loch Modan, Miran carries blasting powder toward Ironband's Excavation Site.",sec={{t="A Powder Run in Peril",b="Prospector Ironband needs blasting powder to cut through stone at his dig. Miran is stranded on the road under threat, carrying a heavy load. You guide him along the uneven roads to the excavation site so the powder can reach the dig.",sp=0},{t="Dark Iron Sympathizers",b="Dark Iron infiltrators wait near the excavation site to seize the explosive cargo. Their ambush shows that Dark Iron forces are securing illicit materials and sowing discord in Loch Modan. The delivery keeps the dig going, but Ironband now knows enemy sabotage reaches into Alliance territory.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Miran?",a="Miran is an Alliance courier carrying vital supplies, including blasting powder, along Loch Modan's dangerous back roads toward Ironband's Excavation Site.",al={"who is miran","miran loch modan","courier miran"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Prospector Ironband need the powder?",a="Prospector Ironband leads an archaeological dig in southern Loch Modan. His team needs blasting powder to clear rock, uncover buried relics, and keep the work going.",al={"why ironband needs powder","powder purpose","ironband blasting powder"},it="purpose"},{q="Who attacks during the escort?",a="Dark Iron dwarf saboteurs ambush Miran near the excavation site, seeking the explosives and trying to thwart Ironforge's operations in the region.",al={"who ambushes miran","ambush attackers","escort attackers"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the escort lead?",a="The escort follows a road in southern Loch Modan and ends at Ironband's Excavation Site in the hills southeast of the lake.",al={"escort destination","where does miran go","where is ironband"},it="place"},{q="Why are Dark Irons in Loch Modan?",a="The Dark Iron clan keeps secret enclaves and spies throughout Khaz Modan. They raid supply lines, sabotage Explorers' League digs, and seek to weaken Ironforge's defenses.",al={"dark iron loch modan","why dark iron dwarves here","dark iron presence"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after the shipment arrives?",a="Prospector Ironband receives the powder and thanks the Light that it arrived, though Dark Iron sympathizers are operating nearby.",al={"quest continuation","what after protecting the shipment","next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Miran want this done?",a="Miran is tasked with hauling vital blasting powder through hostile territory to Prospector Ironband's excavation site. The shipment is heavy and the road is treacherous, made worse by the lurking threat of Dark Iron ambushes. He cannot manage both carrying the volatile cargo and defending himself along the perilous route.",al={"miran motive","why escort miran","why deliver powder"},it="motive",add="a48eefd2"},{q="Why does Miran need your help instead of the local guards?",a="Loch Modan's Mountaineers are stretched thin holding back trogg incursions and securing major settlements throughout the region. With no official patrols available to guard a supply run, Miran relies on capable adventurers like you to fend off the Dark Iron dwarves lurking in the hills.",al={"why me miran","why does miran need help","why no mountaineers miran"},it="why_me",add="bdc08a2b"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you defend Ironband's supplies and protect ancestral discoveries from sabotage by your bitter Dark Iron kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep Loch Modan's couriers safe from subterranean raiders and preserve the link between Ironforge and the eastern frontiers.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know the value and danger of blasting powder when cutting into Khaz Modan's stubborn bedrock."},kw={"blasting powder","dark iron ambush","ironband's excavation site","loch modan escort","miran","prospector ironband"},rel={"quest:302","npc:prospector-ironband","subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site","quest:436","zone:lochmodan","topic:light"},m={start="Miran",["end"]="Prospector Ironband",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=309},src={"Protecting the Shipment (Classic)"}}
E["quest:418"] = {t="quest",n="Thelsamar Blood Sausages",z="lochmodan",s="At Thelsamar's Stoutlager Inn, Vidra Hearthstove keeps Thelsamar Blood Sausages on the table. A favorite across Loch Modan, they need fresh ingredients from the valley.",h="At Thelsamar's Stoutlager Inn, Vidra Hearthstove keeps Thelsamar Blood Sausages on the table.",sec={{t="A Hearty Highland Dish",b="Hungry children and miners returning from the Ironband Excavation fill Thelsamar's tavern. Vidra Hearthstove tends the stove, making sausages known across Loch Modan. Her recipe draws on wildlife from the rugged mountain pass.",sp=0},{t="Unconventional Spices",b="Vidra uses boar intestines for casings and bear meat for the filling. Spider ichor gives the sausages their sharp, pungent bite. Gathering the entrails and venomous fluid takes a steady stomach, though travelers come to appreciate this regional favorite.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vidra Hearthstove?",a="Vidra Hearthstove cooks at the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar. She takes pride in feeding Loch Modan's hard-working folk, especially laborers from nearby excavation sites.",al={"vidra","who is vidra","thelsamar cook"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the recipe use spider ichor?",a="Vidra adds spider ichor to give her blood sausages a sharp, pungent flavor.",al={"spider ichor in sausage","why spider ichor","spider spice"},it="item"},{q="Who eats Thelsamar blood sausages?",a="Thelsamar's townspeople, children, and weary workers returning from shifts at the Ironband Excavation eat the sausages.",al={"who eats blood sausage","why make sausage"},it="people"},{q="Where are the ingredients found?",a="Black bears, mountain boars, and wood lurker spiders roam Loch Modan's wilderness and wooded hills around the lake.",al={"where to get bear meat","where to get boar intestines","ingredient locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What casing is used for the sausages?",a="Vidra uses casings cleaned from local mountain boars to hold bear meat and seasoned filling together over the fire.",al={"sausage casings","boar intestines","casing recipe"},it="item"},{q="Do travelers learn to cook these sausages?",a="Yes. Bring Vidra the ingredients, and she shares the recipe with travelers who know how to cook.",al={"can i cook blood sausage","sausage recipe","cooking recipe"},it="for_you"},{q="Why does Vidra Hearthstove need these ingredients collected?",a="Thelsamar is bustling with hungry locals, from rowdy children running through the streets to exhausted laborers returning from the nearby excavation site. Vidra takes immense pride in keeping everyone fed with the town's famous blood sausages, but keeping up with that endless demand requires a steady supply of fresh local game.",al={"why make blood sausages","vidra hearthstove motive","why does vidra need food"},it="motive",add="afb643f5"},{q="What is the Bear Meat used for in the recipe?",a="Bear meat provides the hearty, filling core of Thelsamar's signature blood sausages. Loch Modan's bears roam plentifully in the surrounding wilderness, offering dense, rich meat capable of satisfying the demanding appetites of hardworking dwarven miners and laborers.",al={"why bear meat","bear meat recipe","what is bear meat for"},it="item",add="97b761ee"},{q="Why does Vidra ask a traveler to gather the ingredients instead of getting them herself?",a="Vidra runs a busy kitchen and expects everyone in town to pull their weight. As she sees it, even visiting adventurers must earn their keep rather than expecting an easy handout, making hunting wild game in the hills a fair trade for a taste of her famous cooking.",al={"why does vidra need me","why can't vidra get meat","why ask traveler"},it="why_me",add="c89e7412"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gather ingredients for Vidra, and aspiring cooks can learn the Blood Sausage recipe for hearty field rations.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, blood sausage is familiar comfort food, shaped by the rugged tastes of Khaz Modan's mountain clans.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help feed Thelsamar's workforce as they maintain key infrastructure and excavate ancient ruins across Loch Modan."},kw={"bear meat","blood sausage","boar intestines","cooking","loch modan","spider ichor","thelsamar","vidra hearthstove"},rel={"npc:vidra-hearthstove","subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Vidra Hearthstove",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=418,ri={"Bear Meat","Boar Intestines","Spider Ichor"}},src={"Thelsamar Blood Sausages (Classic)"}}
E["quest:436"] = {t="quest",n="Ironband's Excavation",z="lochmodan",s="Jern Hornhelm has sent you from Thelsamar to find out why Ironband's Excavation is making so little progress. Supplies reach Prospector Ironband's team, and Jern trusts his diligence, but the work remains slow.",h="Jern Hornhelm has sent you from Thelsamar to find out why Ironband's Excavation is making so little progress.",sec={{t="A Slowdown in the Foothills",b="Jern Hornhelm watches from Thelsamar as provisions and tools cross Loch Modan to the Explorers' League. They arrive steadily, yet the dig makes little progress. Jern suspects something is disrupting the work. He needs you to find out what is holding the team back.",sp=0},{t="The Trogg Infestation",b="At the excavation in the eastern hills, Explorer Magmar Fellhew reports that violent troggs have overrun the site. They harass the dwarven crew and scatter its discoveries. Until the intruders are driven back, the League cannot study the ancient stones.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Ironband's Excavation?",a="Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar asks you to check on the excavation. Deliveries continue, but progress remains slow, and he wants you to learn why.",al={"quest starter","who gives quest","jern hornhelm role"}},{q="Where is the excavation site located?",a="The excavation lies in the foothills east of the loch. From Thelsamar, skirt the southern end of the water, then follow the path east into the hills.",al={"dig site location","where is ironbands excavation","how to get there"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Magmar Fellhew?",a="Magmar Fellhew is an explorer assisting Prospector Ironband at the dig. He oversees its daily work and logistics, and explains the situation to messengers from Thelsamar.",al={"fellhew","who is magmar fellhew","turn in npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why has progress stalled at the dig?",a="Aggressive troggs have halted the expedition. They surged into the ruins, disrupted the excavation, and forced the League to defend itself.",al={"why slow","delay reason","what happened to the dig"},it="conflict"},{q="What comes next after completing this quest?",a="Magmar Fellhew directs you to help the team reclaim what was lost. The work continues with Gathering Idols, as you recover relics stolen by the troggs.",al={"next quest","followup","gathering idols quest"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Explorers' League looking for here?",a="Prospector Ironband's expedition seeks ancient relics and stonework beneath Loch Modan. The discoveries may shed light on dwarven history and their long-lost origins.",al={"excavation purpose","dwarf dig reason","ancient ruins loch modan"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Jern Hornhelm send you to Ironband's Excavation?",a="Jern has been sending steady shipments of supplies out to Prospector Ironband's dig site east of the loch, but progress has ground to an alarming crawl. Knowing Ironband to be a stout, dependable dwarf who prides himself on results, Jern fears foul forces are disrupting the dig. He sends you to investigate with Magmar Fellhew and discover what is holding them up.",al={"why does jern care","jern hornhelm reason","why send to excavation"},it="motive",add="47b557b9"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know each dig in Khaz Modan helps reveal the truth of dwarven ancestry and Titan heritage. Ironforge depends on Ironband's crew staying safe.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure Loch Modan by keeping its trade roads and research sites clear of trogg tribes from below."},kw={"excavation","explorers league","fellhew","hornhelm","ironband","loch modan","thelsamar","troggs"},rel={"npc:jern-hornhelm","npc:prospector-ironband","zone:lochmodan","topic:trogg","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Jern Hornhelm",["end"]="Magmar Fellhew",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=436},src={"Ironband's Excavation"}}
E["quest:454"] = {t="quest",n="After the Ambush",z="lochmodan",s="Miran needs an escort to carry blasting powder to Loch Modan’s southern excavation site. Dark Iron dwarves ambushed the supply run, and the road is still dangerous.",h="Miran needs an escort to carry blasting powder to Loch Modan’s southern excavation site.",sec={{t="A Fractured Supply Line",b="Saean and his conspirators attacked the supply run. Barrels were scattered, and the road became perilous. Huldar remains behind to guard the powder left there. Miran prepares to move ahead with the next load, so the supply line is split.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Dig",b="The southern excavation site needs blasting powder to break stone and uncover titan relics. Miran fears another ambush from the ridges. He seeks a companion before loading his cargo and setting out past any traps the Dark Irons may have prepared.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are Huldar and Miran?",a="Huldar and Miran are dwarven haulers carrying heavy barrels of blasting powder across Loch Modan for local excavations.",al={"who is huldar","who is miran","powder haulers loch modan"},it="people"},{q="Why can't Huldar and Miran travel together?",a="Huldar and Miran cannot travel together because the ambush left the shipment vulnerable. Huldar stayed behind to guard the remaining barrels while Miran moved ahead with the first batch.",al={"why split up","why split powder"},it="why_me"},{q="Who attacked the shipment?",a="Hostile Dark Iron dwarves led by Saean ambushed the haulers. They seek to disrupt Alliance operations and seize or destroy the mining explosives.",al={"who ambushed them","who is saean"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Miran taking the powder?",a="Miran is taking the barrels to Loch Modan’s southern excavation site. Prospector Ironband’s team needs blasting powder there to clear rock and uncover buried ruins.",al={"where is powder going","miran destination"},it="place"},{q="Why is blasting powder so heavily guarded in Loch Modan?",a="The Explorers' League needs blasting powder for its excavations, but the explosives are dangerous in the wrong hands. Dark Iron infiltrators across the region seek to sabotage supplies and weaken Ironforge’s hold on the territory.",al={"why protect blasting powder","powder importance"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after talking to Miran?",a="After checking the wagon and cargo, Miran asks you to escort him along the road so the shipment reaches the excavation site intact.",al={"next step after the ambush","what does miran do"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Huldar want this done?",a="Huldar and Miran were ambushed while transporting blasting powder, forcing them to divide their responsibilities. With Huldar staying behind to guard the remaining barrels from further sabotage, Miran is left to haul the next shipment alone. Knowing that Dark Iron dwarves are actively stalking the roads of Loch Modan, Huldar refuses to let his partner walk into danger without protection.",al={"huldar motive","why help miran","why escort miran"},it="motive",add="f69f8c9d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, protecting Ironforge’s supplies from Dark Iron saboteurs helps keep your homeland’s mountain passes and mining operations safe.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, keeping supplies moving in Loch Modan helps the League’s research continue and keeps the southern passes under Alliance control.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know blasting powder drives deep underground digs, so protecting these barrels matters to any serious mining venture."},kw={"ambush","blasting powder","dark iron","excavation","huldar","loch modan","miran","saean"},rel={"npc:huldar","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Huldar",["end"]="Miran",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=454},src={"After the Ambush"}}
E["quest:455"] = {t="quest",n="The Algaz Gauntlet",z="lochmodan",s="At Dun Algaz, orcs have seized the pass between Loch Modan and the Wetlands. The Dragonmaw threaten Ironforge's route to Menethil Harbor, so Mountaineer Rockgar sends Alliance travelers to strike them and carry word to Valstag Ironjaw.",h="At Dun Algaz, orcs have seized the pass between Loch Modan and the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Severed Artery",b="Crags divide Loch Modan from the Wetlands, and Dun Algaz is the way across. It is the only overland mountain pass between them, and Ironforge depends on it for trade, troop movements, and supplies bound for Menethil Harbor, the Alliance's main coastal port in the region.\n\nIf the pass falls, Ironforge loses its route to the western seas. Isolated outposts would also lose access to dwarven reinforcements.",sp=0},{t="The Dragonmaw Surge",b="Dragonmaw remnants have haunted the hills and ruins of the Wetlands since the Second War. Now they have pushed into Dun Algaz in an organized assault, seizing the tunnels and fortifying the pass with their scouts and grunts.\n\nMountaineer Rockgar asks Alliance travelers to slay the orcs and carry word of the attack to Valstag Ironjaw in Menethil Harbor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Dun Algaz so important to the Alliance?",a="Dun Algaz is the only direct mountain route between Loch Modan and the Wetlands. It connects the heart of Khaz Modan to Menethil Harbor, the main Alliance port for sea travel.",al={"why dun algaz matters","dun algaz importance","why clear the pass"},it="place"},{q="Who are the Dragonmaw orcs occupying the pass?",a="The Dragonmaw are remnants of the Old Horde, known for enslaving red dragons during the Second War. After their defeat, scattered factions retreated into the Wetlands. Now they have pushed south into the pass to seize its strategic choke points.",al={"who are the dragonmaw","why are orcs in dun algaz","dragonmaw clan lore"},it="target"},{q="Where does this mission lead?",a="After you fight through the pass and slay the grunts and scouts, the road leads north through the Wetlands. At the fork, take the western road to Menethil Harbor and report to Valstag Ironjaw.",al={"where do i go after algaz gauntlet","who gets the report","where is valstag ironjaw"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is Valstag Ironjaw surprised by the report?",a="The Dragonmaw usually keep to hidden camps in the marshy hills of the Wetlands. Their bold push into the dwarven tunnels of Dun Algaz marks an unexpected turn toward organized aggression.",al={"valstag reaction","why did orcs attack algaz"},it="conflict"},{q="Who orders the assault on the pass?",a="Mountaineer Rockgar, a dwarven guard at Loch Modan's northern border, orders the strike. He wants to stop the orcs from securing their foothold and cutting off communication with the coast.",al={"who gives the quest","mountaineer rockgar mission"},it="in_charge"},{q="What comes after completing this gauntlet?",a="Your report to Valstag Ironjaw alerts the Menethil Harbor garrison to the immediate threat. It opens further chances to aid the dwarven defense against the Dragonmaw in the Wetlands.",al={"next quest after algaz gauntlet","what to do in menethil"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mountaineer Rockgar want this done?",a="Mountaineer Rockgar fears losing the vital mountain corridor linking Loch Modan to the Wetlands. Dragonmaw orcs have pushed out of their marshland haven and seized Dun Algaz, threatening to sever communication and supply lines between the inland dwarf lands and Menethil Harbor. By sending you to cut down their scouts and grunts, Rockgar hopes to blunt their momentum, break their hold on the tunnels, and get critical word of the incursion to the harbor's defenders.",al={"rockgar motive","why clear dun algaz","why does rockgar send you"},it="motive",add="5ee6c7e9"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, clearing Dun Algaz protects Khaz Modan's ancestral mountain passes and keeps the route between Ironforge and its western sea harbor open.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, Menethil Harbor is your main gateway between the Eastern Kingdoms and western lands. Keeping the overland route clear matters to the whole Alliance."},kw={"dragonmaw","dun algaz","loch modan","menethil harbor","pass","rockgar","valstag ironjaw","wetlands"},rel={"quest:468","subzone:dun-algaz","npc:valstag-ironjaw","topic:dragonmaw-clan","zone:lochmodan","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor"},m={start="Mountaineer Rockgar",["end"]="Valstag Ironjaw",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=455},src={"The Algaz Gauntlet"}}
E["quest:468"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Mountaineer Rockgar",z="lochmodan",s="At Dun Algaz, Mountaineer Rockgar is preparing an expedition into the Wetlands. Mountaineer Kadrell sends you north from Loch Modan to join him in the sodden lowlands along the pass between the dwarven homeland and the northern territories.",h="At Dun Algaz, Mountaineer Rockgar is preparing an expedition into the Wetlands.",sec={{t="The Road to the North Gate",b="Dun Algaz cuts through the northern ridge between Loch Modan and the marshy Wetlands. Trade, messengers, and military detachments pass through this fortified route between Ironforge and Alliance settlements farther north. As tensions rise along the borders, Mountaineer Kadrell watches the road and seeks hardy volunteers for the northern outposts.",sp=0},{t="A Mission Gone Awry",b="Mountaineer Kadrell sends recruits expecting a routine scouting expedition. But at Dun Algaz, Mountaineer Rockgar prepares for active conflict, not a peaceful reconnaissance. Hostile forces choke the pass, and the scouting effort becomes a bitter struggle to secure the gauntlet.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the order to report to Rockgar?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell gives the order. He is stationed in Thelsamar across the road from the Stoutlager Inn, watching the main road toward the mountain pass.",al={"who starts report to mountaineer rockgar","quest giver rockgar","kadrell quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Mountaineer Rockgar?",a="Mountaineer Rockgar is stationed north along the road out of Loch Modan, guarding the entrance to the tunnels of Dun Algaz.",al={"rockgar location","where is rockgar","mountaineer rockgar spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this mission through Dun Algaz so important?",a="Dun Algaz is the main overland corridor between Loch Modan and the Wetlands. Keeping it clear protects Alliance supplies and military messages, and keeps safe travel to Menethil Harbor and beyond.",al={"why go to dun algaz","dun algaz importance","wetlands route"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after meeting Mountaineer Rockgar?",a="Rockgar immediately enlists your help with The Algaz Gauntlet. The scouting expedition has become a bloody fight against hostile forces blocking the mountain tunnels.",al={"what comes after report to rockgar","rockgar follow up","next quest after rockgar"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What level of adventurer should take on this assignment?",a="This assignment is for seasoned travelers around level twenty to twenty-one. They are finishing their duties in Loch Modan and preparing to brave the Wetlands.",al={"rockgar quest level","level for dun algaz","when to go to wetlands"},gp=true},{q="Is this quest available to Horde characters?",a="No. The Ironforge Mountaineers are loyal to King Magni Bronzebeard and the Alliance. Only Alliance travelers can accept the assignment.",al={"can horde do this quest","horde report to rockgar"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why does Mountaineer Kadrell want this done?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell is stationed along the northern road in Loch Modan and knows Mountaineer Rockgar is gathering capable volunteers for a critical scouting mission into the Wetlands. By directing hardy travelers toward Dun Algaz, Kadrell helps ensure the northern mountain passes stay monitored and the outpost receives the extra hands it desperately needs.",al={"why send to rockgar","kadrell motive","why volunteer dun algaz"},it="motive",add="8a14b66e"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, answering fellow mountaineers helps keep the overland link between the Ironforge heartland and the dwarven holdings in the Wetlands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, helping secure Dun Algaz keeps the overland route to Menethil Harbor open. It is the Alliance's main western port in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"dun algaz","ironforge","kadrell","loch modan","mountaineer","rockgar","scouting","wetlands"},rel={"quest:455","subzone:dun-algaz","npc:mountaineer-kadrell","zone:lochmodan","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Mountaineer Kadrell",["end"]="Mountaineer Rockgar",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=468},src={"Report to Mountaineer Rockgar"}}
E["quest:6387"] = {t="quest",n="Honor Students",z="lochmodan",s="Brock Stoneseeker sends an order from Thelsamar to Ironforge for honorary mining picks. He asks you to enlist Thorgrum Borrelson to carry it there.",h="Brock Stoneseeker sends an order from Thelsamar to Ironforge for honorary mining picks.",sec={{t="A Miner's Due",b="Brock teaches new miners about rock composition and tunnel safety. He rewards the apprentices who distinguish themselves with honorary picks. Mining sustains Thelsamar, and dwarves take pride in the craft. Local supplies are limited, so the picks must come from Ironforge across Khaz Modan.",sp=0},{t="Taking to the Skies",b="Thorgrum tends the gryphon roost beside Thelsamar, linking the frontier to Ironforge through the kingdom's aerial courier network. Bring Brock's order to him, and he can arrange a swift courier run to the capital's foundries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brock Stoneseeker?",a="Brock Stoneseeker teaches mining in Thelsamar. He trains novices in excavation and stonecraft.",al={"brock stoneseeker","who is brock","mining trainer thelsamar"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Brock need picks from Ironforge?",a="Brock needs honorary picks for students who excel at mining, but local supplies are limited. His order must reach Golnir Bouldertoe, a mining supplies vendor in Ironforge.",al={"why ironforge","why picks","brock's list"},it="motive"},{q="What role does Thorgrum Borrelson play in this task?",a="Thorgrum Borrelson tends Thelsamar's gryphon roost. Brock asks you to bring him the order so he can arrange aerial transport to Ironforge.",al={"thorgrum borrelson","who is thorgrum","gryphon master thelsamar"},it="identity"},{q="Who receives the list in Ironforge?",a="Golnir Bouldertoe receives the list in Ironforge. He prepares honorary picks for Brock's accomplished students.",al={"who gets the list","golnir bouldertoe","ironforge contact"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this errand lead next?",a="After you speak with Thorgrum Borrelson, he arranges a gryphon flight to Ironforge. There, you can deliver Brock's order to Golnir Bouldertoe.",al={"next step","what follows honor students","after brock's list"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="You begin and finish in Thelsamar, a settlement in the hills of Loch Modan.",al={"quest location","where is thelsamar","where to start honor students"},it="place"},{q="Why does Brock Stoneseeker ask an adventurer instead of delivering the list himself?",a="Brock is busy training aspiring miners right here in Thelsamar, instructing new recruits in the craft and tending to his forge. Leaving his post to travel all the way to Ironforge would stall lessons for the local apprentices, making a traveling adventurer the perfect courier to carry his list to the city.",al={"why ask me brock","why doesnt brock go to ironforge","why can't brock take the list"},it="why_me",add="7a941756"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you see how dwarves honor skill in the craft. Mastering stone and finding veins can earn recognition from an instructor.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see the bond between frontier settlements like Thelsamar and the capital's halls deep in the mountains.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler in Loch Modan, you encounter the flight masters and aerial couriers who link its settlements."},kw={"brock stoneseeker","golnir bouldertoe","gryphon","honor students","ironforge","loch modan","mining","thelsamar","thorgrum borrelson"},rel={"npc:brock-stoneseeker","npc:thorgrum-borrelson","npc:golnir-bouldertoe","subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Brock Stoneseeker",["end"]="Thorgrum Borrelson",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6387},src={"Honor Students (Classic)"}}
E["quest:8642"] = {t="quest",n="Silvervein the Elder",z="lochmodan",s="During the Lunar Festival, travelers find Silvervein the Elder on the hills above Thelsamar in Loch Modan. They honor him and the ancient ties among Azeroth’s elder peoples, and he grants them an ancestral blessing.",h="During the Lunar Festival, travelers find Silvervein the Elder on the hills above Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="A Vigil Over Thelsamar",b="Above Thelsamar, Silvervein keeps watch as travelers honor him. He holds memories from ages past. Though trogg invasions and local disputes trouble Loch Modan, the elder spirit remains peaceful on his overlook.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Olden Races",b="Silvervein welcomes travelers who honor Azeroth’s olden races. His greeting carries ancestral appreciation. To those who pay homage, he offers a commemorative token.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Silvervein?",a="Silvervein is an ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival. He spends the festival atop the high bluffs near Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",al={"silvervein","who is silvervein","elder silvervein loch modan"}},{q="Where can I find Elder Silvervein?",a="Silvervein waits on a grassy hill overlooking Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",al={"silvervein location","where is elder silvervein","find silvervein"}},{q="What is the purpose of seeking out Elder Silvervein?",a="During the Lunar Festival, travelers seek Silvervein to honor the ancestors and ancient races. He gives them a festive token and an ancestral blessing.",al={"why visit silvervein","what does silvervein do","silvervein purpose"}},{q="What does he mean by 'the olden races'?",a="The olden races are Azeroth’s ancient peoples, who lived and shaped the world long before modern conflicts took center stage. Their heritage endures.",al={"olden races meaning","why olden races"}},{q="Is Elder Silvervein friendly to Horde travelers?",a="Yes. Silvervein welcomes peaceful travelers of every background who come during the Lunar Festival to honor the ancestors.",al={"can horde talk to silvervein","horde silvervein"}},{q="Does Elder Silvervein have any connection to the trogg invasion?",a="No. Trogg incursions and excavator troubles trouble Loch Modan, but Silvervein remains apart from local military conflicts and focused on honoring the ancestors.",al={"silvervein troggs","is silvervein fighting troggs"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can honor your shared ancient history with Silvervein near Thelsamar.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler in Loch Modan, you can climb the ridge above Thelsamar and honor the ancient dead between trogg hunts."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","elder","loch modan","lunar festival","silvervein","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Elder Silvervein",id=8642},src={"Silvervein the Elder"}}
E["subzone:algaz-station"] = {t="subzone",n="Algaz Station",z="lochmodan",s="At Algaz Station, Mountaineers keep watch over the northern road from Loch Modan to the Wetlands. South of Dun Algaz, the outpost guards the mountain pass.",h="At Algaz Station, Mountaineers keep watch over the northern road from Loch Modan to the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Watching the Northern Pass",b="Dwarven Mountaineers watch the road north from Loch Modan at Algaz Station. East of North Gate Pass and south of Dun Algaz, the post guards the route between Ironforge and the northern lowlands. Trade and troops travel through the mountain tunnels, though beasts and troggs threaten the hills. The Mountaineers keep the way open and give weary travelers a place to rest, make repairs, and find martial support before entering the pass.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Algaz Station?",a="Algaz Station is an Ironforge military outpost in northwestern Loch Modan. Its Mountaineers guard the passes leading north to Dun Algaz and aid travelers on the way.",al={"what is this place","algaz station purpose","who runs algaz station"},it="place"},{q="Where does the station get its name?",a="The station takes its name from Dun Algaz, the great dwarven pass and tunnel system just to its north. Dun Algaz connects Loch Modan to the Wetlands.",al={"why is it called algaz station","dun algaz connection","name meaning"},it="name"},{q="Who can be found at Algaz Station?",a="Dwarven Mountaineers man the outpost, including Mountaineer Stormpike. Armorer Gothor Brumn repairs travelers' gear.",al={"who is here","npcs at algaz station","mountaineer stormpike location"},it="residents"},{q="Is Algaz Station dangerous?",a="The outpost itself is a safe haven manned by vigilant dwarven mountaineers, but the surrounding roads are rife with peril. Situated just south of Dun Algaz and east of the North Gate Pass, travelers resting here must remain watchful of hostile troggs, beasts, and greenskins roaming the northern reaches of Loch Modan.",al={"algaz station danger","is algaz station safe","threats at algaz station"},it="danger",add="c8a5caec"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Algaz Station marks Ironforge's reach. Its Mountaineers guard the king's highways against dangers from the mountains.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can use the outpost as a secure staging ground and repair stop on the way between Loch Modan and the northern marshlands."},kw={"algaz station","dun algaz","gothor brumn","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineer stormpike","mountaineers","north gate pass"},rel={"subzone:dun-algaz","zone:lochmodan","subzone:north-gate-pass","npc:mountaineer-stormpike"},src={"Algaz Station"}}
E["subzone:farstrider-lodge"] = {t="subzone",n="Farstrider Lodge",z="lochmodan",s="In southeastern Loch Modan, Farstrider Lodge welcomes hunters and travelers bound for the wilds. Its high elven style sets it apart, though dwarves and humans live there too.",h="In southeastern Loch Modan, Farstrider Lodge welcomes hunters and travelers bound for the wilds.",sec={{t="An Elven Haven in the Mountains",b="Farstrider Lodge looks unlike the stone buildings of Khaz Modan. Its design recalls high elven craft, though Vyrin Swiftwind is the only known high elf still living there. Dwarves and humans make their homes beside him. No one knows who founded the lodge or when it was built.",sp=0},{t="A Waystation for the Wilds",b="In the southeastern hills of Loch Modan, Farstrider Lodge offers hunters and travelers a place to stop before entering the wilds. Hunter and pet trainers work there, alongside merchants. Others come seeking help with local wildlife.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there an elven lodge in Khaz Modan?",a="Farstrider Lodge bears a design that suggests high elven origins, and Vyrin Swiftwind is its only known high elven resident. No one knows who founded it, when it was built, or what its first purpose was.",al={"why elven building loch modan","who built farstrider lodge","why high elf lodge here"},it="origin"},{q="Are there still high elves living here?",a="Vyrin Swiftwind is the only high elf known to live at Farstrider Lodge. Dwarves and humans live there too, including mountaineers and huntsmen who maintain the lodge and trade with travelers.",al={"are there high elves here","who lives in farstrider lodge","vyrin swiftwind"},it="residents"},{q="What services are available at Farstrider Lodge?",a="Farstrider Lodge has hunter and pet trainers, merchants, and requests for help with Loch Modan's wilderness.",al={"what is at farstrider lodge","hunter trainers loch modan"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is Farstrider Lodge?",a="Farstrider Lodge is a hunting outpost nestled along the southeastern shores of Loch Modan. Distinctive for its elegant elven architecture amidst the rugged dwarven hills, it serves as a tranquil haven for trackers, beastmasters, and wayfarers traveling through Khaz Modan.",al={"what is farstrider lodge","farstrider lodge lore","tell me about farstrider lodge"},it="place",add="ede1c062"},{q="Why is it called Farstrider Lodge?",a="The name recalls the Farstriders, the rangers of Quel'Thalas, fitting the lodge's high elven architecture. The lodge's exact founding history is not established.",al={"why is it called farstrider lodge","farstrider lodge name meaning","who are the farstriders loch modan"},it="name",add="048016ac"},{q="Is Farstrider Lodge dangerous?",a="Farstrider Lodge itself is a secure sanctuary for members of the Alliance, offering rest and supplies. However, the wilderness just beyond its doorstep crawls with aggressive wildlife and nearby hostile troggs and gnolls roaming the Loch Modan valleys.",al={"is farstrider lodge safe","is farstrider lodge hostile","danger farstrider lodge"},it="danger",add="65e56c06"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can find marksmanship and beast training at Farstrider Lodge, amid the game in Loch Modan's surrounding hills.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you share Farstrider Lodge with human residents and the high elf Vyrin Swiftwind."},kw={"farstrider lodge","farstriders","high elf","hunter lodge","loch modan","thelsamar","vyrin swiftwind"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:thelsamar","topic:dwarf"},src={"Farstrider Lodge"}}
E["subzone:grizzlepaw-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Grizzlepaw Ridge",z="lochmodan",s="Bears claim the rough hills of Grizzlepaw Ridge, south of Thelsamar in Loch Modan. Local hunters fear Ol' Sooty, a massive bear among them.",h="Bears claim the rough hills of Grizzlepaw Ridge, south of Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Home of the Bears",b="Grizzlepaw Ridge rises above the road south of Thelsamar, with Stonesplinter Valley along its western edge. Territorial bears threaten travelers skirting the mountains, so those passing between the dwarven settlements watch the tree line and rocky terraces. Deep within the ridge lives Ol' Sooty, an unusually fierce bear feared by local hunters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Grizzlepaw Ridge located?",a="Grizzlepaw Ridge lies in Loch Modan's central hills, directly south of Thelsamar and east of Stonesplinter Valley.",al={"where is grizzlepaw ridge","grizzlepaw ridge location","how to get to grizzlepaw ridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What dangerous creatures live on Grizzlepaw Ridge?",a="Aggressive bears roam Grizzlepaw Ridge. The most infamous is Ol' Sooty, an exceptionally large and ferocious beast that sometimes prowls toward the mountain base.",al={"bears at grizzlepaw ridge","who is ol sooty","ol sooty loch modan"},it="threat"},{q="What is Grizzlepaw Ridge?",a="Grizzlepaw Ridge is a rugged, mountainous area in Loch Modan, rising south of Thelsamar and east of Stonesplinter Valley. It is untamed dwarven wilderness dominated by dense forests and rocky crags, best known as a hunting ground and the territory of dangerous mountain bears.",al={"what is grizzlepaw ridge","grizzlepaw ridge lore","about grizzlepaw ridge"},it="place",add="57fe1f79"},{q="Is Grizzlepaw Ridge dangerous?",a="It is quite perilous for unwary travelers. The ridge is prowled by a large pack of aggressive bears. Worst among them is Ol' Sooty, a notoriously fierce bear whose lair lies up on the heights, occasionally wandering down to the base of the valley to maul anyone who crosses his path.",al={"how dangerous is grizzlepaw ridge","grizzlepaw ridge danger","threats in grizzlepaw ridge"},it="danger",add="09913c6a"},{q="Why is it called Grizzlepaw Ridge?",a="The ridge takes its name from the large, aggressive population of mountain bears that claim its slopes and rocky heights as their territory, most notably savage beasts like Ol' Sooty.",al={"grizzlepaw name origin","why grizzlepaw ridge","how did grizzlepaw ridge get its name"},it="name",add="d9ee2216"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can track wild beasts on Grizzlepaw Ridge and face apex predators like Ol' Sooty.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the bears on the ridge beside Thelsamar trouble local mountaineers and supply routes."},kw={"bears","grizzlepaw ridge","loch modan","ol' sooty","sooty","thelsamar"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:thelsamar","subzone:stonesplinter-valley"},src={"Grizzlepaw Ridge"}}
E["subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site"] = {t="subzone",n="Ironband's Excavation Site",z="lochmodan",s="In southeastern Loch Modan, troggs have driven the miners from Ironband's Excavation Site. The dig lies south of the Loch and southwest of Farstrider Lodge.",h="In southeastern Loch Modan, troggs have driven the miners from Ironband's Excavation Site.",sec={{t="Unearthing the Past",b="Prospector Ironband began the dig to seek the dwarves’ ancient Titan origins. Then the miners disturbed an unusually fierce and large breed of subterranean troggs. The creatures surged from the earth and drove the miners back. Now they camp among scattered tools, broken carts, and half-excavated relics.",sp=0},{t="Ruins in the Red Earth",b="Troggs hold the site while surviving prospectors wait at its perimeter. Like archaeological efforts in the Badlands, Wetlands, and Uldaman, this dig is caught in danger. The prospectors hope to reclaim their stolen gear and guard exposed artifacts from the ravenous troggs. Strange ancient statues remain among those artifacts, left by long-forgotten builders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Ironband's Excavation Site located?",a="Ironband's Excavation Site lies in southeastern Loch Modan, south of the Loch and southwest of Farstrider Lodge.",al={"ironband location","where is ironbands digsite","ironband map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Prospector Ironband?",a="Prospector Ironband is an archaeologist and explorer leading the Explorers' League excavation. He is trying to salvage artifacts and drive back the local troggs.",al={"who is ironband","prospector ironband lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the excavation site overrun with troggs?",a="Miners dug deeper into Loch Modan and broke into underground pockets inhabited by a large, aggressive breed of troggs. The troggs overwhelmed the workers and seized the site.",al={"why are troggs here","who attacked the digsite","ironband troggs"},it="ruin"},{q="What were the dwarves hoping to find here?",a="The dwarves hoped to find ancient Titan relics and stone ruins that could shed light on their race's ancestral origins.",al={"what are they digging for","ironband artifacts","why dig here"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Ironband's Excavation Site?",a="Ironband's Excavation Site is an expansive dwarven archaeological dig located in southeastern Loch Modan, nestled south of the loch and southwest of Farstrider Lodge. Led by Prospector Ironband, Ironforge archaeologists of the Explorers' League set up camp to unearth relics of ancient titan origins, though their digging has unfortunately awakened dormant subterranean terrors.",al={"what is this digsite","ironbands excavation site info","about ironband dig site"},it="place",add="e2620dfb"},{q="What happened at Ironband's Excavation Site?",a="Much like similar dwarven digs across Khaz Modan and beyond, the prospectors dug too deep into the subterranean layers of the earth. In doing so, they breached a nest of particularly massive and volatile troggs. The ferocious creatures surged into the open, overrunning the excavation trenches and forcing the miners and researchers to abandon their work and fight to reclaim the grounds.",al={"history ironbands excavation site","what happened to the digsite"},it="history",add="ade9a17c"},{q="Is Ironband's Excavation Site dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. The excavation trenches and terraces swarm with a brutal breed of troggs that will violently attack anyone who trespasses on their reclaimed territory. Until the League can mount a coordinated counteroffensive, solitary travelers should approach with heavy guard or steer well clear of the diggings.",al={"is ironbands excavation site safe","how dangerous is ironband digsite"},it="danger",add="2d8b70cf"},{q="Why is it called Ironband's Excavation Site?",a="The site is named after its chief supervisor, Prospector Ironband, the dwarf who founded the operation on behalf of the Ironforge Explorers' League to unearth ancient titan artifacts buried beneath the red hills of Loch Modan.",al={"why is it called ironbands excavation","who named ironband excavation site"},it="name",add="a83f1173"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know that losing this dig is a stinging setback for the Explorers' League. Recovering ancient relics here matters to understanding dwarven heritage.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can see how dwarves use heavy extraction techniques in the quarry and open pits. Trogg hostility makes prospecting hazardous."},kw={"digsite","excavation site","explorers league","ironband","loch modan","prospector ironband","troggs"},rel={"npc:prospector-ironband","quest:436","zone:lochmodan","subzone:farstrider-lodge","topic:trogg","topic:dwarf","subzone:uldaman","subzone:the-loch"},src={"Ironband's Excavation Site"}}
E["subzone:mo-grosh-stronghold"] = {t="subzone",n="Mo'grosh Stronghold",z="lochmodan",s="In northeastern Loch Modan, Mo'grosh Stronghold threatens the dwarven settlements below. Ogres raid supply caravans from caves and outer camps among ancient ruins.",h="In northeastern Loch Modan, Mo'grosh Stronghold threatens the dwarven settlements below.",sec={{t="A Looming Threat",b="Mo'grosh ogres raid supply caravans in northeastern Loch Modan. Their caves and outer camps threaten travelers and the peace of Thelsamar. Rugged stonework scattered through the camp points to an older settlement. The ogres claimed the site and raised their distinctive mounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mo'grosh Stronghold?",a="Ogres inhabit caves and surrounding grounds in the fortified compound dug into the hills of northeastern Loch Modan. Together, they form the territory's largest hostile ogre enclave.",al={"mogrosh stronghold","ogre camp loch modan","mogrosh cave"},it="place"},{q="Who used to live here before the ogres?",a="The old stonework suggests a settlement stood here before the ogres, but no one knows who its original inhabitants were.",al={"ancient ruins loch modan","who built mogrosh","trolls in loch modan"},it="history"},{q="Why are the ogres a problem for the dwarves?",a="The ogres live close to key travel routes, making them a severe hazard to local traffic and trade caravans moving through Loch Modan. Dwarven authorities call on adventurers to thin their numbers and keep the mountain passes safe.",al={"why kill mogrosh ogres","ironforge threat mogrosh"},it="threat"},{q="Who lives in Mo'grosh Stronghold?",a="The stronghold is occupied by the Mo'grosh ogres, a brutish clan that claims the hills and mounds of northeastern Loch Modan. Among their ranks are brutes, shamans, and other powerful bruisers. They dwell within crude dirt mounds and cavernous dugouts, fiercely defending their encampment from any encroaching outsiders or dwarven patrols.",al={"who lives in mogrosh stronghold","mogrosh stronghold ogres","who leads mogrosh stronghold"},it="residents",add="c213ae8d"},{q="Is Mo'grosh Stronghold dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. The Mo'grosh ogres represent one of the most perilous threats in all of Loch Modan. Unlike the scattered troggs and beasts nearby, these ogres are massive, organized, and wield brutal physical strength alongside shamanistic magic. Wandering into their camp alone is often fatal for unwary explorers, and Mountaineers from Thelsamar warn against entering without heavy backup.",al={"is mogrosh stronghold dangerous","how dangerous is mogrosh stronghold","mogrosh stronghold danger"},it="danger",add="c4467cb6"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Mo'grosh ogres constantly menace dwarven patrols and travelers. Eradicating their stronghold is a matter of civic defense for the Mountaineers of Loch Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping the Mo'grosh ogres in check helps secure Loch Modan and safe passage between Ironforge and the northern mountain roads."},kw={"loch modan","mo'grosh","mogrosh","mountaineers","ogre","ruins","stronghold"},rel={"zone:lochmodan"},src={"Mo'grosh Stronghold"}}
E["subzone:north-gate-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="North Gate Pass",z="lochmodan",s="Travelers cross North Gate Pass through the Khaz Modan peaks between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan. A fortified dwarven outpost watches the northern corridor, where travelers bound for the Wetlands pass.",h="Travelers cross North Gate Pass through the Khaz Modan peaks between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Gateway Between the Peaks",b="North Gate Pass cuts through Khaz Modan between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan. From the west, you leave steep mountain tunnels for the broad loch valley. Roads lead down toward the Wetlands, carrying dwarven messengers, merchants, and wandering adventurers. North Gate Outpost gives the route its strategic value. Mountaineers there watch for troggs and mountain predators.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does North Gate Pass lead?",a="North Gate Pass links eastern Dun Morogh with northwestern Loch Modan. The road continues north around the loch toward mountain tunnels that descend into the Wetlands, making the pass a vital junction for northern travelers.",al={"where does north gate pass go","north gate pass destination","path through north gate pass"},it="place"},{q="What guards the pass?",a="Ironforge Mountaineers guard North Gate Outpost beside the road. They watch travelers and keep prowling beasts and roaming troggs from the mountain passage.",al={"who guards north gate pass","north gate pass guards","dwarf outpost north gate"},it="in_charge"},{q="How does this differ from South Gate Pass?",a="Both passes link Dun Morogh and Loch Modan through carved tunnels. North Gate Pass is the most direct overland route for travelers bound for the Wetlands and northern lands.",al={"difference north and south gate pass","north gate vs south gate"}},{q="What is North Gate Pass?",a="North Gate Pass is a vital mountain thoroughfare carved through the Khaz Modan peaks, linking the snowy heights of Dun Morogh to the west with the lower basin of Loch Modan to the east. It is a heavily trodden route for travelers and adventurers heading toward the Wetlands descent.",al={"what is north gate pass","about north gate pass","north gate pass info"},it="place",add="c14f680d"},{q="Who lives in or runs North Gate Pass?",a="The pass is maintained and secured by the Ironforge Mountaineers stationed at North Gate Outpost. While no permanent civilian population resides directly in the pass, dwarven guards patrol and safeguard the corridor for allied travelers making the journey between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan.",al={"who controls north gate pass","who guards north gate pass","north gate pass residents"},it="residents",add="8f6c351e"},{q="Why is it called North Gate Pass?",a="The corridor takes its name from North Gate Outpost and its geographic role as the northernmost of the two primary tunnels cutting through the mountain ridge separating Dun Morogh from Loch Modan, directly contrasting with South Gate Pass to the south.",al={"why north gate pass","north gate pass name meaning","where does north gate name come from"},it="name",add="a4ac9bea"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf traveling between Ironforge and the frontier settlements around The Loch, you know North Gate Pass as a familiar, stone-hewn threshold guarded by fellow mountaineers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you rely on North Gate Pass as a vital military and supply corridor from the dwarven capital to northern expeditions bound for the Wetlands."},kw={"dun morogh","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineers","north gate outpost","north gate pass","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:north-gate-outpost","zone:lochmodan","zone:dunmorogh","zone:wetlands","subzone:the-loch"},src={"North Gate Pass"}}
E["subzone:silver-stream-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Silver Stream Mine",z="lochmodan",s="In northern Loch Modan, Silver Stream Mine lies between Algaz Station and the Stonewrought Dam. Its silver veins are spent, and Tunnel Rat kobolds now hoard stolen equipment and rare minerals in the Miners' League depot.",h="In northern Loch Modan, Silver Stream Mine lies between Algaz Station and the Stonewrought Dam.",sec={{t="From Rich Vein to Storage Depot",b="Silver Stream Mine once sent rich silver to Ironforge. Dwarf miners worked its veins until they ran dry, leaving broad chambers beneath the earth. The Miners' League put those hard-won shafts to use as a guarded storehouse for tools, mining crates, and regional equipment. The mine also yields Charged Rift Gems, which draw arcanists seeking delicate tailoring reagents.",sp=0},{t="The Kobold Incursion",b="Tunnel Rat kobolds came in great numbers and drove the Miners' League caretakers out into the cold of Loch Modan. Now they guard the stolen dwarf crates with manic fervor. Beyond the rear entrances, shattered orcish catapults and wagons lie forgotten, remnants of older frontier skirmishes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Silver Stream Mine originally used for?",a="Dwarves of Ironforge first worked Silver Stream Mine for its rich silver. When the veins ran dry, the Ironforge Miners' League turned its empty halls into a depot for tools and mining supplies.",al={"what is silver stream mine","silver stream history","why was silver stream built"},it="purpose"},{q="Who currently occupies the mine?",a="Tunnel Rat kobolds occupy Silver Stream Mine. They drove out the dwarf caretakers and now guard the League crates, hoarding supplies and digging for what remains.",al={"who lives in silver stream mine","silver stream mobs","what is inside silver stream mine"},it="residents"},{q="Why do mages travel to Silver Stream Mine?",a="Charged Rift Gems come only from Silver Stream Mine. Alliance arcanists seek them to weave enchanted robes.",al={"mage quest silver stream","charged rift gems","silver stream mage robes"}},{q="What are the ruined catapults behind the mine?",a="Broken orcish wagons and ruined catapults lie behind Silver Stream Mine. They remain from earlier wartime conflicts that threatened the passages between Loch Modan and the northern mountain passes.",al={"orc wagons behind silver stream","broken catapults loch modan mine","horde siege engines loch modan"},it="history"},{q="What is Silver Stream Mine?",a="Silver Stream Mine is a former dwarven excavation nestled in the northern crags of Loch Modan, situated east of Algaz Station and southwest of the Stonewrought Dam. Once a rich silver deposit worked by Ironforge dwarves, it was later repurposed as a supply depot for the Miners' League before falling into hostile hands.",al={"silver stream mine info","what is silver stream mine","about silver stream mine"},it="place",add="fbe48c53"},{q="Why was Silver Stream Mine abandoned?",a="The mine was initially phased out as an active dig when its silver veins tapped out long ago. The Miners' League continued using the tunnels as a secured storage depot, but dwarven workers were entirely driven out when aggressive Tunnel Rat kobolds swarmed the site to claim whatever resources remained inside.",al={"why is silver stream mine abandoned","why did dwarves leave silver stream mine","why was silver stream abandoned"},it="ruin",add="6efdd539"},{q="Is Silver Stream Mine dangerous?",a="Yes. The mine has been thoroughly overrun by hostile Tunnel Rat kobolds. Fiercely territorial and desperate to hoard the mine's contents, these subterranean pests attack any travelers or miners who dare approach the entrance or venture into the depths.",al={"is silver stream mine dangerous","threats in silver stream mine","silver stream mine monsters"},it="danger",add="339be7ce"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Silver Stream Mine is Ironforge work now lost to clumsy kobolds, who sully a respectable Miners' League depot.",["class:Mage"]="As an apprentice mage, you brave the kobold-infested tunnels for Charged Rift Gems, an indispensable ingredient in ritual garments."},kw={"charged rift gem","kobold","loch modan","miners league","silver stream mine","tunnel rat"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","quest:307","quest:1961","topic:kobold","subzone:algaz-station","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance"},src={"Silver Stream Mine"}}
E["subzone:south-gate-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="South Gate Pass",z="lochmodan",s="Travelers cross South Gate Pass between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan. Its guarded road links Ironforge with Thelsamar.",h="Travelers cross South Gate Pass between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan.",sec={{t="The Road East",b="South Gate Pass cuts through the Khaz Modan range, joining Dun Morogh's high mountains to Loch Modan's valley in the east. Stone archways mark the way from cold slopes into warmer dwarven heartlands. The road leads toward Thelsamar, carrying mountaineers, couriers, and newly trained adventurers setting out from the capital.",sp=0},{t="A Guarded Threshold",b="Dwarven mountaineers keep watch at South Gate Outpost, guarding the pass against wild beasts and prowling troggs. The road is safer than the untamed parts of the valley, though hostile wildlife and roving threats still test its approaches. Stay on the road as you travel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does South Gate Pass lead?",a="Take the road west through the tunnels to Dun Morogh's snowy highlands, then continue toward Ironforge. Eastward, the pass descends into Loch Modan's basin and leads toward Thelsamar.",al={"where does south gate pass go","south gate pass destination","south gate road"},it="place"},{q="Is South Gate Pass safe to travel?",a="Dwarven guards at South Gate Outpost make the road relatively secure. Bears, spiders, and troggs still inhabit the crags and hillsides around the tunnel mouth.",al={"is south gate pass dangerous","south gate pass threats"},it="danger"},{q="Why is this pass used more than North Gate Pass?",a="South Gate Pass offers the most direct and convenient overland route between Dun Morogh and Thelsamar. Local trade, supply caravans, and travelers bound for central Loch Modan favor it for that reason.",al={"south gate vs north gate","why use south gate"}},{q="What is South Gate Pass?",a="South Gate Pass is a vital mountain passage carving through the crags between snowy Dun Morogh to the west and the valleys of Loch Modan to the east. Because it emerges right near the town of Thelsamar, it serves as the primary route for mountaineers, couriers, and travelers journeying between Ironforge's homeland and the Loch.",al={"south gate pass info","what is south gate pass","south gate pass lore"},it="place",add="ae3b1570"},{q="Who watches over South Gate Pass?",a="The pass is guarded and maintained by the Ironforge Mountaineers stationed at South Gate Outpost. These dwarven sentries keep watch over traffic passing through the tunnels, ensuring the trade route remains open against the wild beasts and hostile threats lurking in the surrounding hills.",al={"who controls south gate pass","south gate pass guards","south gate outpost"},it="residents",add="d7b0d8f2"},{q="Why is it called South Gate Pass?",a="The pass earns its name from its position relative to the mountain spine separating Dun Morogh and Loch Modan. It forms the southern gateway through the range, mirrored to the north by North Gate Pass.",al={"south gate pass name meaning","why south gate pass","why south gate"},it="name",add="487bb631"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf leaving Dun Morogh, you pass from icy mountain air into Loch Modan's open valleys and quarries.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, South Gate Pass links Ironforge with the eastern Alliance territories. The King's Mountaineers maintain and secure the route."},kw={"dun morogh","loch modan","mountaineers","south gate outpost","south gate pass","thelsamar","tunnel"},rel={"subzone:south-gate-outpost","subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"South Gate Pass"}}
E["subzone:stonesplinter-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonesplinter Valley",z="lochmodan",s="In southwestern Loch Modan, Stonesplinter troggs hold a mountain vale behind crude defenses. Their chieftain, Grawmug, leads the tribe from within.",h="In southwestern Loch Modan, Stonesplinter troggs hold a mountain vale behind crude defenses.",sec={{t="A Chittering Stronghold",b="Among the crags of southwestern Loch Modan, Stonesplinter troggs have made their stronghold. Troggs clawed up from underground across Khaz Modan and ended the quiet that once filled this hollow. The Stonesplinter tribe claimed the valley and carved crude defenses into its rocky passes.\n\nThey dug dens and raised barricades, and now hunt anything that comes too close. Their numbers threaten the roads through southern Loch Modan. So Mountaineers from Thelsamar hire mercenaries to thin the tribe and bring down Grawmug, its towering warlord.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Stonesplinter Valley located?",a="Stonesplinter Valley lies in the mountains of southwestern Loch Modan, just south of the main road past Grizzlepaw Ridge.",al={"stonesplinter valley location","where is stonesplinter valley","trogg valley loch modan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who rules Stonesplinter Valley?",a="Grawmug rules the encampment as its brutish trogg chieftain. From the deepest part of the valley, he directs raids on local travelers and patrols.",al={"who leads the stonesplinter troggs","grawmug","trogg boss loch modan"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are the troggs here in Loch Modan?",a="Dwarven excavations elsewhere in Khaz Modan unearthed troggs from deep underground. Driven by senseless aggression, separate warbands came to the surface. The Stonesplinter tribe chose this secluded vale as its main staging ground.",al={"why are there troggs in loch modan","where did the troggs come from","trogg origin loch modan"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the dwarves care about clearing the valley?",a="Stonesplinter Valley lies dangerously close to dwarf settlements, mines, and mountain roads. If the entrenched troggs go unchecked, travelers in southern Loch Modan face danger, and Mountaineer patrols face added strain.",al={"why fight stonesplinter troggs","thelsamar trogg problem"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Stonesplinter Valley?",a="Stonesplinter Valley is a rugged mountain vale carved into southwestern Loch Modan. Once a pristine alpine landscape, it has been thoroughly overrun by a massive clan of hostile troggs who have claimed the hollows and mountain passes as their own stronghold.",al={"stonesplinter valley overview","what is stonesplinter valley","about stonesplinter valley"},it="place",add="c84babb8"},{q="What happened to Stonesplinter Valley?",a="What was once an untouched and peaceful corner of the loch's mountain basin turned into a warrens for the troggs. After unearthing themselves across Khaz Modan, the Stonesplinter clan flooded into the valley in force, defiling the wilderness and driving out anyone who dared approach.",al={"stonesplinter valley history","what happened to the valley","trogg infestation stonesplinter valley"},it="history",add="30aeaf73"},{q="Is Stonesplinter Valley dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Hostile Stonesplinter troggs swarm the terrain in dense numbers, fiercely guarding their territory against outsiders. Deep within the heart of the valley lurks their formidable chieftain, Grawmug, making any foray deep into the vale a deadly endeavor.",al={"how dangerous is stonesplinter valley","stonesplinter valley threat","is stonesplinter valley safe"},it="danger",add="39c06fe2"},{q="Why is it called Stonesplinter Valley?",a="The valley takes its name directly from the Stonesplinter trogg tribe that infests and controls it. Their entrenched presence has completely redefined the area in the eyes of the surrounding dwarven defenders.",al={"stonesplinter valley name origin","why called stonesplinter valley","origin of stonesplinter name"},it="name",add="27e6d962"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can help the Mountaineers of Thelsamar push back the troggs and drive Grawmug's brutes from Loch Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help secure Loch Modan's supply routes. They are vulnerable while Ironforge forces are stretched thin across the realm."},kw={"grawmug","loch modan","stonesplinter","stonesplinter valley","thelsamar","troggs"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","topic:trogg"},src={"Stonesplinter Valley"}}
E["subzone:stonewrought-dam"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonewrought Dam",z="lochmodan",s="Along Loch Modan’s northern rim, waters gather behind Stonewrought Dam. The dwarven barrier holds back the Loch and drains the Wetlands below into habitable marshes.",h="Along Loch Modan’s northern rim, waters gather behind Stonewrought Dam.",sec={{t="A Wonder of Dwarven Craft",b="East of Dun Algaz, Stonewrought Dam spans a canyon in one of the great works of dwarven craft. Dark Iron architect Franclorn Forgewright designed it and pioneered the stonewrought technique used to raise it. By holding water in the mountain basin, the dam doubled the Loch’s surface area and steadily lowered the waters to the north. The Wetlands formed from a valley once wholly flooded.",sp=0},{t="Sabotage and Defense",b="Stonewrought Dam now serves Ironforge, but Dark Iron saboteurs from the southern mountains target it. After recent assaults and attempts to slip inside, Ironforge placed a garrison here under Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII. Guards and engineers patrol the masonry day and night. Should the dam be breached, the Loch could drain and send a devastating flood across the Wetlands below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built the Stonewrought Dam?",a="Dark Iron architect Franclorn Forgewright designed and oversaw Stonewrought Dam. He pioneered the stonewrought technique used to build it. Though a Dark Iron master built it, the dam serves the Bronzebeard kingdom today.",al={"who made stonewrought dam","creator of the dam","dam architect"},it="origin"},{q="What happens if the dam breaks?",a="If Stonewrought Dam collapsed, the Loch would rapidly drain and leave Loch Modan an empty crater of mud. Its waters would then sweep into the Wetlands in a devastating, uncontrollable flood.",al={"if dam breaks","what if the dam breaks","dam destroyed"},it="threat"},{q="Why are Dark Iron dwarves attacking it?",a="The Dark Iron clan attacks Ironforge’s vital works to destabilize the region. Crippling the dam would cripple supply lines, drown the northern Wetlands and strike a bitter blow against Bronzebeard pride.",al={"why attack dam","dark iron dam attack"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is currently in charge of the dam's defense?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII manages the dam’s daily operations and defenses. He coordinates with Ironforge forces to root out saboteurs.",al={"who runs the dam","dam engineer"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Stonewrought Dam?",a="Stonewrought Dam is a colossal dwarven marvel positioned along the northern edge of Loch Modan, just east of the Dun Algaz pass. It holds back the massive lake, dramatically expanding its size while regulating the waterways that spill down into the Wetlands below. Renowned as one of the world's greatest architectural wonders, it stands as an enduring monument to ancient dwarven engineering.",al={"what is stonewrought dam","about stonewrought dam","stonewrought dam lore"},it="place",add="721eb9b8"},{q="What is the history of Stonewrought Dam?",a="The dam was conceived and overseen by Franclorn Forgewright, a brilliant Dark Iron architect who pioneered revolutionary construction techniques before his clan's fall to shadow. His grand design doubled the volume of Loch Modan and helped drain the marshy basin of the Wetlands. Though built long ago during a period of unity, it has recently become the front line in a bitter conflict as Dark Iron saboteurs seek to destroy it.",al={"stonewrought dam history","history of the dam","what happened at stonewrought dam"},it="history",add="b3d97da7"},{q="Is Stonewrought Dam dangerous?",a="The structure itself is solid and sturdy, but the area crawls with peril. Dark Iron dwarf infiltrators and saboteurs skulk around its flanks and tunnels, armed with explosives and dark magic in hopes of breaching the walls. Alliance forces and Ironforge guards are spread thin trying to ward off constant sabotage attempts, making travel around the rim hazardous for unprepared wanderers.",al={"stonewrought dam dangerous","is the dam safe","threats at stonewrought dam"},it="danger",add="a124034a"},{q="Why is it called Stonewrought Dam?",a="The dam takes its name from the \"stonewrought\" building method, an advanced technique of dwarf masonry and architecture invented by its chief builder, Franclorn Forgewright. The precision and resilience of this style allowed the massive wall to withstand immense water pressure for generations.",al={"why is it called stonewrought dam","stonewrought dam name meaning","stonewrought name origin"},it="name",add="e9d9cbd5"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see the dam as a monument to dwarven masonry and ingenuity. Its Dark Iron heritage remains a sore point contested among Ironforge’s historians.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can study the dam’s hydraulic controls and stonewrought load-bearing mechanics. Its design rivals the great works beneath Ironforge."},kw={"dark iron","franclorn forgewright","hinderweir","loch modan","stonewrought dam","the loch","wetlands"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:wetlands","npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","topic:dark-iron-clan","subzone:dun-algaz","zone:ironforge","topic:dwarf"},src={"Stonewrought Dam"}}
E["subzone:stoutlager-inn"] = {t="subzone",n="Stoutlager Inn",z="lochmodan",s="In Thelsamar, Stoutlager Inn welcomes travelers crossing western Loch Modan with a warm hearth and a place to gather.",h="In Thelsamar, Stoutlager Inn welcomes travelers crossing western Loch Modan with a warm hearth and a place to...",sec={{t="A Welcoming Hearth in the Hills",b="Stoutlager Inn draws miners, mountaineers, and travelers passing between Dun Morogh and the Wetlands. They trade rumors, find beds, and share dwarven ale beneath its roof. Beyond Thelsamar, troggs and kobolds make the wilderness dangerous, so the inn’s stone walls and fires offer welcome shelter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What services are available at the Stoutlager Inn?",a="Travelers crossing Loch Modan can find beds, provisions, and drinks at Stoutlager Inn. The innkeeper can bind hearthstones, and local merchants sell supplies.",al={"inn services","what is in the inn","thelsamar innkeeper"},gp=true},{q="Where is the Stoutlager Inn located?",a="Stoutlager Inn stands beside the main road in the center of Thelsamar, the main Alliance town in western Loch Modan.",al={"inn location","where is stoutlager","find stoutlager inn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the inn so important to Thelsamar?",a="Stoutlager Inn gives Thelsamar a place for food, lodging, and news. Local mountaineers post bounties there, and travelers plan excursions into the surrounding hills.",al={"why is it popular","thelsamar tavern lore"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Stoutlager Inn?",a="The Stoutlager Inn is the beating heart of Thelsamar and one of the most bustling gathering halls in all of Loch Modan. It serves as a warm, welcoming refuge for weary travelers stepping off the mountain roads, offering strong dwarven ale, hot food, and soft hearth beds. Local mountaineers, miners, and visiting adventurers regularly gather beneath its heavy timber rafters to share rumors, plan excursions into the surrounding hills, and enjoy good company away from the wilderness.",al={"what is stoutlager inn","stoutlager inn lore","thelsamar inn"},it="place",add="621b2370"},{q="Is Stoutlager Inn dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest. The Stoutlager Inn is a secure sanctuary nestled right in the center of Thelsamar, firmly protected by local dwarven guards and passing mountaineers. While troggs, kobolds, and hostile wildlife roam the shores and ridges of Loch Modan, the inn itself remains a peaceful haven where you can rest, catch your breath, and bind your spirit to the hearth without fear of attack.",al={"is stoutlager inn safe","stoutlager inn danger","threats in thelsamar inn"},it="danger",add="7e615305"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a Bronzebeard dwarf, you may find the warmth of home at Stoutlager Inn. Its hospitality, fresh ale, and reliable company are welcome far from Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can find shelter and prepare at Stoutlager Inn before heading north toward the Wetlands or patrolling the troubled valleys around the loch."},kw={"dwarf","hearthstone","innkeeper","loch modan","stoutlager inn","tavern","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan"},src={"Stoutlager Inn"}}
E["subzone:the-loch"] = {t="subzone",n="The Loch",z="lochmodan",s="The Loch's waters fill the heart of Loch Modan, held back by the Stonewrought Dam. The lake is Khaz Modan's largest body of water and sustains the dwarven settlements around it.",h="The Loch's waters fill the heart of Loch Modan, held back by the Stonewrought Dam.",sec={{t="Heart of the Valley",b="At the center of Loch Modan, The Loch spreads among the largest inland lakes in the known world. Only Lordamere Lake and Darrowmere Lake to the north rival its size. Local fishermen draw from its waters, while Thelsamar and nearby hunting lodges enjoy a peaceful setting along its shores. Beneath the calm surface, aggressive threshadons and freshwater beasts make swimming across perilous.",sp=0},{t="The Stonewrought Barrier",b="To the north, the Stonewrought Dam keeps The Loch in its tranquil state. The massive dwarven structure crosses a cleft in the mountains and prevents the lake from flooding into the Wetlands below. Its upkeep preserves the valley's ecosystem and helps keep Khaz Modan secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Loch?",a="The Loch fills the center of the Loch Modan valley in Khaz Modan. This vast mountain lake is one of the world's largest freshwater bodies and shapes local dwarven life and the valley's geography.",al={"the loch lore","what is the loch lake","loch modan lake"},it="place"},{q="How does the lake stay full?",a="The Stonewrought Dam contains The Loch to the north. The towering dwarven structure holds back the water that would otherwise spill through the mountain pass into the low-lying Wetlands.",al={"why doesn't the loch drain","what holds the loch back","stonewrought dam purpose"}},{q="Is it safe to swim in The Loch?",a="Swimming in The Loch can be dangerous. Predatory threshadons and snapping beasts in deeper waters often attack travelers who venture far from shore.",al={"loch monsters","swimming the loch","creatures in the loch"},it="danger"},{q="How large is The Loch compared to other lakes?",a="The Loch is Khaz Modan's largest body of water and the third largest known lake in the Eastern Kingdoms. Only Lordamere Lake and Darrowmere Lake in Lordaeron are larger.",al={"biggest lake","the loch size comparison","how big is the loch"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can take pride in The Loch, a centerpiece of Ironforge pride. Its waters and the Stonewrought Dam show how dwarven masonry can tame nature and sustain settlements such as Thelsamar.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can follow The Loch's tranquil waters. They provide vital freshwater and trade routes between Ironforge's central valley and the surrounding outposts."},kw={"khaz modan","lake","loch modan","stonewrought dam","the loch","thelsamar","threshadon","wetlands"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:wetlands","subzone:darrowmere-lake"},src={"The Loch"}}
E["subzone:thelsamar"] = {t="subzone",n="Thelsamar",z="lochmodan",s="In Thelsamar, travelers find shelter on the road between Dun Morogh and the Wetlands. The town keeps watch over the western bluffs above Loch Modan's great lake as troggs and ogres press nearby.",h="In Thelsamar, travelers find shelter on the road between Dun Morogh and the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Heart of Loch Modan",b="Thelsamar gathers dwarven life beneath stout roofs of stone and timber. At the Stoutlager Inn, travelers can rest, and nearby they find a gryphon roost, crafting stations, and supply merchants. The town lies along the road from the South Gate Pass into Dun Morogh to the Algaz Pass toward the Wetlands. Travelers crossing the region pass through its doors.",sp=0},{t="Trouble on the Frontier",b="Trouble presses in on Thelsamar from several sides. Troggs pour from Stonesplinter Valley to the south, while bears and other predators haunt Grizzlepaw Ridge. Ironforge's regular forces are stretched thin across the realm. So the local magistrate and Mountaineers rely on travelers and mercenaries to patrol the trade roads and drive back hostile forces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What services are available in Thelsamar?",a="Thelsamar offers lodging and refreshment at the Stoutlager Inn, a flightmaster with connections across central Khaz Modan, trade vendors, and an outdoor forge. Several trainers teach professions and combat skills to growing adventurers.",al={"thelsamar vendors","what is in thelsamar","trainers in thelsamar"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where does the road through Thelsamar lead?",a="The road west of Thelsamar runs south through a tunnel into Dun Morogh and onward toward Ironforge. Northward, it passes through the Algaz Gate and descends into the marshy Wetlands.",al={"thelsamar road","where does the path go","travel from thelsamar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the town hiring so many mercenaries?",a="The local Mountaineers face several threats at once. Stonesplinter troggs have overrun the southern excavations, wild beasts prowl the settlement's edges, and organized ogres press in. Town leaders offer bounties to independent fighters.",al={"why are there quests in thelsamar","who is attacking thelsamar"},it="motive"},{q="What is the famous local specialty here?",a="Hunters and travelers prize Thelsamar Blood Sausages, a rich dwarven dish prepared by Vidra Hearthstove at the Stoutlager Inn from local wildlife entrails and flesh.",al={"thelsamar food","blood sausages loch modan"},it="fame"},{q="What is Thelsamar?",a="Thelsamar is the primary dwarven settlement in Loch Modan, nestled on the western bluffs overlooking the loch. Positioned right along the major north-south road connecting Dun Morogh to the Wetlands, the town serves as an essential hub for mountain travelers, merchants, and Mountaineer patrols defending the valley.",al={"thelsamar town","what is this town","tell me about thelsamar"},it="place",add="19f21b39"},{q="Who lives in or runs Thelsamar?",a="Thelsamar is populated by Bronzebeard dwarves and falls under the civil authority of Magistrate Bluntnose, who manages local matters and enlists outside aid to deal with surrounding threats. The town is actively protected by dwarven Mountaineers and guards reporting up through Ironforge's military command.",al={"who leads thelsamar","who is in charge of thelsamar","thelsamar leader"},it="residents",add="a244cff7"},{q="Is Thelsamar dangerous?",a="The town itself is secure and well-guarded by Mountaineers, but the surrounding wilderness poses serious hazards. Trogg incursions from Stonesplinter Valley threaten nearby farms, bears prowl to the south, and ogres press in from Mo'grosh Stronghold, forcing the town to rely on traveling adventurers to keep the perimeter safe.",al={"is thelsamar safe","threats to thelsamar","thelsamar danger"},it="danger",add="c5fc67c9"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf leaving cold Dun Morogh, you find warmer lowlands in Thelsamar, with great ale, stout stone hearths, and active service with the Mountaineer guard.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook traveling through Thelsamar, you can stop at the Stoutlager Inn to learn the regional recipe for hearty blood sausages made from local bears, spiders, and boars."},kw={"blood sausages","grizzlepaw","loch modan","mountaineers","stonesplinter","stoutlager inn","thelsamar"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:stoutlager-inn","subzone:the-loch","quest:418","quest:255","quest:256","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","subzone:grizzlepaw-ridge"},src={"Thelsamar"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-kings"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Kings",z="lochmodan",s="At Valley of Kings, stone rulers guard the southern road into the Searing Gorge. In southwestern Loch Modan, the canyon lies south of the passage to Dun Morogh. Blackrock forces and troggs threaten travelers beneath the dwarven monuments.",h="At Valley of Kings, stone rulers guard the southern road into the Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="Guardians of the Southern Pass",b="Two immense statues watch over the southern pass: King Madoran Bronzebeard and High Thane Khardros Wildhammer. After the kings died, their sons commissioned the carvings together. The statues honor the allied victory in the War of the Three Hammers, and they face the Dark Iron clan. Beyond them, the southern lands still bear the ruin left by Ragnaros's summoning.",sp=0},{t="The Gate to the Searing Gorge",b="The valley links South Gate Pass with Stonesplinter Valley, and an iron gate opens into the Searing Gorge. Hostile Blackrock orcs, Dark Iron dwarves, and volcanic dangers make the passage perilous. So Ironforge mountaineers keep the gate locked and guarded, with Mountaineer Pebblebitty watching the threshold. Only the hardiest travelers may pass, after showing they have the strength to survive beyond it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who do the two giant statues represent?",a="The statues depict King Madoran Bronzebeard of Ironforge and High Thane Khardros Wildhammer. Their sons commissioned them together after their fathers died, to honor the alliance that won the War of the Three Hammers.",al={"statues in valley of kings","dwarf statues loch modan","who are the statues"},it="people"},{q="Why were the statues built facing south?",a="The statues face the southern lands ruined by the Dark Iron clan's summoning of Ragnaros. The twin kings watch over the approach to the northern dwarven lands and warn hostile forces away.",al={"why statues look south","purpose of statues","statues facing searing gorge"},it="purpose"},{q="How do I get through the locked gate at the southern end?",a="The gate into the Searing Gorge stays locked for travelers' safety. Speak with Mountaineer Pebblebitty, who guards it, and prove your abilities by completing a task for her. Then she will give you the key.",al={"how to open searing gorge gate","mountaineer pebblebitty key","valley of kings gate locked"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where does this valley lead?",a="The valley links South Gate Pass toward Dun Morogh, trogg-infested Stonesplinter Valley to the east, and the Searing Gorge through its guarded southern gate.",al={"valley of kings connections","where does valley go"},it="place"},{q="What is the Valley of Kings?",a="The Valley of Kings is a lush mountain pass tucked into the southwestern corner of Loch Modan, just west of Stonesplinter Valley. It serves as a vital crossway connecting travelers journeying between Dun Morogh through the South Gate Pass and the perilous, volcanic lands of the Searing Gorge to the south.",al={"valley of kings loch modan","what is valley of kings","valley of kings info"},it="place",add="7c2b9610"},{q="What happened at the Valley of Kings?",a="Following the devastating War of the Three Hammers and the tragic deaths of High King Madoran Bronzebeard and Khardros Wildhammer, their sons jointly commissioned the valley's two colossal monuments. Carved into the cliffs overlooking the southern pass, the statues stand as an eternal monument to their united victory over Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan and the scorched wasteland he left behind.",al={"history of valley of kings","why are there statues here","valley of kings lore"},it="history",add="0960ad5d"},{q="Who controls the Valley of Kings?",a="The valley lies under the sovereign authority of Ironforge and is patrolled by dwarven Mountaineers. At the southern gate leading down into Searing Gorge, Mountaineer Pebblebitty keeps watch, ensuring that only seasoned adventurers who have proven their mettle may unlock the heavy gates and venture toward the scorched wastes.",al={"who controls valley of kings","who runs valley of kings","ironforge guards valley of kings"},it="residents",add="f059810f"},{q="Is the Valley of Kings dangerous?",a="While the valley itself is relatively secure and patrolled by Ironforge mountaineers, it borders extreme hazards. Just to the east lies the trogg-infested Stonesplinter Valley, and directly to the south, sealed behind locked gates, awaits the scorching, hostile terrain of the Searing Gorge and Blackrock Mountain.",al={"valley of kings danger","is it safe here","threats in valley of kings"},it="danger",add="960bcb2e"},{q="Why is it called the Valley of Kings?",a="The valley draws its name from the two colossal statues carved into the mountainsides, which depict High King Madoran Bronzebeard of Ironforge and King Khardros Wildhammer of Grim Batol. Their sons had these towering effigies raised together to honor their fathers' leadership in the War of the Three Hammers.",al={"why is it called valley of kings","valley of kings name origin","who named valley of kings"},it="name",add="04615939"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you walk hallowed ground honoring the bond between Bronzebeard and Wildhammer, forged against the Dark Irons' treachery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an ally, you pass through the northern bulwark against threats from the southern badlands. The dangers of the Searing Gorge threaten Khaz Modan."},kw={"khardros wildhammer","loch modan","madoran bronzebeard","pebblebitty","searing gorge gate","valley of kings","war of the three hammers"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","zone:searinggorge","subzone:south-gate-pass","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"Valley of Kings"}}
E["zone:lochmodan"] = {t="zone",n="Loch Modan",z="lochmodan",s="Loch Modan's great lake stands above the Wetlands, held back by the Stonewrought Dam. Around Thelsamar, troggs threaten the southern valleys, kobolds work the mines, and ogres hold the northeast highlands.",h="Loch Modan's great lake stands above the Wetlands, held back by the Stonewrought Dam.",sec={{t="A Highland Jewel",b="Loch Modan's lake fills a green valley east of Dun Morogh. Pines and birches climb toward rugged peaks, and the Stonewrought Dam spans the northern rim. The dwarven town of Thelsamar draws mountaineers, hunters, and miners. Copper and tin run through the surrounding hills.",sp=0},{t="Unearthed Terrors and Invasions",b="Broken catapults and ballistae on the lake bed recall the Second War. The orcish Horde occupied Loch Modan then, until the dwarves drove them out. More recently, dwarven excavations opened underground chambers and released savage troggs. Their tribes, led by chieftains, overran the southern canyons of Stonesplinter Valley and the Valley of Kings. The Ironforge Mountaineers fight to defend the trade routes.",sp=0},{t="Plots in the Shadows",b="Troggs and the ogres of Mo'grosh Stronghold threaten the valley. Investigations into local sabotage point to the treacherous Dark Iron dwarves, who came through the burning passes to the south. Dark Iron infiltrators target dwarven blastpowder reserves and harbor designs against the Stonewrought Dam.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What holds the lake back from flooding the Wetlands?",a="The Stonewrought Dam holds back the entire Loch. Dwarven engineers maintain it carefully, since a breach would wash out the Wetlands' lower marshlands to the north.",al={"what is the dam","stonewrought dam purpose","why does loch modan have a dam"},it="place"},{q="Where did all the troggs come from?",a="Dwarven explorers and miners broke into underground chambers deep in the mountains. Savage troggs poured out, swarmed to the surface, and established camps in the valleys.",al={"why are there troggs here","trogg invasion loch modan","trogg origin"},it="origin"},{q="What is the primary Alliance settlement in the zone?",a="Thelsamar, on the western bluffs, is the main Alliance town and travel hub. Its Stoutlager Inn, tradesfolk, and gryphon masters connect travelers to Ironforge and beyond.",al={"loch modan town","hub in loch modan","thelsamar"},it="place"},{q="Who rules Mo'grosh Stronghold?",a="Brute ogres hold Mo'grosh Stronghold in the northeast mountains. They descended into the valley and built a fortified outpost that terrorizes nearby hunters and travelers.",al={"ogre camp loch modan","ogres northeast loch modan","mogrosh"},it="leader"},{q="What happened to Ironband's Excavation Site?",a="Troggs pouring from underground chambers overran Prospector Ironband's archaeological dig. The team abandoned its work and fought to secure its remaining supplies.",al={"ironbands dig","why was ironbands site abandoned","prospector ironband problem"},it="threat"},{q="Can you travel from Loch Modan to the Badlands or Searing Gorge?",a="Yes. Footpaths lead south through the mountains to the arid Badlands. The Stonewrought Pass through the Valley of Kings leads southwest to the volcanic crags of Searing Gorge.",al={"loch modan to badlands","loch modan south exit","path to badlands"},gp=true},{q="What is Loch Modan?",a="Loch Modan is a temperate valley in eastern Khaz Modan, lying east of Dun Morogh and south of the Wetlands. Enclosed by rugged mountains and light pine forests, its defining feature is the massive freshwater loch held back by the magnificent Stonewrought Dam. It serves as an integral territory of the Ironforge dwarven kingdom.",al={"loch modan zone","about loch modan","what is this place"},it="place",add="2ab9b343",nx={10,11}},{q="What happened at Loch Modan?",a="During the Second War, the Horde swept into Loch Modan and fortified positions across the valley against the Alliance. Ironforge's defenders fought a brutal campaign to liberate their land. While the dwarves reclaimed the region, broken catapults and ballistae resting on the lake bed and islands remain as remnants of that war.",al={"loch modan history","past battles loch modan","second war loch modan"},it="history",add="4c6debd3"},{q="Is Loch Modan dangerous?",a="Behind its tranquil alpine appearance, Loch Modan faces numerous crises. Vicious troggs unburied by recent digs overrun the hills and mines, Mo'grosh ogres occupy the northeast, kobolds plague the roads, and infiltrators from the Dark Iron clan actively sabotage dwarven positions around the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"dangers in loch modan","is loch modan safe","threats in loch modan"},it="danger",add="11acca40"},{q="Who lives here?",a="The valley is home to Ironforge dwarves and gnomes, centered around the settlement of Thelsamar, as well as hunters and trackers at Farstrider Lodge. However, aggressive troggs, kobolds, Dark Iron saboteurs, and the Mo'grosh ogres heavily contest dwarven control across the wilderness.",al={"who lives in loch modan","inhabitants of loch modan","who resides here"},it="residents",add="85c52931"},{q="Is this part of the dwarf kingdom?",a="Yes. Loch Modan is an essential eastern province of the Kingdom of Ironforge, governed under King Magni Bronzebeard's authority and defended by the Ironforge Mountaineers.",al={"is loch modan ironforge","does ironforge rule loch modan","dwarven kingdom loch modan"},it="ties",add="0925f1bd"},{q="Was the lake always this big?",a="No. The loch was once much smaller. When the master architect Franclorn Forgewright designed and erected the Stonewrought Dam, the massive structure impounded the runoff from the Khaz Modan mountains, more than doubling the original size of the water body.",al={"how big was loch modan","original loch size","did the dam make the lake bigger"},it="place",add="90a2b33d"},{q="Who's in charge around here?",a="The region answers directly to King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge. Locally, civilian administration in Thelsamar is overseen by Magistrate Bluntnose, military garrisons follow officers like Captain Rugelfuss, and defense of the vital Stonewrought Dam falls under Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII.",al={"who leads loch modan","loch modan leadership","who rules this land"},it="in_charge",add="ef90b12a"},{q="What is Thelsamar?",a="Thelsamar is the primary dwarven settlement in Loch Modan, located along the western bluffs. It hosts Stoutlager Inn, craftsmen, gryphon handlers, and the local administration, serving as a staging post between Ironforge, the Wetlands, and the eastern frontiers.",al={"thelsamar village","town of thelsamar","about thelsamar"},it="place",add="0cf9ab54"},{q="What are troggs and where did they come from?",a="Troggs are savage, subterranean humanoids inadvertently unleashed by dwarven archaeological and mining excavations beneath the Khaz Modan peaks. Once awakened, they swarmed upward into the valleys, building primitive encampments and assaulting travelers.",al={"where did troggs come from","what is a trogg","trogg origins"},it="threat",add="9c1680d8"},{q="What are the Dark Iron dwarves doing at the dam?",a="Dark Iron saboteurs have encroached upon the Stonewrought Dam with explosives, seeking to undermine Ironforge's crown jewel. Their plots threaten to shatter the dam and devastate the region, forcing Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII to enlist help to root them out.",al={"dark irons at dam","why are dark irons at stonewrought dam","dark iron threat loch modan"},it="threat",add="15b5e85c"},{q="What is Ironband's excavation digging for?",a="Prospector Ironband's team was sent to unearth ancient titan artifacts and uncover forgotten dwarven heritage. Unfortunately, their digging broke into trogg-infested caverns, sparking an overrun that drove the miners out and led Ironband to look toward the ancient ruins of Uldaman.",al={"ironband dig site goal","what are they digging for at ironband","ironband excavation"},it="purpose",add="0550e806"},{q="What is Dun Algaz and why is it dangerous?",a="Dun Algaz is the fortified mountain pass linking Loch Modan to the Wetlands to the north. It is dangerous because hostile forces, including Dragonmaw orcs and local brigands, constantly besiege and contest the pass, making passage perilous without dwarven patrols.",al={"dun algaz pass","why is dun algaz dangerous","pass to wetlands"},it="place",add="c3dabc80",nx={19}},{q="What's on the other side of Dun Algaz?",a="Through the winding tunnels of Dun Algaz lies the Wetlands, a vast and misty swamp reaching toward Menethil Harbor and the northern lands.",al={"where does dun algaz lead","what is north of dun algaz","beyond dun algaz"},it="place",add="2a064472"},{q="How did I end up in Loch Modan?",a="If you are a dwarf or gnome, your path likely led east out of the snowy crags of Dun Morogh, passing through the guarded tunnels of North Gate or South Gate Pass. Travelers from further afield, including humans and night elves arriving from Stormwind via the Deeprun Tram to Ironforge, travel that same mountain road down into this temperate valley, or fly directly to the settlement of Thelsamar.",al={"how did i get here","how did i reach loch modan","getting to loch modan"},it="arrival",add="52ebefe5"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Loch Modan?",a="The defenders of Loch Modan are stretched thin and urgently need your help. Hostile troggs unearthed by dwarven mining operations threaten the settlements, while savage Mo'grosh ogres dominate the northeast. In Thelsamar and the Valley of Kings, Captain Rugelfuss and local mountaineers look to recruits to push back the trogg incursions, aid Prospector Ironband's beleaguered archaeological dig, and protect the vital Stonewrought Dam from looming sabotage.",al={"why am i here","what should i do in loch modan","what is my mission here"},it="purpose",add="13e88a97"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see Loch Modan's unmatched stonework and the dangerous ancient history your people keep uncovering beneath the stone.",["class:Hunter"]="At the Farstrider Lodge on the southeastern ridges, trackers gather to hunt bears, crocolisks, and mountain buzzards.",["profession:Mining"]="Loch Modan's hills, quarries, and trogg-infested caves hold accessible veins of copper, tin, and silver.",["faction:Alliance"]="Loch Modan guards the route between Dun Morogh and the northern roads to the Wetlands, helping defend Ironforge's territory."},kw={"farstrider lodge","ironband","mo'grosh stronghold","stonesplinter","stonewrought dam","the loch","thelsamar","troggs","valley of kings"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:dunmorogh","zone:wetlands","subzone:mo-grosh-stronghold","subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site","quest:161","quest:217"},m={levels="10-20"},src={"Loch Modan (Classic)","Loch Modan"}}
